window.AKK_XIANXIA_INN_MANAGEMENT_RPG_CHAPTERS=(window.AKK_XIANXIA_INN_MANAGEMENT_RPG_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"number":1,"title":"Chapter 1","paragraphs":["The heavens are divided into nine wilds, and the earth into nine provinces.","Ever since the Barrier Between Heaven and Earth was severed and Nuwa led the gods in their ascension to the Ninth Heaven, the nine provinces of the mortal realm had been governed and inhabited by earth immortals and mortal cultivators.","In the central region of the nine provinces, the people revered the Divine Firmament Sect above all others. Thus, this province was known as Divine Firmament Province. In Yuntai Prefecture, in the northern part of Divine Firmament Province, there stood a small city built against the mountains. It was called Plum Mountain City.","On a remote street in that little city stood an equally little inn.","Heroes and immortal guests came and went, yet none had ever noticed this unremarkable establishment. Peddlers and hawkers carrying shoulder poles passed by and paused here and there, but never once stopped at this place.","At dawn, a black-clad burly man eight feet tall stood at the entrance of the inn. His sharp, hawk-like eyes were fixed on the signboard hanging above the door.","Carved into the sign in tiny engraved characters was the name of the inn—","Ah ah ah oh oh oh uh uh uh let me see which game has the longest name, padding padding padding As If the Emperor Were Here—Inn.","“............?”","A question mark slowly appeared above the burly man’s head.","***","The reason the inn had such a bizarre name was that the player, Wu Guanyue, had typed it in on a whim because she thought it would be funny...","That’s right—the player.","This was a full-dive game called Immortal Innkeeping Log. The game claimed to use the most advanced brain-computer technology available, providing an extraordinarily immersive physical experience that would make players feel as though they were truly living inside the game. It was currently in closed beta.","Although Wu Guanyue had no idea why a management simulation game needed to be full-dive... she had nothing better to do, so she applied for a beta slot anyway.","Perhaps there simply weren’t many applicants, because she received her full-dive helmet very quickly.","Wu Guanyue was twenty-two years old. She neither attended school nor held a job, because she was paralyzed.","At the age of five, she had been diagnosed with a rare illness. She had been bedridden and unable to move ever since. Fortunately, her family was fairly well-off and could provide for all her needs.","In her spare time, Wu Guanyue liked playing games. After all, even a paralyzed person needed to find some fun in life, right? She had joined the beta for this obscure game mainly because she had recently run out of new games to play.","She hadn’t taken the game’s extravagant claims of “total immersion” and “an extraordinarily realistic experience” seriously at all.","But the moment she logged in and arrived at the character-customization screen, she was stunned by the game’s physical immersion.","This—this was way too real!","It wasn’t merely the responsive sensation of a virtual game. It felt as though she had truly regained the connection between her brain and her limbs!","It was like heaven dropping a pie straight into her lap! For Wu Guanyue, being able to move freely—even if only inside a game—was already an incredible stroke of luck.","There was only one drawback: the game used Honor Mode. All progress was saved in real time and could not be rolled back. Once a character died for good, the game immediately ended.","When Wu Guanyue first saw this notice, she was so shocked that she nearly grabbed the developers by the shoulders and demanded: Why make a management simulation game this punishing?!","The official announcement also stated that, because the game used the most advanced AI technology and every NPC’s reaction was calculated in real time, the beta’s computing power was limited. As a result, each player had one—and only one—chance to play.","One single chance... They didn’t even give players the option to start over?","Sigh... Whatever.","After spending so many years paralyzed in bed, Wu Guanyue had relied on games to pass the time. She could consider herself something of a high-level player. Even if the difficulty was extremely high, she didn’t think she would fail at a management simulation game. She still had that much confidence.","She imported a photograph of herself, generated a character model resembling her real-life appearance, and casually named the inn. Then she officially began the game.","The world before her slowly darkened, then gradually brightened again.","As soon as she opened her eyes, Wu Guanyue saw a blue-dyed cotton bed curtain. Little white flowers bloomed across the thick, coarse fabric like clusters of faded stars.","From the corner of her eye, she took in the small but adequately sized room. There was a table and two benches. The wooden window stood open, revealing the faint light of dawn and distant blue-green mountains. Shades of verdant greenery lay over the tiled roofs of the homes below like dark clouds, spilling even into this little room and filling it with a fresh, rustic, ancient charm.","At the same time, a line of translucent text appeared before her eyes.","[Yesterday, you arrived in the unfamiliar Plum Mountain City and took over the inheritance your grandfather left you.]","Oh, inheriting an estate. A classic backstory.","[Plum Mountain City is surrounded by spiritual energy. Several secret realms left behind by ascended masters can be found in the nearby mountains, so heroes and immortal guests from all across the Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands pass through the city year-round.]","Mm-hmm. In other words, an inn in a prime location near a top-tier tourist attraction.","[You are filled with anticipation for the new life that is about to begin, but you also feel unfamiliar with it. Wang Er, the shop assistant your grandfather left behind, will help you.]","All right, so he’s the tutorial NPC who teaches the player the basics.","[He should have come to find you at this time, but he has not appeared. Could something have happened?]","Hmm? Is there a plot?","[Main Quest: Speak with Shop Assistant Wang Er (New!)]","[Quest Details: The shop assistant failed to show up at the appointed time. Get out of bed and look for him. While you’re at it, take a look around your inn!]","Following the quest instructions, Wu Guanyue opened the door and walked around the inn.","The inn had two floors. The upper floor contained the guest rooms, while the lower floor was a main hall where diners could drink and eat. Wu Guanyue’s starting room was at the end of the second-floor corridor. Looking down from inside, she could even see the backyard, where there was a well filled with sweet water. The kitchen was in the same area.","The place was small, but it had all the necessary parts. However, the entire guest-room area on the second floor was utterly bare. Not only was there no decoration, but even the most basic furniture—tables, chairs, beds, and the like—was missing. It made one wonder what on earth Grandpa had been doing all these years...","Perhaps the game’s developers knew this was a glaring flaw, because another line of text appeared before Wu Guanyue’s eyes.","[Bleak, run-down, and on the verge of collapse... This is the inn your grandfather left you. Could it be that doing business with a conscience truly offers no future? You cannot help but fall into deep thought.]","[Choose a business path: Legitimate Inn / Black Inn]","[Legitimate Inn: You are a diligent proprietor who relies on exploring the map, updating your recipes, and expanding your guest rooms to earn money. Your inn is a safe harbor where travelers can rest without worry... (Initial Specialty: Culinary Mastery)]","[Black Inn: You are a cold-hearted and ruthless proprietor. Making money fast is your guiding principle. Your inn is dangerous and mysterious, and anyone who comes here must remain on their guard... (Initial Specialty: Pickpocketing Mastery)]","Hmm?","There was actually a choice of business paths?","Then of course she would choose the Black Inn~","After all, if she chose the Black Shop route, she could still make an honest living if things went south. At worst, she would have to collect recipes herself and progress more slowly. But if she chose the White Shop route, there was a chance that the special skills and recipes would be locked away entirely, leaving her with no room to advance or retreat.","Besides... who could see a pickpocketing skill and not choose to have it? Had they just gotten out of rehab?!","Wu Guanyue decisively chose the Black Shop route.","【You have made up your mind. You will never end up as destitute and down-and-out as your grandfather. In this world, hard work alone is not enough to live a good life. You have hidden some of your unique skills, and when the opportunity arises, you do not mind using them...】","【Acquired: Pickpocketing Mastery!】","Excellent.","Now, she just had to go find the shop assistant, Wang Er.","Wu Guanyue followed the stairs down from the second floor. The moment she reached the main hall, she triggered an event.","The inn’s front doors stood wide open, and several people had gathered outside. They were all dressed in black, with fierce expressions on their faces. A short man in a coarse cloth shirt was bowing and scraping before the leader of the group of black-clad men.","Above their heads were the labels [Shop Assistant Wang Er] and [Debt Collector Zheng San].","【Wang Er: “Third Master Zheng, what brings you here today? Please, come right in, come right in! We just got some new Jinwu Bai in stock. I’ll brew you a pot right away!”】","【Zheng San: “Wang Er! Stop running your mouth. I don’t have time for your nonsense. Where’s Old Man Wu’s brat? Hurry up and tell her to come out!”】","【Wang Er: “Third Master Zheng, our boss only arrived last night, so she’s still... Ah? Boss, what are you doing down here?”】","【Zheng San (letting out a cold laugh): “So you’re Old Man Wu’s brat? What’s your name?”】","【Please enter your name】","So that was how it worked. She had reached the naming screen.","Wu Guanyue casually replied, “My name is Coca-Cola.”","Zheng San: “...”","Wang Er: “...”","Ellipses appeared above both NPCs’ heads.","【Zheng San: “...What?”】","Was that not allowed? Was “Cola” a restricted word?","Wu Guanyue obediently changed her answer. “My name is Flying-Through-Heaven-and-Drilling-Into-the-Earth Handsome Cockroach.”","Zheng San: “......”","【Zheng San (eyes bulging with rage): “A debt must be repaid—that’s only right and proper! You little brat, do you really think you can get out of this by pretending to be crazy and playing dumb?!”】","As he spoke, Zheng San reached into his sleeve and pulled out a contract. He gave it a shake, and because the game’s rendering was so realistic, even the rustling of the document sounded completely authentic.","【Zheng San: “Fellow townsfolk, neighbors, and friends! This little girl’s grandfather owes our Yongfeng Money House a full one hundred taels of Tongxuan silver! The borrower’s signature and fingerprint are all clearly stamped on this IOU. There’s not the slightest bit of forgery! And yet this little girl is pretending to be crazy and refusing to acknowledge the debt. What kind of sense does that make?”】","【The thugs: “What kind of sense does that make! What kind of sense does that make!”】","【Zheng San (clearing his throat): “Your grandfather borrowed the money from us using the inn’s land and property deed as collateral. We’re reasonable people, so here’s the deal: either you produce one hundred taels of Tongxuan silver today to repay the debt, or you hand the inn over to us. What do you say?”】","The scene on the long street was incredibly lifelike as well. Day had broken, and some of the shops on either side were open while others had yet to start business. There were not many pedestrians, but everyone was looking in this direction. Among them were even a few cultivators carrying weapons.","At the Four Treasures Hall directly across from the inn, the shop assistant ducked his neck and shrank behind the shop sign that read “Talismans and Ink, Everything You Need.” Several passing cultivators stood with their arms folded, watching from a safe distance.","Another line of translucent narration appeared before Wu Guanyue’s eyes.","【Merchants are afraid of inviting trouble, while cultivators are wary of getting entangled in karma. When faced with this sort of situation, no one wants to step forward and interfere. It seems everything will have to depend on you...】","***","At that very moment, Zheng San cast a sidelong glance at the young woman standing before him.","The girl appeared to be around eighteen or nineteen years old. She was so young that the fine, translucent fuzz on her face had yet to fade completely. After hearing his words, her eyes widened in unmistakable shock.","A little brat who hasn’t even finished growing yet... Hmph!","There wasn’t a money house in existence that wasn’t ruthless and black-hearted, and Yongfeng Money House was no exception. In fact, they made their fortune by issuing predatory loans at exorbitant interest rates. In the years since they had established themselves, they had already driven countless families to ruin, forcing them to sell off their property and land.","This time was no different.","Yongfeng Money House had set its sights on Old Man Wu’s inn. Taking advantage of his serious illness, they had tricked him into pressing his fingerprint onto a contract mortgaging the property and land. They had expected to take the place without a fuss, but then Old Man Wu died—and a granddaughter suddenly appeared to get in their way.","That was why Zheng San had come today: to seize the inn by force!","Zheng San glared at her with his tiger-like eyes and demanded harshly, “Are you paying the money or handing over the property? Give us your answer right now!”","And the player... the player was also utterly shocked!","Because her main quest had changed!","【Main Quest: Prevent the Inn from Being Mortgaged (New!)】","【Quest Details: The shop assistant is being harassed. It turns out your grandfather incurred a massive debt with Yongfeng Money House, and the debt collectors are forcing you to hand over the property deed. Stop the inn from being mortgaged! (P.S. Losing the inn will result in an immediate Game Over.)】","Wu Guanyue: “???”","Wait, what?!","It was perfectly normal for a simulation management game to begin with a mountain of debt... but hadn’t that NPC just said she had to repay the money immediately? He really had said immediately, hadn’t he?! The game had only started five minutes ago! How was she already facing a Game Over?!","No, calm down, Wu Guanyue. Even Hidetaka Miyazaki wouldn’t pull something like this. An unknown game developer had no reason to deliberately make things this infuriating. That meant there had to be an obvious solution—she just hadn’t noticed it yet.","An obvious solution...","An obvious solution...","Wu Guanyue’s mind raced as she clicked every icon within sight on the game’s control panel—","【Open Inventory】—There were twelve inventory slots in total, currently containing only the starting tools, such as a broom and a mop, along with [Property and Land Deed] ×1. That was the item she had to defend to the death, so she couldn’t simply display it like a lawyer’s badge.","【System Settings】—[Return to Main Menu], [Exit Game], [Unstuck]... She had no idea why she had even bothered opening this screen.","【View Attributes】—View the personal attributes of [Debt Collector Zheng San]!","【Name: Zheng San】","【Occupation: Debt Collector for Yongfeng Money House】","【Level: LV.2 (Qi Gathering)】","【Inventory: [Bulging Money Pouch] ×1, [Wu Guizhen’s IOU] ×1, [Wine Gourd] ×1, [Roasted Chicken Wings] ×3, [Guokui Flatbread] ×2, [Fried Rice Cakes] ×5】","The instant she saw [Bulging Money Pouch], a bolt of wisdom struck Wu Guanyue’s mind!","So that was it—she knew what to do now!","【Using initial skill—Pickpocketing!】","And so Zheng San watched as Old Man Wu’s granddaughter... under the pressure he was exerting, the young woman abruptly raised her head. Her pair of jet-black eyes fixed intently on him—and then vanished from before his eyes!!!","Zheng San’s pupils contracted sharply, and he immediately retreated several steps.","But Wu Guanyue had already moved. She was so fast that Zheng San couldn’t see her clearly. In the next instant, she was standing behind him.","She stood there quietly, turning to look at Zheng San, a bulging money pouch still bouncing lightly in her hand.","【Obtained: [Bulging Money Pouch] ×1】","She suddenly smiled and naturally held the money pouch out to Zheng San. In a bright, clear voice, she asked, “Look, is there enough money in here to pay off the debt?”","Zheng San stared at her, dumbfounded.","Her footwork... was actually that good?","No, wait! Why did this money pouch look so familiar?!","His expression changed. He hurriedly reached into his sleeve... and, sure enough, found nothing.","He looked back at Wu Guanyue. She was still holding out the money pouch, staring at Zheng San with complete seriousness. Her expression was utterly innocent and self-righteous, as if she hadn’t noticed anything wrong at all.","Zheng San: “............”","Zheng San: “..................”","Above Zheng San’s head, a gigantic crossroads appeared."]},{"number":2,"title":"Chapter 2","paragraphs":["In broad daylight! With everyone watching! Someone had actually lifted his money pouch right out from under his nose!","And that wasn’t even the worst of it! She was planning to use his money to pay off his debt!","If that didn’t count as provocation, then what did?!","Zheng San felt as though all the blood in his body had rushed straight to his head.","“How dare you! You wretched little thief! Just you wait—we’ll take you to Verdant Cloud Cave Heaven and have them judge this!”","As he shouted, Zheng San struck Wu Guanyue with one palm!","[HP -50]","Wu Guanyue: “??!”","She had thought she’d found the perfect solution and was secretly congratulating herself when an NPC suddenly lashed out and smacked her!","Why had she suddenly become a red-name target?!","And why on earth could you get killed by a random encounter the moment you walked out of the shop in a management sim? Were you Zheng San or the Tree Sentinel?!","No, that wasn’t the point. The point was—","The player’s health bar had already fallen below one-third!","Wu Guanyue had only one life. If this NPC hit her one more time, she would die on the spot, triggering the fastest Game Over in history.","No! Not like this!!!","Despite her shock, Wu Guanyue’s mind was racing. When she saw the NPC raise his palm and strike at her again, her years of gaming experience kicked in, and she immediately made her move—","[Using starting skill: Pickpocketing!]","The girl in front of him suddenly moved again.","Once more, she displayed that furtive, sneaky technique of hers. Zheng San saw only a lock of black hair sweep past his eyes. In the next instant, something had appeared in her hand.","And the thing in her hand looked awfully familiar...","[Obtained: 3 Roasted Chicken Wings]","[Roasted Chicken Wing: “Braised wings~ My favorite~” Restores 85 HP when consumed.]","Excellent! Food could restore health!","Wu Guanyue didn’t hesitate for even a moment. She ate the food and refined its energy in an instant!","Thus, Zheng San watched as the girl stared at him expressionlessly, suddenly tossed the chicken wings she had stolen from him high into the air, and swallowed them in a single bite.","Then she flipped her wrist and drew a magical treasure from her spatial pouch!","A three-foot-six-inch-long...","A long-handled mop suddenly appeared in her hand. She flipped her wrist again and gave the mop a sweep. Its ragged head fluttered in the sunlight, whistling through the air with frightening force!","Zheng San: “............”","Zheng San: “..................”","The scene was simply too absurd. Zheng San was completely dumbfounded...","Zheng San might have been stunned, but the player was doing just fine! Wu Guanyue had no idea why the NPC had suddenly staggered, but taking advantage of an opening to finish off your opponent was the essence of player combat!","Wu Guanyue raised her mop and charged!","Zheng San was a level-two mob. His level wasn’t particularly high, but the game’s creator did seem to harbor a strange admiration for Hidetaka Miyazaki. When the player attacked him, it was like scratching an itch; when he attacked the player, each hit took away more than half her health bar.","Fortunately, Zheng San was carrying plenty of food. Stealing from him while attacking and healing herself was a perfectly viable strategy.","Zheng San felt like he was about to go insane.","He had come to collect a debt and hadn’t intended to use force at all. Yet this woman had humiliated him in front of everyone. He had only wanted to show off a little and save face, but she had started stealing his food while ramming that wretched mop into him!","Zheng San left himself open for the briefest moment, and the mop smacked him directly in the face!","As for why he had left an opening in front of someone who clearly had no martial training, that was because the woman had just stolen a guokui flatbread from his spatial pouch and eaten it...","That flatbread was bigger than her face! And she had actually tossed the whole thing into the air and swallowed it in one bite?!!","Zheng San was deeply shaken. He froze for a moment.","His mind thrown into disarray, he was struck several more times by the mop!","Then he clearly heard a belch.","“Burp!”","“So there’s a fullness meter too?”","The girl holding the mop frowned deeply, her expression solemn as she spoke.","Zheng San: “............”","Zheng San: “..................”","Zheng San was tilted beyond reason.","“You! You chewing maggots and eating dung—”","“Zheng San, stand down.”","A voice suddenly rang out from farther down the street.","The curse Zheng San had only half-finished died in his throat. He swallowed it with difficulty, his face turning the color of liver, and silently retreated behind the newcomer.","Wu Guanyue raised her eyes and saw a middle-aged man approaching. He wore fine silk robes and had a pale, clean-cut face. However, because he was short and fat, he looked rather like a tangyuan wearing clothes.","The title above his head read: [Proprietor of Yongfeng Money House · Qian Shi'an]","Qian Shi'an clasped his hands behind his back and slowly walked over. He studied Wu Guanyue for a long while.","[Qian Shi'an, cupping his hands: “I am Qian Shi'an of Yongfeng Money House. May I ask your esteemed name?”]","[Please state your name]","This time, Wu Guanyue didn’t bother being eccentric.","Player: “I’m Wu Guanyue.”","She used her real name outright. It made the immersion stronger that way.","[Qian Shi'an, smiling amicably: “So you are Miss Wu. A pleasure to meet you. While Old Master Wu was still alive, he mentioned you to me as well. Seeing you today, I can tell that heroes truly do come from the younger generation... Miss Wu, you move with great agility. Might I ask which sect you study under?”]","[Please state your background]","Huh? She had to make up something like this too?","Wu Guanyue: “The Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect.”","Qian Shi'an’s brows furrowed.","The Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect? What sect was that? He had never heard of it!","The Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands were rich in spiritual energy, and cultivation was widespread. Countless sects, both large and small, stood throughout the world. In Divine Firmament Province, the Divine Firmament Dao held supreme authority, commanding the Nine Peaks and Thirty-Six Cave Heavens. The Cloud Platform Realm, where Plum Mountain City was located, took its name from one of those Nine Peaks—the Cloud Platform Peak, home of the Profound Heaven Sect.","Below the Nine Peaks and Thirty-Six Cave Heavens were the local sects.","Although no local sect had produced a great immortal capable of ascending in several thousand years, anyone who underestimated them was sure to die without even knowing how it happened.","Qian Shi'an made his fortune lending money at exorbitant interest. If he wanted to keep doing so, he naturally needed to know who could be provoked and who absolutely could not. He knew every major and minor power in the vicinity of Plum Mountain City like the back of his hand, and he had never heard of any Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect.","Still, the less familiar a name was, the more cautiously it had to be treated.","[Qian Shi'an, laughing heartily: “So you are a distinguished disciple of the Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect. I have long admired your sect—please forgive my earlier disrespect. My subordinate Zheng San offended you. I hope Miss Wu is magnanimous enough not to hold it against him.”]","Wu Guanyue kept her face composed and nodded with great reserve.","“Mm.”","【Qian Shi'an: “A debt must be repaid—that’s only right and proper. The IOU signed by Old Master Wu is written clearly enough, and your shop assistant, Wang Er, can testify to it. Even if this matter were brought before Verdant Cloud Adept, the facts would remain the same.","“However, Miss Wu, you’ve only just arrived, and demanding the shop and land right off the bat was indeed rather inhospitable. How about this? I’ll give you three months’ grace. At the latest, repay these one hundred taels of Tongxuan silver by the end of September. I won’t even charge you interest; consider it a gesture of friendship. What do you say?”】","Now this was how a normal debt-related opening was supposed to go!","Wu Guanyue still kept a solemn expression and nodded with great reserve. “Mm-hmm.”","Qian Shi'an smiled, and his fair, plump face looked just like that of a laughing Buddha.","【Qian Shi'an: “In that case, I won’t disturb you any longer, Miss Wu. I’ll take my leave... Farewell, farewell.”】","With that, he clasped his hands behind his back and turned to leave.","Zheng San followed behind him, and the whole line of black-clad burly men trailed after Zheng San, all of them walking away with their heads bowed.","Before long, the NPCs lining the street had dispersed as well.","***","After Wu Guanyue dealt with the Tree Sentinel—ah, no, after she dealt with Zheng San—the main quest was indeed completed.","【Main Quest: Prevent the Inn from Being Mortgaged (Complete!)】","【Quest Details: For some unknown reason, the owner of Yongfeng Moneylender has agreed to give you three months’ grace on your debt...】","【Reward: [Qian Shi'an’s Promise] ×1】","A new quest appeared right after that—","【Main Quest: Repay the Debt (NEW!)】","【Quest Details: Your grandfather owes Yongfeng Moneylender one hundred taels of Tongxuan silver. Basic common sense tells you that one hundred taels of Tongxuan silver equals one hundred thousand Shensiao copper coins. Within three months, you must pay off this debt... In short, start running the inn as soon as possible! Your shop assistant, Wang Er, will tell you what to do.】","【Progress: 0/100,000 Shensiao copper coins】","Mm-hmm. The beginner’s tutorial was finally about to begin.","Wu Guanyue walked over to Wang Er, triggering a cutscene.","【Wang Er (bowing deeply): “Shopkeeper, welcome! You arrived so late yesterday that I didn’t get the chance to explain everything to you, and I’m terribly sorry for frightening you. It was all my fault, all my fault.”】","After saying this, he even raised a hand and lightly slapped each of his cheeks twice.","【Wang Er: “From now on, whether it’s serving tea, carrying water, running errands, or doing odd jobs, just give the word, and I’ll take care of it!”】","Wu Guanyue: “What should I do now?”","【Wang Er: “You’ve only just arrived and aren’t familiar with the place yet... I’ll take you to the kitchen first and show you around.”】","Wu Guanyue: “Mm-hmm!”","Wang Er then led Wu Guanyue toward the back courtyard, even turning around to remind her to watch out for the threshold. He was being exceedingly attentive and cautious.","He had no choice but to be attentive... because he had a guilty conscience!","Old Shopkeeper Wu had always been in poor health, and over the past two years, his condition had worsened to the point that he could no longer manage the inn’s affairs. Seeing this, Wang Er had secretly begun selling off things from the shop. At first, he had shown some restraint, but as his nerve grew, he eventually sold off even all the furniture in the guest rooms.","As for the matter of Yongfeng Moneylender coercing the old shopkeeper into pressing his fingerprint onto the IOU... Wang Er had naturally made things convenient for them as well.","He had thought the old man was merely a sickly widower who could be bullied to death without consequence...","Who could have guessed that a granddaughter would suddenly appear from who-knew-where?","And this granddaughter was a cultivator—a prized disciple of the Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect!","When Wang Er had watched Wu Guanyue toy with Zheng San just now, his very liver had trembled with fear!","Fortunately, the moneylender—the smiling tiger that he was—clearly had no intention of letting her off so easily. And she still knew absolutely nothing about the situation.","Wang Er figured that as long as he was careful and didn’t reveal anything, the moneylender would deal with her sooner or later.","With these thoughts in mind, Wang Er brought Wu Guanyue to the kitchen.","The kitchen was not large, but it was far from full. There was only a two-burner stove and a yellow-mud baking oven. A large wooden cabinet stood in the corner for storing ingredients, though it was empty now. Apart from that, the kitchen contained only two large flour jars—one filled with wheat flour and the other with buckwheat.","Naturally, this was also Wang Er’s doing. He sighed heavily and said mournfully, “The old shopkeeper was terribly ill toward the end, and our inn hasn’t been open for a long time. We haven’t even bought any supplies... Shopkeeper, shall we go take a look out front?”","The new shopkeeper did not suspect a thing. She merely asked, “What dishes can we sell right now?”","Wang Er secretly breathed a sigh of relief.","Cultivators were obsessed with martial training and knew nothing about these mundane affairs. She really was incredibly easy to fool.","Wang Er put on a bitter smile. “The only thing we can sell is baked flatbread.”","The new shopkeeper continued asking questions. “How much does it cost?”","“Four copper coins each.”","I see, the player thought.","One hundred taels of Tongxuan silver was one hundred thousand copper coins. If each baked flatbread sold for four copper coins, then...","Suddenly, she clapped her hands in realization. “That means we only need to sell twenty-five thousand baked flatbreads to pay off the debt! Wang Er, hurry up and get to work!”","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “?!!”","None"]},{"number":3,"title":"Chapter 3","paragraphs":["No way?! Hold on?!!","Wang Er was utterly shocked. His eyes went wide as he stared at the new innkeeper in horror.","And the new innkeeper stood there, looking at him with cold indifference—without the slightest hint that she was joking!","Wu Guanyue certainly wasn’t joking... She was being completely serious!","You see, in a business simulation game like this, there were a great many tasks for the player to handle at the establishment—preparing food, receiving customers, cleaning, and so on. These were all important parts of the game, but they were also repetitive actions.","Without a hiring system to free the player’s hands and let them pursue more interesting explorations, the game wouldn’t have much appeal at all.","For example, right now... In an immortal-cultivation world, there was absolutely nothing appealing about making nothing but baked flatbread!","So the solution was obvious—delegate all the repetitive tasks at the inn to the shop assistant, Wang Er, while the player herself went exploring the overworld!","There was only one problem: What kind of worker exactly was Wang Er? What sorts of tasks could he handle?","Therefore, Wu Guanyue decided to observe him first.","Wu Guanyue didn’t move at all.","Wu Guanyue stared at Wang Er.","Wu Guanyue: Stare.jpg","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “..................”","A huge cold-sweat bubble appeared above Wang Er’s head.","He opened his mouth, trying to struggle one last time. “Innkeeper, I’m afraid flatbread alone won’t sell very well.”","Wu Guanyue: “Collect recipes. Mm-hmm.”","Wang Er: “We don’t seem to have much firewood left in storage...”","Wu Guanyue’s eyes lit up. “Chop trees and stock up on resources. Mm-hmm.”","Wang Er: “............?”","Wang Er: “The inn hasn’t had any business for a long time. I’m afraid our regular customers...”","Wu Guanyue pondered. “This NPC talks a lot... Could there be some hidden storyline to trigger?”","Wang Er: “!!!”","Although he had no idea what “NPC” meant, the word “hidden” immediately struck a chord in Wang Er’s heart, as though a thunderbolt had hit him!","Wang Er: “...Ha-ha, then I’ll get to work right away. Just call me if you need anything!”","He immediately turned around, scooped a ladleful of flour from the flour jar, and began kneading the dough on the cutting board.","Wu Guanyue’s probing gaze remained fixed eerily on his back.","Wang Er kneaded the dough even more vigorously...","Once the dough had been kneaded and placed in the oven, it would still take some time to bake. To avoid Wu Guanyue’s scrutiny, Wang Er busied himself to the point of exhaustion. He grabbed a broom and swept the first-floor common room, wiped down the tables, and put up the menu.","Wu Guanyue’s figure drifted into the common room like a ghost, still staring thoughtfully at Wang Er...","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “..................”","Wang Er hurried to the entrance and flung open the inn’s front doors with a “whoosh.” Standing in the doorway, he began calling out, “Come take a look! Freshly baked flatbread, four copper coins each! Tasty and affordable—don’t miss it as you pass by!”","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","He could actually handle every kind of task—a truly all-purpose NPC!","In most business simulation games, a single employee could usually handle only part of the workload. To completely hand off the inn’s daily operations, one would need to hire three or four employees.","The game was surprisingly player-friendly in that regard.","Wu Guanyue was very satisfied and prepared to explore the town.","As she was leaving, she spotted a sparkling point on the counter in the inn’s common room that could be investigated. When she went over to examine it, she found a blank thread-bound notebook.","[Obtained: Business Journal!]","[Business Journal: Running an inn is a complicated and tedious undertaking. You can record anything you wish to remember here.]","So that was how it worked.","Since it wasn’t convenient to jot down little in-game tips beside the computer while playing a full-dive game, the game came with a built-in notebook function.","Wu Guanyue took the business journal with her and left the inn.","The thin morning mist had gradually dispersed, and sunlight now shone over the small town surrounded by mountains. A wild, roguish downpour had swept through during the night, leaving the flagstones of the streets damp.","An old man selling fruit stepped across the wet flagstones. The shops on both sides of the road were opening one after another, though many still had their doors tightly shut behind wooden shutters. The shop assistant at the Four Treasures Hall across the street was dozing inside the store...","The whole place looked terribly desolate.","Wu Guanyue opened the world map.","Meishan City was not particularly large. A main street divided the entire city into two halves. To the east, the city extended up along the mountain. Halfway up the slopes, immortal mist swirled around a peak marked on the map as [Feilai Peak · Azurecloud Grotto-Heaven], the sect domain governed by the mountain lord, Verdant Cloud Adept.","As a result, the buildings in eastern city were noticeably more orderly and luxurious than those in the west. It was a typical neighborhood for the wealthy.","As for Wu Guanyue’s inn... Naturally, it was in the poorer western district.","Her inn was located on a narrow lane called Flagflower Road. It wasn’t even considered a good location by western-district standards, and every household along it looked gloomy and lifeless.","Once she reached Meishan City’s main street, however, the atmosphere was completely different. The road was clearly wider and smoother, and the pedestrians passing by were bustling. Shops with high-hanging signboards lined both sides of the street: clothing stores, talisman shops, magical artifact stores, Rejuvenation Halls, carriage and horse agencies... Not to mention the establishments that absolutely could not be missing—restaurants and inns!","There were at least thirty or forty restaurants along the street, along with seven or eight inns. The most conspicuous of them was a large establishment called the Yue Lai Inn. It stood three full stories high, with glazed lotus lamps perched on its soaring eaves. The male guests passing through wore crane cloaks and light furs, while the women wore tall coiffures and feathered robes. At a glance, it was obvious that they were either rich or noble.","Because she had started with the basic Pickpocketing proficiency, Wu Guanyue felt an irresistible urge to try her hand on these rich and noble NPCs...","But unlike Zheng San, the NPCs here were at least level three or four. Her chance of successfully pickpocketing them was very low...","And if she failed, it would immediately start a fight!","As for her own level...","Wu Guanyue opened the status interface.","[Inn Details]","[Name: Ah Ah Ah Oh Oh Oh Uh Uh Uh Let Me See How Many Characters the Longest Game Name Has—Filler Filler Filler Filler As If the Emperor Himself Were Present—Inn]","[Inn Level: LV.1 (Your little shop is completely unknown)]","[Inn Popularity: 11/100 (This morning’s events made some people willing to patronize your business)]","[Inn Revenue: 104/10,000 (The stream has only just begun to flow)]","[Innkeeper Details]","[Innkeeper: Wu Guanyue]","[Level: LV.1 (Your strength and the inn’s fate are inseparably linked)]","[Skills: [Pickpocketing · Beginner]]","The innkeeper’s level was clearly tied to the inn’s level. She had only obtained the inn today, so of course she was merely a level-one newbie player.","If this were any other game, she would absolutely have tried something reckless. At worst, she could restart.","But this game couldn’t be restarted...","Wu Guanyue opened the journal and solemnly recorded a little tip:","Don’t pickpocket people on the street before leveling up!","After that, she even explored the outskirts of town and brought back quite a haul of wild-foraged items.","[Branches] ×8, [Stones] ×5, [Wild Apricots] ×15, [Plantain] ×4, [Dandelions] ×3, [Potentilla] ×6, [Dragon’s Tooth Grass] ×7...","There was no doubt about it—scavenging was the most fun part of the game. Some of these resources even had the “ingredient” tag, meaning they could be processed in the shop and sold!","Wu Guanyue continued recording another little tip: You can forage for resources in the wilderness!","Before she knew it, all twelve of Wu Guanyue’s inventory slots were full.","Satisfied, she returned to the inn!","But who could have expected that, the moment she got back, she would witness a shocking scene!","The shop assistant, Wang Er, wasn’t working at all. Instead, he was crouched in the kitchen, reaching his sinful hand toward her baked flatbreads!","—NPCs could actually steal things!!!","Wu Guanyue was horrified. She charged at Wang Er and demanded furiously, “Wang Er! Why aren’t you working? And why are you stealing food?!”","Wang Er: “......”","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er had genuinely worked all day and was so exhausted that his stomach was pressed against his back. He stared wide-eyed at her and cried out incredulously, “Boss! You expect me to work, but you won’t even let me eat?! You’re trying to starve me to death!”","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","So that was it!","The game actually had a feature where employees needed to eat!","The previous game she’d played, Rest of the [Something], hadn’t had any such feature, so she’d completely overlooked it!","Wu Guanyue stood where she was and nodded solemnly. Then she once again opened her management journal and recorded the most valuable little tip she had learned that day—","“Shop assistants need to eat to stay alive.”","Then she left as though nothing had happened.","Her inventory was full, so Wu Guanyue sorted everything into the chest behind the first-floor counter.","She had been playing for several hours. It was about time to log off.","The game ran at the same speed as real time, and when players logged off, their characters automatically remained on standby—rather like in Animal Crossing.","Wu Guanyue guided her character back to the starting room on the second floor and lay down on the bed. Then she logged out of the game.","***","Meanwhile, Qian Shi’an, master of Yongfeng Money House, immediately sent people to investigate the so-called Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect after returning to the money house.","Yet after asking around for half a day, they discovered that no one had ever heard of such a sect.","That was strange. Meishan City might not be large, but thanks to Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven and its numerous secret realms, it attracted heroes and beauties from all across the Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands. News traveled freely here. There was absolutely no reason they should have been unable to find anything.","Could that little girl have been bluffing him?","And yet there was no denying that the girl was extremely abnormal. She clearly possessed not the slightest trace of true force or spiritual energy, but she had nevertheless toyed with Zheng San until he was completely helpless. Her ability to pluck things from a bag had even allowed her to steal items directly from Zheng San’s storage pouch...","Old Man Wu’s death was connected to them. This grudge was certainly going to be settled.","No. He had to investigate personally!","Taking advantage of the darkness of night, Qian Shi’an changed into a black outfit and left the money house. He leaped onto the rooftops and headed straight for Wu Guanyue’s inn...","What was the name of that inn again?","His movements were so nimble that he looked almost like a nimble, light-footed wild boar.","After spotting the inn signboard covered in tiny lettering, Qian Shi’an flipped through the air and landed on the ground without making the slightest sound. He was far better at this than Zheng San.","The inn’s main doors were tightly shut, and no lanterns had been lit outside. The entire street was pitch-black.","Qian Shi’an moved his hand and formed the “Opening” hand seal. The main doors swung open silently.","Qian Shi’an’s specialty was a concealment technique. Once activated, this technique was so powerful that even the Verdant Cloud Adept of Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven might not be able to see through it.","Therefore, he wasn’t worried that Wu Guanyue would discover him.","With a single flash, he landed behind the counter in the main hall.","A wooden chest sat there. Qian Shi’an focused his attention and examined it for a moment. Seeing no trace of a sealing spell, he formed the “Opening” hand seal again and opened the chest.","Inside was a jumbled pile of branches and weeds. Qian Shi’an frowned and rummaged through them. Suddenly, he caught sight of a thread-bound notebook with yellowed pages.","Qian Shi’an reached out and opened it...","His pupils contracted sharply!","On the page he had turned to was a line of writing that no human being could possibly have said—","[Shop assistants need to eat to stay alive.]","...Could it be a demon?!","“Rumble—!”","A peal of thunder suddenly sounded outside, and the rain began to fall again.","I changed all the “towns” to “cities”...... Towns are too small to work with."]},{"number":4,"title":"Chapter 4","paragraphs":["People need to eat. That was common knowledge.","Ordinary mortals ate the five grains, naturally, while Daoist cultivators treated their bodies as furnaces and cultivated inner elixirs. If they wanted their bodies to become tough and powerful, they needed more than just physical training. What they ate and drank was equally important.","Besides, eating and sexual desire were the two oldest urges known to humanity. Daoist cultivators merely practiced the Dao; they had not actually ascended beyond the Ninth Heaven. How could they possibly sever themselves from all emotion and desire? It was true that some great masters consumed nothing but pills...but such people were few and far between.","Qian Shi'an’s gaze shifted upward, where he noticed several more lines of small writing.","[You can pick up resources in the wild!]","[Don’t pickpocket people on the street before you level up!]","The handwriting was crooked, and the ink still looked fresh... It was almost as if some demon who had just entered the mortal world, utterly ignorant of humanity, was observing, writing things down, and learning how to appear more human!","“Rumble—!”","Another peal of thunder rang out. Raindrops pelted the ground, quickly forming a dense, pale curtain of rain.","A demon... A demon...","For a demon to cultivate a human form, it needed at least several hundred years of cultivation. What was more, demons seeking enlightenment and ascension had to pay even greater heed to karma than humans did. That was why there were so many stories about foxes repaying those who had saved them. If Wu Guanyue had come to avenge Old Man Wu...","Qian Shi'an’s heart gave a jolt. He immediately extended a hand and prepared to divine Wu Guanyue’s origins.","Although Qian Shi'an’s cultivation was not particularly high, he had an excellent master: Daoist Master Songfeng, a thousand-year-old tree demon. Daoist Master Songfeng was profoundly accomplished, especially in divination, and Qian Shi'an had inherited considerable skill in that area.","Earlier that day, when Zheng San had tangled with Wu Guanyue, Qian Shi'an had actually been watching from the shadows. He had also heard Wu Guanyue introduce herself at the very beginning...","Since she was a demon, he first needed to determine what kind of demon she was. Only then could he know what to do next.","Had she said... “Flying-through-the-Sky, Burrowing-through-the-Earth, Handsome Cockroach”?","What kind of origin was that?","Flying-through-the-Sky, Burrowing-through-the-Earth, Handsome Cockroach... Flying-through-the-Sky, Burrowing-through-the-Earth, Handsome Cockroach...","Qian Shi'an knitted his brows tightly. His fingers moved incessantly as he calculated, while he murmured under his breath, “Trace the trail, seek the source, pursue the name. Flying-through-the-Sky, Burrowing-through-the-Earth, Handsome Cockroach, reveal your true form!”","Suddenly, his expression froze.","Qian Shi'an felt a sharp pain in his chest. His blood and qi churned, and with a retch, he actually spat out a mouthful of blood!","That... That was...!","It was an indescribable entity completely unrelated to the Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands, something that had come from another world!","Qian Shi'an endured the pain and forced his way through the mists between worlds, finally seeing the strange creature clearly.","A shiny shell, twitching antennae... An insect! Wu Guanyue’s true form was an insect!","Qian Shi'an: “......”","A cockroach... repaying a debt of gratitude?","Was Old Man Wu bored out of his mind? When other people saved someone, they saved a white fox. He, on the other hand, had gone and lavished his kindness on a long-whiskered vermin.","Still...an insect demon would be easy to deal with. An insect demon would be easy to deal with!","He happened to know of a place that was particularly effective against insect demons...","His figure blurred, and he flashed into the rear courtyard where Wang Er lived. He woke him up and whispered a few instructions into his ear.","Rise and shine!","Face the sun!","Time to start the game!","Meow meow meow meow!","Yesterday’s gaming experience had been so wonderful that when Wu Guanyue removed her helmet that night, she had actually felt a pang of reluctance.","Still, being able to move about freely with a normal body inside the game was already more than enough to satisfy her.","So she logged into the game first thing in the morning.","It was morning in the game as well. Sunlight shone through the wooden window, seemingly coaxing out the fresh scent of pine. The inn’s assistant, Wang Er, was already awake and was drawing water in the rear courtyard.","First, she should check the progress of her quest.","[Quest · Progress: 208/100,000 Divine Firmament Coins]","She had sold fifty-two baked flatbreads yesterday, bringing in 208 copper coins. At that rate, she would make 18,720 copper coins over the course of three months—that was only...one-tenth of what the quest required.","As expected, the quest was not going to be that simple.","But that was within Wu Guanyue’s expectations. After all, if she could complete the quest simply by relying on the baked flatbreads automatically sold by the hired-worker system, where would the gameplay be?","The proper way to play was, of course, to gather ingredients and sell more expensive food to increase her turnover.","She was not discouraged. She sprang from the bed and happily dashed outside.","She rushed out of the inn and spoke to the neighboring street NPC!","[Businesswoman · Auntie Wei (sighing inwardly): “Miss Wu, you... Ah, listen to your auntie. No one can make a successful business in a place like this. You’d best leave while you still can.”]","[What should you say?]","[A. (Passionate) I’m going to become the Innkeeping Queen!]","[B. (Scolding) Counsel from a defeatist strategist is worthless!]","Select A.","Wu Guanyue: “Don’t say another word, Auntie Wei. I’m going to become the Innkeeping Queen!”","Auntie Wei: “............”","Why did she feel that this girl’s brain was a little... Well...","Wu Guanyue: “Auntie Wei, what sort of tasty foods have been popular in the city lately?”","Auntie Wei sighed silently.","She was not close to Old Master Wu. She had only given Wu Guanyue that oblique warning because she could not bear to watch the girl throw herself foolishly against a brick wall. But the girl clearly had not understood...","Ah, there was nothing more she could do. Everyone had their own fate.","She said no more and simply told Wu Guanyue what she wanted to know.","[Auntie Wei: “There are plenty of wealthy Daoist cultivators in Meishan City. If you want to make money, you need to cater to them. It’s sweltering these days, so what they need are things that can relieve the dryness caused by their elixir flames.”]","Wu Guanyue seized upon the key phrase. “The dryness caused by elixir flames?”","[Auntie Wei: “We don’t cultivate the Dao ourselves, so we don’t understand it very well. But they say that the deeper a cultivator’s cultivation, the more strongly they’re affected by the forces of Heaven and Earth. Take this scorching weather, for example. If you imagine the sun as an alchemy furnace, we ordinary people are being roasted outside it. Daoist cultivators, however, are closer to the furnace—and some even want to climb inside. They can actually feel the sun’s true fire!”]","[Auntie Wei: “The Yue Lai Inn on the main street sells Frostflower Lotus Seed Soup. It’s made with frostflower lotuses from the Bingyi Secret Realm, so it can dispel the sun’s true fire. And the Xihua Old Establishment sells Jadeite Chilled Soup, made with Everlasting Ice. Daoist cultivators love eating there.”]","[Auntie Wei: “But frostflower lotuses and Everlasting Ice can only be found in secret realms.”]","So that was how it worked.","If she wanted to make money, she had to cater to Daoist cultivators. And if she wanted to cater to Daoist cultivators, she had to enter secret realms to find special ingredients capable of dispelling the sun’s true fire.","Wu Guanyue opened the map and took a look...","[Secret Realm · Bingyi Realm], [Secret Realm · Redpine Forest], [Secret Realm · Huiming Mountain], [Secret Realm · Fire Crow Territory]...","There were so many! And none of them had a recommended entry level!","Given this game’s usual behavior, if she accidentally wandered into a high-level secret realm, there was a very real chance she would die in there.","So she immediately continued questioning Auntie Wei.","Wu Guanyue: “So, which secret realm can I go to?”","Auntie Wei was horrified. “What?! You’re going in by yourself? You silly girl... You’re supposed to hire rogue cultivators for this! Don’t treat your life like a joke!”","Auntie Wei advised the player not to go.","But naturally, the player wasn’t going to listen to such defeatist remarks meant only to set the mood. She merely nodded calmly, thanked Auntie Wei, and turned back toward the inn.","She found the shop assistant, Wang Er, and initiated a conversation.","Wu Guanyue: “Wang Er, do you know of any nearby secret realms that produce something capable of relieving the dryness caused by alchemical fire?”","—Wang Er was a tutorial NPC. Asking him would definitely be the more reliable option.","Wang Er: “!!”","He had still been worrying about how to deceive the shopkeeper!","Last night, the moneylender had come to see him and told him that he already knew the shopkeeper’s true identity. As long as Wang Er lured her into a certain secret realm, she was guaranteed never to return.","He had been wondering how exactly to trick the shopkeeper into going there... but now, it seemed like the answer had practically landed in his lap!","Wang Er’s heart bloomed with delight. He eagerly leaned forward, rubbing his hands together as he said, “Shopkeeper, I really do know one! You should go to Red Pine Forest! It has exactly what you need!”","Wu Guanyue: “Oh? What does Red Pine Forest have?”","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er fell silent.","Right. What did it have?","He couldn’t exactly say it had something capable of killing the shopkeeper.","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Wu Guanyue once again fixed Wang Er with those pitch-black eyes, staring at him thoughtfully...","Wang Er was practically sweating bullets. In his panic, he blurted out, “It... it has fish, Shopkeeper! The old shopkeeper loved going there to fish!”","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","It had appeared! The fishing mechanic!","In any cozy farming sim... no, in any game that lets you explore a vast open world, a fishing mechanic was absolutely essential. Whenever you came across an unfamiliar body of water during your travels, who wouldn’t want to hurriedly cast a line a couple of times?","So that was how it was...","That was how it was...","Then, now...","She waited patiently.","Wang Er: “............”","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Wang Er asked cautiously, “Shopkeeper, aren’t you going?”","Wu Guanyue: “Where’s the fishing rod?! Shouldn’t you be giving me a fishing rod too?!”","Wang Er: “............”","Why did he have to be the one to provide the fishing rod as well?!","Still, wanting to send this walking calamity away as quickly as possible, he put on a smiling face and said, “Ah, now that you mention it, I really had forgotten. Just wait a moment—the old shopkeeper did leave you a fishing rod!”","He then went back inside and brought out the fishing rod he himself had mooched off the old shopkeeper...","【Obtained: Old Fishing Rod!】","【Old Fishing Rod: It looks ordinary enough, but there seems to be something unusual about its pitch-black rod shaft...】","Wu Guanyue snatched the fishing rod and ran off!","Wang Er: “Hey! Hey! Be careful with that thing!!!”","But Wu Guanyue didn’t hear him at all! She charged straight toward [Secret Realm: Red Pine Forest]!","Running across the map out of sheer boredom...","【Entered: Secret Realm: Red Pine Forest】","This was a pine forest shrouded in cold mist. The tree trunks appeared a strange dark red through the fog, while a layer of white frost clung to the pine needles.","Several ax-wielding men dressed like lumberjacks were chopping wood and singing work chants: “One, two! One, two!”","Red Pine Forest produced a type of fire-resistant pinewood used as fuel for refining external elixirs. Many ordinary villagers came here to chop wood and sell it to alchemists.","Wu Guanyue came charging over!","【Lumberjack·Eldest Brother Li (smiling amiably): “Hey! Are you here to chop wood too?”】","Wu Guanyue plunged straight into the depths of the forest!","【Lumberjack·Second Brother Li (frowning): “Hey! Don’t go any deeper! People have gone missing in there lately!”】","Wu Guanyue’s eyes were filled with nothing but the desire to fish. She sped away, and her figure quickly vanished from sight.","【Lumberjack·Eldest Brother Li (muttering): “What a strange person...”】","【Lumberjack·Second Brother Li (his expression changing dramatically): “Where’s Third Brother Li?! Where did Third Brother run off to?!”】","By this time, Wu Guanyue had already found the fishing spot!","The fishing spot was a frigid pool deep within Red Pine Forest. Its waters were so clear they looked like a flawless piece of ice, and flat, round fish swam among the aquatic plants.","Wu Guanyue took the fishing rod from her inventory.","She charged up her throw and cast the line—!!!","Something was on the hook!","【Obtained: Waterweed!】","【Waterweed: It’s slimy. (Eating it restores 10 HP.)】","She charged up and cast the line again—!","【Obtained: Waterweed!】","【Waterweed: It’s slimy. (Eating it restores 10 HP.)】","【Obtained: Bone Fragment!】","【Bone Fragment: Seems to be a fragment of some animal’s bone.】","The odds of catching an actual fish didn’t seem very high. Wu Guanyue cast her line more than a dozen times in a row, but most of the time, all she caught was waterweed.","No matter. Keep going!","Fishing was the most fun thing ever!","After all, Wu Guanyue had managed to complete the entire fish collection in Stardew Valley!","She charged up and cast the line—!","A powerful musical score suddenly rang out beside her ears, and blue-violet sparks exploded across the surface of the water.","【[Wu Guanyue] triggered the [Lightning Force] effect of the [Old Fishing Rod]!】","【Obtained: Crucian Carp (Bronze Star) ×5, Crucian Carp (Silver Star) ×3, White Minnow (Gold Star) ×10!】","【Crucian Carp: Delicious and popular with men and women of all ages. (Eating it restores 75 HP.)】","【White Minnow: A common little fish, shaped like a willow leaf and glittering silver-white beneath the sunlight. (Eating it restores 35 HP.)】","【Item: Thunderstruck Wood Fishing Rod (New!)】","【Description: A fishing rod made from thunderstruck wood. Casting ten times in succession will trigger its Lightning Force effect. It can be used to electrocute fish, and was purchased by someone at a very high price.】","【Skill·Lightning Force: Powerful lightning qi capable of piercing through anything!】","【[Wu Guanyue] was struck by the [Lightning Force] of the [Thunderstruck Wood Fishing Rod]. HP -85!】","【[Wu Guanyue] learned her lesson: Electrofishing is illegal.】","Wu Guanyue: “............”","...Huh?"]},{"number":5,"title":"Chapter 5","paragraphs":["Wu Guanyue remained silent for a full five seconds before she finally understood what had happened.","So... she had been beaten up by her fishing rod while fishing?","“............”","“..................”","A huge crossroad-shaped vein popped out on Wu Guanyue’s forehead.","She had finally figured it out... The creator of this game had indeed inherited the true teachings of Miyazaki the Old Thief, always finding the most inexplicable places to screw over the player.","And when that was combined with the fact that she only had one chance to play, it made the whole thing especially vicious...","But a player would never bite the dust so easily! Nor would they give up on elec—fishing so easily!","Although she had lost eighty-five HP, she had obtained a full eighteen fish. There was no doubt about it—this was a profitable business!","Wu Guanyue opened her inventory, pulled out nine pieces of waterweed, and wolfed them down, restoring her HP to full. Then she continued trading her health for fish.","Charge up, cast—","At that moment, a panicked cry suddenly shattered the silence.","“What is that?!”","“A demon... It’s a demon!”","“Run! Third Brother Li, run!”","Several men dressed as woodcutters stumbled out from deep within the forest, their faces filled with terror.","Wu Guanyue took a closer look. Two of them were NPCs she had spoken to on the outskirts of Red Pine Forest. Running alongside them was a boy of about eight or nine, who was clutching a completely black, long-haired cat in his arms.","The entire pine forest rustled violently, while the earth trembled ever so slowly, as if something were awakening beneath the soil. In an instant, every living creature in the forest sensed the danger and fled in all directions. The mortals were merely the most insignificant among them.","Then Wu Guanyue saw the red-name monster.","It was a pine tree—the tallest tree in the entire Red Pine Forest, its crown blotting out the sky and sun.","At that very moment, its roots writhed through the earth, supporting its enormous trunk as it slowly advanced toward them!","[Name: Living Pine Tree]","[Race: Tree Demon]","[Level: LV.4]","[Description: An ancient tree that has lived for over a thousand years. Just who was it that awakened it...?]","Wu Guanyue: “???”","Why was it a level-four monster?! Wasn’t this game incapable of supporting battles against monsters above one’s level? Yesterday, she had practically only scratched Zheng San, who was level two!","[Woodcutter · Eldest Brother Li: “Could it be that it killed all the people who went missing before?!”]","[Woodcutter · Second Brother Li: “It’s slow, and we’re fast! Run, fisherman! What are you standing there for?!”]","[Boy · Li Sanlang: “There’s something wrong with it!”]","[Black Cat · Wuyun: (hissing)]","The pine crown that blotted out the sky suddenly shifted. In the next instant, countless pine needles shot down like a torrential rain!","“Pfft-pfft-pfft-pfft-pfft—!”","A wolf that leaped into the air was instantly turned into a porcupine. The force of the pine needles was so great that they made a dull thudding sound as they sank into its flesh.","“Awooo—!”","The wolf was knocked onto its back, letting out a pained howl.","Then something even more terrifying happened—the wolf’s body suddenly began to swell.","Bubbles emerged from inside its body one after another. The wolf thrashed wildly, as if undergoing some excruciating torture!","“Bang—!”","Its body was forced apart by countless pockets of air, exploding like a firework!","[Skill · Pine Needle Storm: Plants use their leaves to breathe... Leaves that burrow deep into flesh breathe too!]","At the same time, the sky-covering rain of pine needles charged straight toward the people beside the pool!","[Woodcutter · Second Brother Li: “We’re going to die! We’re going to die!”]","[Boy · Li Sanlang: “Wuyun! Don’t run around!”]","[Black Cat · Wuyun: “Meow—woof—!”]","The black cat Wuyun, who had just let out a suspiciously dog-like cry, leaped into the air.","The pool water surged upward, carrying crucian carp with it, and formed a curtain of water above everyone’s heads. The pine needles sank into the watery barrier. Bubbles churned within it, and the sound of pfft-pfft-pfft-pfft-pfft rang out without end.","[[Wuyun] used [Skill · Water Curtain] and blocked [Pine Needle Storm]!]","Every strand of fur on Wuyun’s body stood on end! Its tiny body trembled nonstop—","Wuyun: “Meow... gurgle... mrr...”","It was about to collapse!","Wuyun was a demon who had gained intelligence at a young age. It had neither parents nor family, and had been taken in by Auntie Wu when it was little. Now, sixteen years had passed. After Auntie Wu died of old age, Wuyun left her household and spent more than half a month searching around Mount Mei for a quiet place where it could cultivate.","After carefully searching, it had selected Red Pine Forest. Who could have known that Auntie Wu’s three grandsons would happen to be chopping wood there?","Who could have known that Li Sanlang would discover it and chase it into the forest?","Who could have known that such a terrifying demon would be hiding in Red Pine Forest?!","No one had ever taught Wuyun how to cultivate. It did not even know what kind of demon it was! The fact that it had managed to figure out that it was a water-element demon and learn to control water was already impressive enough...","But how could a wood-element demon be afraid of water?!","Water nourished wood... That was the natural law of the five elements...","“Pfft—pfft—!”","More and more pine needles broke through the water curtain and sank deeply into the soil... Yet Auntie Wu’s grandsons and the fisherman were also unable to escape, because behind them lay a freezing pool so deep that its bottom could not be seen...","Wuyun’s claws dug deeply into the earth. Even its tiny triangular mouth was trembling.","“Pfft—!”","A pine needle broke through the water curtain and shot straight toward Wuyun!","Right then, at that very moment, a figure faster than lightning suddenly flew in!","[Used starting proficiency skill—Pickpocket!]","Wuyun felt a sharp pain in its tail... A tuft of fur had been plucked away by the newcomer!","[Obtained: [Fur] ×1]","[Fur: Fur from an unknown creature, but soft to the touch.]","That person’s body firmly blocked the way in front of it. A fishing rod was gripped tightly in her hand—","It was the fishing addict. That fishing addict!","The pine needles came shrieking through the air and struck her!","[[Wu Guanyue] took the [Pine Needle] attack for [Wuyun]. HP -90!]","Yet her body did not burst apart like the wolf’s.","The pine needles struck her, but she did not move an inch. Her expression was as cold and calm as ice, as if there were nothing in this world capable of shaking her resolute heart!","Wuyun stared at her in a daze and heard her icy declaration—","“Even if you’re a monster under the command of Miyazaki the Old Thief, I’ll still kill one for you!”","She abruptly raised her left hand and fiercely bit into the waterweed she was holding!","Wuyun: “............?”","A master’s movements took place in the blink of an eye. Wuyun had only paused for a moment before that fishing senior had already swallowed eight or nine slimy pieces of waterweed in one gulp. Then...","She moved again!","[Used starting proficiency skill—Pickpocket!]","[Pickpocket failed!]","That’s right! Wu Guanyue had used Pickpocket on the level-four monster, [Living Pine Tree]!","Although she had failed, this was already within Wu Guanyue’s expectations. The level gap between her and the monster was simply too great, so the success rate had been extremely low to begin with.","But pickpocketing has a prerequisite effect, and that effect can make her speed unbelievably fast! That was exactly the trait she used to save the black cat Wuyun just now.","As for the Living Pine Tree... its advantage is its massive size, but that's also its biggest weakness!","Wu Guanyue decided to pickpocket the matsutake growing on the Living Pine Tree's roots.","Star-swift, lightning-quick!","Faster than a flash of light!","In the blink of an eye, Wu Guanyue was already standing on top of the enormous pine root. The fishing rod in her hand vanished in an instant, replaced by a lumberjack's axe!","\"Crack——!\"","She swung the axe down hard at the root!","[The Living Pine Tree] took a [Slash] attack from [Wu Guanyue], HP -10!","[Wu Guanyue dodged the [Pine Root Whip] attack from [Living Pine Tree], a total miss!","The entire crown of the Living Pine Tree shook violently. The hit clearly stung it, and it was too distracted to keep fighting with Wuyun. The pine needles lost their power boost, got swept up by the water curtain, and crashed right back onto the Living Pine Tree's body!","[The Living Pine Tree] took a [Water Vortex] attack from [Wuyun], HP -3!","That's not even as much damage as the player's axe!","Oh well... when it comes to NPCs that join in mid-battle, it's already good enough that they don't drag the player down.","Wu Guanyue hefted her axe and kept trying to pickpocket the matsutake.","[The Living Pine Tree] took a [Slash] attack from [Wu Guanyue], HP -10!","[The Living Pine Tree] took a [Scratch] attack from [Wuyun], HP -3!","Auntie Wu's three grandsons weren't sitting idle either!","Eldest Brother Li: \"You monster! I'll fight you!\"","[The Living Pine Tree] took a [Slash] attack from [Eldest Brother Li], HP -10!","Second Brother Li: \"Senior! Wuyun! I'm here to help you—wait, where'd my axe go?!\"","Li Sanlang: \"Wood is afraid of fire! Second Brother, get the flint!\"","Second Brother Li quickly pulled out his flint and tried to light the fallen leaves on the ground... but the forest was so damp that the dirt and leaves were all soaked. The two of them fumbled for ages and couldn't get a single spark going.","Wu Guanyue's axe had also reached its maximum durability, slipped right out of her hand, and flew off to who knows where.","Meanwhile, the Living Pine Tree still had four-fifths of its HP left.","Worse yet...","[4 minutes and 39 seconds until [Skill: Pine Needle Storm] finishes charging!]","The wild monster's ultimate skill was less than five minutes away from being ready!","To be honest, this monster wasn't that hard to fight. Its attack pattern was super simple—it only knew how to swing its roots and pine branches to whip people. And since there were matsutake mushrooms all over its roots and Wuyun had a fluffy, thick tail, Wu Guanyue moved nimbly around the battlefield and wasn't in any real danger of losing her own HP.","But its health bar was absurdly thick!","Wu Guanyue had only been in this game for two days, she didn't have any good gear at all. The random lumberjack axe she'd swiped earlier already hit harder than her mop, and even that dealt damage so little it was like scraping dirt off its body... Even that wouldn't have been so bad, she could have just grinded on it all day to kill it. The real problem was that its ultimate skill was completely broken!","Pine Needle Storm was an AoE attack that dealt massive damage. The wolf in the opening cutscene had already showed how terrifying it was. The only thing that could block that attack was Wuyun's Water Curtain skill.","Wuyun planted its four paws on the ground, its tail held high, hissing nonstop at the Living Pine Tree, but its little paws were trembling nonstop.","[Name: Wuyun]","[Race: ???]","[Level: LV.1]","[Description: A creature that doesn't know what it is, so it often makes suspicious sounds.]","But since Wuyun was only level one, its mana bar was almost completely drained, and it didn't have enough left to cast Water Curtain one more time.","Ugh... this is so hard... this game is way too difficult!","But just think about yesterday's tutorial level, Wu Guanyue!","Yesterday's tutorial was just as tough! Back then she used her newly acquired [Pickpocket] skill to turn the situation around. And she had to admit, that tutorial was really useful—now she had a super deep understanding of how the pickpocket skill worked!","So she could definitely use the same line of thinking to solve this problem today!","The same line of thinking... the same line of thinking...","A flash of brilliant inspiration suddenly struck Wu Guanyue!","She got it! She knew exactly what to do!","The new item she got today was the [Lightning-Struck Wood Fishing Rod]!","Just think about it—earlier she got hit by that rod, right? The rod automatically charges up and zaps fish with electricity after you reel in ten items. But she was standing on the shore, so why did she get shocked too?","There's only one truth— the electricity traveled right through the wooden rod!","Wood is supposed to be an insulator, but wait a second! Think about the skill description for the [Lightning-Struck Wood Fishing Rod]!","[Skill: Thunder Force: The powerful thunder qi can penetrate absolutely anything!]","Penetrate absolutely anything— that definitely includes this huge tree!","Wu Guanyue made up her mind in an instant, gathering all her strength as she yelled: \"Guard—my—back—for—me!\"","Wuyun's eyes narrowed into slits, completely on guard: \"Woof woof!\"","Eldest Brother Li held up his axe: \"Senior! You can focus on your special skill! We've got this!\"","This senior was risking her life to save them, and she was their only hope of surviving. They would never let that accursed tree monster touch even a single hair on the senior's head!","They wondered what kind of powerful formation the senior was about to cast.","But then they watched the senior pull a fishing rod out of her pouch... and then plop herself down on the ground and start fishing!","Eldest Brother Li: \"............?\"","Wuyun the cat: \"............?\"","Living Pine Tree: \"............?\"","Wait a second, this tree monster has a mind of its own!"]},{"number":6,"title":"Chapter 6","paragraphs":["***","A crow suddenly flew across the sky...","Silence blanketed the Red Pine Forest today...","Wu Guanyue’s behavior was so bizarre that even their opponent, the Living Pine Tree, was stunned. After several breaths, its crown suddenly began shaking violently, and its roots started slapping the ground with a series of smacks.","Eldest Brother Li: “............”","Eldest Brother Li: “..................”","Was it just his imagination, or had he really been mocked by a tree?","Wuyun and Third Brother Li stared dumbfoundedly at Wu Guanyue as she went fishing...","Wu Guanyue suddenly turned around and declared righteously, “What are you standing around for? Come lend me a hand!”","Li Sanlang: “Ah! ...Ah... uh... mm...”","Li Sanlang had failed to comprehend the profound meaning of the expert’s words. Ashamed, he said, “Please enlighten us, Senior!”","Wu Guanyue put on a solemn expression. “Put fish on my hook!”","Li Sanlang: “............”","Black Cloud Cat: “............”","Li Sanlang: “............ I see!”","Black Cloud Cat: “............ Meow-woof, meow-woof, gurgle-gurgle?!”","Li Sanlang and Wu Guanyue both turned to stare at Wuyun!","Wuyun: “............”","A string of incomprehensible curses came from Wuyun’s triangular mouth. It shook itself furiously, kicked off with its hind legs, and leaped into the frigid pool!","Wuyun had mastered the art of controlling water without instruction, so diving into the frigid pool to put fish on the angler’s hook was naturally no challenge at all.","The moment Wuyun entered the water, its entire body stretched out long, swimming in a wave-like motion... It actually bore a faint resemblance to a swimming dragon. It extended its little paws and slapped a crucian carp unconscious, then carried it in its mouth and hung it on Wu Guanyue’s hook...","[Obtained: Crucian Carp (Gold Star)!]","[Obtained: Catfish (Gold Star)!]","[Obtained: Sturgeon (Gold Star)!]","Wu Guanyue was positively floating with joy... It seemed there really was a reason anglers dreamed of becoming divers who could put fish on their own hooks...","Still, she didn’t forget to count the catch!","Four, five, six...","The Living Pine Tree’s crown began to rustle and shake!","Seven...","Even the pine needles on its crown were trembling violently!","Eight...","“Not good! It’s about to use that move again!” Second Brother Li cried out in terror.","Nine... Now!","The fishing hook shot high into the air, glittering brilliantly in the sunlight!","“Wuyun! Water tornado!”","Wu Guanyue shouted her command with all her strength!","The black cat leaped from the pool like a fish!","Its fur was completely soaked, sleek and glossy in the sunlight like a giant sea cucumber, while all four of its paws had spread open like plum blossoms—","“Meow—guh—!”","It let out a desperate howl, using up the last trace of its true qi!","A water tornado surged into the sky, roaring forward like a silver dragon. Waterweeds and fish tumbled within it, and at that very moment, Wu Guanyue’s hook flew out and precisely snagged a clump of waterweed—","[[Wu Guanyue] triggered the [Thunderstruck Wooden Fishing Rod]’s [Thunder Force] effect!]","No one could say exactly how thunderous this move was, nor could anyone say why it had come about in the first place.","The roaring water tornado, wrapped in blue-violet light, slammed heavily into the Living Pine Tree!","The magnificent thunder pierced through the trunk in an instant, filling it with a cacophony of crackles and pops. The entire crown writhed wildly, while the roots that had thrust up from underground danced like demons.","But the lightning had already ignited the tree, causing the trunk to burn from within. The flames would not stop until the tree was dead.","—Thunder belonged to fire, and fire naturally countered wood.","Water could nourish wood, but it could also carry thunder. The myriad things in the world were born to support and restrain one another; that relationship had always been so flexible.","Wuyun stared blankly at the Living Pine Tree as it struggled madly.","For a moment, it had thought it was going to die.","It couldn’t help looking toward the human who could remain calm even in the midst of danger.","That person stood exactly where she was, calmly watching the burning Living Pine, as if this were precisely what had been meant to happen.","Wuyun’s round eyes gradually filled with respect.","Wu Guanyue let out an “Aah!” and charged forward, then crouched on the ground and began frantically scooping up everything in sight and stuffing it into her sleeves.","Wuyun: “............”","Wuyun tilted its head, seemingly a little confused.","The three sons of the Li family, however, were quick to catch on. Seeing what was happening, they called to one another and helped Wu Guanyue gather the scattered loot.","After a while, Wuyun obediently joined the looting operation as well.","***","Wu Guanyue discovered that this game’s item-pickup system was incredibly realistic... Realistic in the sense that every single dropped item had to be picked up individually; nothing stacked automatically.","Fortunately, the NPCs’ helpfulness made up for it.","Two woodcutters and a young man were helping her pick up the [Living Pine Needles] scattered all over the ground. Wuyun even had a small pile of pinecones balanced on its head, wobbling as it ran toward her and dropping them one by one along the way... So cute!","The NPCs’ reactions were also genuinely intelligent and perfectly responsive. Just watching Wuyun coordinate with her made her feel as though she were playing an online game and running a dungeon with her teammates...","So this was the power of real-time AI computation... What exhilarating gameplay!","The loot was equally exhilarating!","[Obtained: [Matsutake Mushrooms] ×88!]","[Obtained: [Pine Frost Candy] ×35!]","[Obtained: [Frost Pinecones] ×99!]","[Obtained: [Pine Pollen] ×99!]","[Obtained: [Thunderstruck Wood] ×25!]","[Obtained: [Living Pine Needles] ×999!]","[Obtained: [Living Pine Needles] ×999!]","[Obtained: [Everbright Pine Resin] ×78!]","The player has struck it rich~ The player has struck it rich~ The player has struck it rich~","Most of the Living Pine Tree’s drops were ingredients. Matsutake mushrooms could be sliced and grilled over charcoal for a delicious meal, while pine pollen could be wrapped around rice cakes to make pine-scented pastry balls that were packed with fragrance...","As for the [Pine Frost Candy] and [Frost Pinecones], both came with the [Frost-Cool] effect. They were exactly what Wu Guanyue needed!","As for the Living Pine Needles—the item she had obtained the most of—well, Wu Guanyue had no idea what they were for.","But who cared? As long as her inventory had room, she would take everything back with her!","And finally, she didn’t forget to talk to the NPCs.","Naturally, the NPCs’ reactions were perfectly standard: the usual dialogue about how they could never repay her great kindness. Li Sanlang even gave her a straw-woven Wuyun as a quest reward, which Wu Guanyue happily accepted.","The Living Pine Tree had already dropped an astonishing amount of loot. She hadn’t expected much from an NPC who looked this ordinary, so receiving a limited-edition accessory was already quite nice.","Eldest Brother Li and Second Brother Li, however, broke out in cold-sweat bubbles above their heads when they saw the straw-woven Wuyun.","After learning that she had opened an inn in the city and was short on ingredients, Eldest Brother Li said that their family were farmers from a mountain hollow nearby. If she needed them, they could deliver fresh ingredients to her every day.","Of course she was happy to hear that!","One more supply channel added.","And finally, there was Wuyun.","Wuyun sat primly on the ground, licked one of its paws, and gazed up at Wu Guanyue.","[Black Cat, Black Cloud: “Meow... chirp...”]","[Young Man, Third Brother Li: “Sister Wu, Wuyun says it wants to stay by your side to repay you.”]","[Woodcutter, Second Brother Li: “??? Sanlang, how did you understand that? I grew up with Wuyun, and even I can’t understand him!”]","[Young Man, Third Brother Li (scratching his head): “Anyway... I think that’s what Wuyun meant. Isn’t that right, Wuyun?”]","[Black Cat, Black Cloud: “Meow meow!”]","[Black Cat, Black Cloud] has submitted a [Job Application] to [Innkeeper Wu Guanyue]. Approve?","[Yes]","[No]","Of course, you pick yes!","[Black Cat, Black Cloud] has joined your inn. Please assign it a role!","A. Cleaning (A long-haired cat is excellent at mopping floors)","B. Fishing (A water demon can attach fish to your hook underwater)","C. Mount (You can stand on one leg on its back)","The player picks ABC!","Wu Guanyue: “So, can you mop the floors first every day, then put ten fish on my hook, and finally carry me around to increase my movement speed?”","Eldest Brother Li: “............”","Second Brother Li: “............”","Li Sanlang: “............”","Black Cloud Cat: “............”","Wuyun’s triangular mouth suddenly opened, producing a string of incomprehensible meows. Judging by the sound of it, the insults were rather nasty.","The male lead’s character design has undergone several revisions and now looks completely different from the pixel character in the protagonist panel. I’m taking that one down for now; I’ll put it back up once the new commission is finished."]},{"number":7,"title":"Chapter 7","paragraphs":["***","Although fighting monsters far above her level had been quite perilous, the loot had been extraordinarily bountiful. Wu Guanyue had made a trip to [Secret Realm: Red Pine Forest], struck it rich, and even gained a cat employee on top of that. One could hardly ask for more emotional value.","When they reached Li Family Hollow, the three Li brothers said their farewells. Li Sanlang even asked, rather reluctantly, whether she could come to the inn to visit Wuyun in the future.","Wuyun licked its paws, its ears twitching sharply. Then it shot off and vanished in the blink of an eye. Wu Guanyue did not see it again, even after returning to the inn.","However, Wuyun’s little portrait had indeed appeared on the employee roster beneath Wang Er’s, and its duties were listed as [Cleaning], [Fishing Assistance], and [Mount].","...So although it cursed and grumbled nonstop, had it actually accepted the job?","Hmm...","Wu Guanyue happily stepped into the inn.","It was getting late, and time to rest. She returned to the starting room, logged out of the game, and planned to log back in first thing tomorrow morning.","***","Wang Er, meanwhile, was having a much rougher time of things.","That morning, he had followed the moneylender’s orders and lured the shopkeeper to Red Pine Forest. He had heard that several people had gone missing there before. The moneylender had been utterly confident, claiming he had already seen through her true nature—that she was some kind of insect—and that this time, she was sure to perish without a trace.","But who could have expected...","The shopkeeper had actually come back!","She had returned carrying her fishing rod, standing in exactly the same manner as when she had left that morning. She had even earnestly told him that the fishing spot he recommended was quite good...","Uh...","Wang Er spent the entire latter half of the night unable to sleep.","He tossed and turned in bed.","What, exactly, had the shopkeeper meant by that? Had she fallen into the moneylender’s trap when she went to Red Pine Forest? Hadn’t the moneylender guaranteed that she would never return? How was it that she had not only escaped without injury, but looked more radiant and energetic than ever?","The more he thought about it, the more frightened and uneasy he became. In the middle of the night, Wang Er suddenly sat bolt upright.","No! He couldn’t just sit around waiting for death!","Wang Er immediately got out of bed, reached beneath his pillow, pulled out a piece of cloth, and hurriedly began packing his valuables so he could flee.","Everyone already knew that the shopkeeper was a monster. How could he possibly stay here any longer? True, if the shopkeeper discovered tomorrow that he was gone, she would certainly become suspicious... But he couldn’t afford to worry about that now!","There were two strings of silver coins hidden in the stove—money Wang Er had gotten by selling off items from the inn, and most of his entire fortune. Taking advantage of the darkness, he tiptoed into the kitchen and crouched down to peer into the stove—","...and came face-to-face with Wuyun, which was hiding inside and playing with the ashes.","Wang Er: “............”","Wuyun: “............”","Wang Er: “Aaaah! There’s a demon! A demon!!!”","Wuyun: “Woof woof woof woof woof!!!”","Wuyun let out an indignant cry and fled on all fours.","A pitch-black, suspicious-looking clump of aquatic weeds let out a series of highly questionable dog barks as it vanished into the darkness of the kitchen!","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “..................”","Wang Er rolled his eyes back and collapsed limply like a noodle, scattering the silver coins from his hands.","After a while, Wuyun cautiously poked its head out from a corner.","It circled Wang Er once, leaving a trail of gray paw prints on the floor, then sat down and solemnly began licking its paws.","Wu... Wu Guanyue had said she wanted it to be her mount... But Wuyun didn’t think it could carry her.","Hmm...","Wuyun’s gaze fell upon the unconscious human. Its catlike pupils alternated between round and narrow slits.","After another while, Wuyun spread itself across the floor into a flat cat pancake.","The black cat pancake wriggled along the ground and flowed beneath Wang Er’s body. Wang Er’s body slowly slid forward until his head slammed into something with a bang.","It turned out that the kitchen threshold had blocked their path.","Wuyun: OωO","Wuyun’s eyes opened wide as it appeared to fall into deep thought...","Wuyun: OωO!","Suddenly, it seemed to understand something. It excitedly let out a wolf howl, then flowed back beneath Wang Er’s body.","Back up! Build speed! Charge!","“Bang!”","That was the sound of Wang Er’s head smashing through the threshold.","With Wuyun carrying Wang Er, they shot out of the kitchen like lightning! Even the profound principle that kinetic energy could be converted into potential energy was something Wuyun understood!","“Meow! Meow! Awoof-woof-woof!”","Wuyun let out an excited, rhythmic work chant. Wang Er was plastered against the ground, sliding along at breakneck speed, his head repeatedly slamming into one object after another...","But those were all minor details!","Wuyun was using Wang Er to practice how to carry a person while moving faster.","After nearly half an hour, Wuyun finally deposited the panting Wang Er back in his room.","Two hours later, the crowing of a rooster suddenly broke the silence. The sky began to pale like a fish’s belly, and a new day dawned.","Wang Er groaned and slowly regained consciousness.","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “..................”","...What had he been doing last night? Why was he lying on the floor? And why did his head hurt so much? For some reason, he felt a little nauseated, too.","Holding his head, Wang Er struggled to his feet. The moment he stepped outside, he saw a huge gap in the kitchen threshold. The courtyard was also a complete mess: the water bucket had been knocked over, the firewood had been scattered, and the stool used for washing clothes had been overturned.","...Damn it, had they been robbed?","Wang Er absolutely couldn’t let the shopkeeper see this mess, so he hurried to clean everything up.","Once he had finished, he went to draw a bucket of water and wash his face.","Wang Er lowered the bucket into the well.","But when he pulled it back up, the weight suddenly became much lighter. He hauled up the well rope...and something hanging from the hook glimmered with an eerie light.","It was... a string of silver coins.","The coins looked strangely familiar...","They were clearly the very same coins he had hidden in the stove!","Wang Er’s pupils contracted sharply.","He remembered! He remembered everything!","Last night, he had been planning to flee when he encountered a black clump of aquatic weeds that could bark like a dog in the kitchen!!!","The bucket hit the ground with a bang, spilling water everywhere. Wang Er was just about to run for his life when the shopkeeper suddenly flung open the second-floor window with a loud clatter and cheerfully greeted him.","“Wang Er! Good morning! Did you sleep well last night?”","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “..................”","Suddenly, Wang Er burst into tears and wailed, “Shopkeeper, I swear I’ll never do it again! Shopkeeper!!!”","Wu Guanyue: “?”","***","At that moment, Wu Guanyue was sitting solemnly on a small stool in the inn. Kneeling before her was Wang Er, who kept begging for mercy.","Hmm... A new storyline had been triggered.","Wang Er had suddenly dropped to his knees and confessed everything.","It turned out that the debt had never existed in the first place! The whole thing had been a lie fabricated by Qian Shi’an to seize the inn! Even yesterday’s trip to Red Pine Forest had been a trap set by them to surround and kill her!","How outrageous! Simply outrageous!","At the same time, Wu Guanyue’s main quest was updated as well—","【Main Quest: Pay Your Debts! (Updated)】","【Quest Details: Qian Shi'an drove your grandfather to his death, then went a step further and tried to kill you as well... Behind him stands the mysterious great tree demon. Having slain the tree demon’s minions and descendants, how will you protect the inn your grandfather left behind—and how will you protect your own life?】","So... was a BOSS going to come knocking next?","The mysterious great tree demon was information Wang Er had provided. Apparently, quite a few people had been spreading rumors about it... Though there was no proof, the people nearby were all deeply wary of it and thus afraid to offend Qian Shi'an.","If there was no proof, then it had to be true. How could a game include useless information?","Wu Guanyue opened her character panel again.","【Inn Details】","【Name: Ah Ah Ah Oh Oh Oh Uh Uh Uh Let Me See What This Game’s Longest Name Is—Filler Filler Filler As If I Were the Emperor—Inn】","【Inn Level: LV.1 (Your little shop is completely unknown)】","【Inn Popularity: 5/100 (Selling nothing but baked flatbread has caused your inn’s popularity to plummet)】","【Inn Revenue: 355/10,000 (Selling nothing but baked flatbread has left your inn’s revenue pitifully low)】","【Owner Details】","【Owner: Wu Guanyue】","【Level: LV.1 (Your strength is inseparably linked to the inn’s fate)】","【Skill: [Stealing · Beginner]】","Hmm... So, for players, there was only one path to development after all: upgrade the inn!","As long as the inn’s level increased, the player’s level would naturally increase along with it. There was no reason for the first fixed BOSS to be especially difficult. As long as the player was willing to grind, there shouldn’t be any real problem!","Excellent. How does one dispel one’s worries? Through innkeeping, of course!","As for Wang Er...","Wu Guanyue stared at Wang Er with a stern expression.","Wuyun hissed at him.","Wu Guanyue: “What about the things from my grandfather’s inn? Don’t just tell me about other people’s crimes and ignore your own!”","Wang Er said nothing. He merely kept kowtowing.","【How will you deal with Wang Er?】","【A. (Dark Souls) I’ll chop off your hands and feet, then throw you into the river to feed the fish!】","【B. (Because I’m a good person) What’s past is past. From now on, you’d better work honestly... Oh, right. How about becoming my nuclear-powered donkey?】","Naturally, she chose B!","At a time when the player was about to start grinding like mad, a living nuclear-powered donkey was obviously more useful than a dead traitor!","Wu Guanyue sighed. “Sigh... Who can blame me for being such a good person...”","Wang Er raised his head hopefully.","Wu Guanyue: “You! Right now, clean the entire front hall and rear courtyard, then brush Wuyun’s fur. After that, bake a hundred batches of flatbread and sell them, fry up two dishes, and finally hand over every last coin on you to me!!!”","Wang Er: “............”","Wang Er: “Huh?!”","Wu Guanyue: “What! Are! You! Waiting! For?!”","Wuyun the cat: “Meow! Meow! Meow! Meow!”","Wang Er managed to survive. He rolled and scrambled to hand Wu Guanyue the twenty taels of silver he had made by selling off the inn’s belongings, then slunk away to become a nuclear-powered donkey.","Wu Guanyue, meanwhile, prepared to study some new recipes. She had gotten a huge haul from fighting monsters yesterday, so today she would use those ingredients to experiment with different combinations!","Moreover, early that morning, Eldest Brother Li had brought over some free ingredients as a token of his gratitude.","【Obtained: [Donkey Meat] ×9!】","【Obtained: [Large Intestines] ×8!】","【Obtained: [Green Plum Dew] ×8】","【Obtained: [Limeng Fruit] ×28】","Then, first things first: she would freely combine all the ingredients on hand!","Wu Guanyue pondered for a moment, then suddenly pulled out the large intestines!","【[Wu Guanyue] has created [Large Intestine Sashimi]. Congratulations!】","【Large Intestine Sashimi: Something only a small number of people could possibly enjoy.】","Uh... What a nonsensical dish.","Next attempt.","【[Wu Guanyue] has created [Salt-Grilled Matsutake]. Congratulations!】","【Salt-Grilled Matsutake: The finest ingredients need only the simplest preparation...】","In the game’s item rarity system, it was a purple-quality dish, which meant it was incredibly delicious... But it didn’t have the [Frostcool] attribute, and there weren’t many matsutake mushrooms available, so it couldn’t be sold as a signature dish.","Next.","【[Wu Guanyue] has created [Limeng Fruit Sparkling Water]. Congratulations!】","【Seasonal · Limeng Fruit Sparkling Water: Place living pine needles in water to fill otherwise flavorless water with carbon dioxide bubbles, then add fresh Limeng peel... The True Fire of the Sun sweeps everything away!】","!!!!!!","Isn’t this just Sprite?!","When summer came, what could be more satisfying than a glass of ice-cold, sparkling, refreshing soda? Coca-Cola’s flavoring formula was extremely complicated, but Sprite really was just lemon-flavored sparkling water!","Excellent. This would be the inn’s seasonal summer specialty. The decision was made!","Sprite would conquer the world of immortal cultivation!","There you have it—using pine needles to make sparkling water really does work! Of course, there’s an even simpler way to make carbonated drinks: ginger ale."]},{"number":8,"title":"Chapter 8","paragraphs":["They say the mountains are blessedly cool, but that's only half true. Meishan Town sits nested in the valleys between several peaks, where the yang heat of the sun can stream in but never finds a way out, leaving it far swelterier than the high mountains surrounding it.","Auntie Wei's whole household had been up since the crack of dawn, bustling about rinsing buckwheat grains, spreading pancakes on the griddle, and mixing garlic sauce.","By now, the sun's fiery rays were already searing the ground. Qihua Road was desolate, with barely a handful of passersby, all of them dragging their feet listlessly. The few wandering cultivation travelers who lived nearby were even sparser, only a handful dotted along the street, each carrying weapons and magic artifacts on their persons.","In this kind of weather, even the merchants were going about their work half-heartedly.","The clerk at Four Treasures Hall was dozing off behind the shop counter. The vendor selling flowing cold noodles next door was sitting on the threshold fanning himself, only mustering the energy to call out feebly when he spotted a pedestrian passing by.","\"Flowing cold noodles! Just twenty copper coins for a bowl of flowing cold noodles!\"","Auntie Wei had long grown accustomed to this scene. She unfastened the shop shutters at a leisurely pace to open for business, and no sooner had she stepped outside than she noticed that the inn next door had, for the first time in memory, stopped selling roasted flatbread that day.","A sheet of red paper was pasted to the inn's entrance, bearing neatly written bold characters that read: New product Sprite now on sale! Refreshingly cool, lifting your spirits! Only thirty copper coins a bowl!","Sprite...? What on earth is that?","The name sounded quite nice, and the slogan that followed was lovely too. \"Refreshingly cool, lifting your spirits\" made anyone sweltering in the summer heat unable to tear their eyes away from the sign.","As Auntie Wei stared, Wu Guanyue stepped out carrying a large earthen jar, setting it down on the table under the awning at the entrance. Right behind her trailed a fluffy black cat, balancing a stack of clay bowls on its head. Once everything was in place, Wu Guanyue picked up a large ladle with a serious look on her face, ready to start her business.","Auntie Wei gaped at the big earthen jar. Good heavens! Could this \"Sprite\" that was selling for thirty copper coins be some kind of chilled drink?","She could not help but warn her, \"Miss Wu, it's far too expensive to sell a chilled drink for that price. Look, the cold noodle vendor down the road only charges twenty copper coins a bowl.\"","Ordinary chilled drinks usually went for five or six copper coins. Of course, the Yue Lai Inn on the main street did sell their Frost Lotus Seed Sweet Soup for two taels of dark silver a bowl... but the main street was a prime location, while Qihua Road was nothing like that.","The young Miss Wu did not take her warning to heart, just as cheerful and straightforward as ever. \"No problem, no problem, no problem at all! Leave everything to me!\"","Auntie Wei: \"............\"","Seeing that, Auntie Wei could not very well say anything more.","There were not many pedestrians on the road to begin with. A few people were drawn over by the slogan \"Refreshingly cool, lifting your spirits\", but the moment they saw the price tag of thirty copper coins, they all shook their heads and walked away. By then, Auntie Wei's pancake shop had already sold more than a dozen servings, and Sprite still had not made a single sale.","But when something is new and novel, there are always people willing to give it a try.","A wandering cultivation traveler carrying a long sword on his back walked over, raising an eyebrow when he saw the word \"Sprite\" on the sign. Then he caught sight of the price and burst out laughing. \"This Sprite of yours, is the 'snow' part made of gold, or is the 'green' part made of gold?\"","For some reason, Wu Guanyue lit up with delight when she heard that line, and said very earnestly, \"You think it's too expensive? I think it's too cheap! This is all greenhouse-grown Sprite!\"","The wandering cultivator: \"............?\"","The wandering cultivator: \"Fine... give me a bowl. But let's get one thing straight first: if it doesn't cool me down and chase the heat away, I'm not paying!\"","This wandering cultivator had a fire-aligned spiritual root. Every summer, the dan fire in his body would be stirred up by the scorching yang qi of the sun, leaving him feeling unbearably uncomfortable on the hottest days. At the peak of summer, he had to recite the Mental Calming Formula a hundred times every day just to get by, which was why he was willing to pay thirty copper coins to give this Sprite a shot.","That said, he did not have high expectations at all. His comment about not paying if it did not work was just a casual remark. Cultivators who studied the laws of the universe and sought the path of enlightenment would never pick on ordinary common folk.","As he was thinking that, the young shop owner handed him his serving of Sprite.","The wandering cultivator looked down and saw a clear, spring-like drink in the clay bowl. It was not the pink hue of perilla peach drink, nor the hazy yellow of wild apricot drink. It had no color at all, but it held a marvelous quirk: countless tiny bubbles were rising from the bottom of the bowl to the surface, popping the moment they reached the air, and releasing a fresh, inviting aroma that had been trapped inside them.","This wandering cultivator had traveled far and wide across many lands, but he had never seen anything like this in his life!","He did not even step away from the inn entrance, tilting his head back and downing the whole bowl in one go.","The second the drink touched his tongue, his expression shifted instantly.","The fine, fizzing bubbles burst across his tongue, sending that fragrant, crisp, refreshing aroma flooding his entire mouth in an instant. It was a little like the bright scent of citrus, but far more crisp and pleasant; a little like fresh, unfermented wine, but with a far more lively, invigorating kick.","Even more wondrously, the moment he swallowed the Sprite, the restless dan fire in his spiritual mansion was soothed immediately.","This Sprite had rare, heavenly spiritual herbs mixed into it!","And it was only selling for thirty copper coins? The wandering cultivator could barely believe his eyes.","Heavenly spiritual herbs earned their name for a reason, after all—they were incredibly difficult to come by. Take the Frost Lotus Seed Sweet Soup at the Yue Lai Inn for example. It used frost lotus flowers from the icy Ice Fiend Secret Realm, a place no ordinary person could ever enter. You had to hire cultivators to venture in and harvest them, so of course the cost was sky-high.","The wandering cultivator's guess was right on the mark. The evergreen pine trees grew in the mist-shrouded red pine forests, carrying a natural frosty chill in their very fibers. Fresh pine needles were not even the coolest part—once the long-burning pine resin was lit, the cool feeling it gave off was simply heavenly.","But for Wu Guanyue, cost was never something she needed to worry about.","After all, she was playing a xianxia game. If she did not go out to hunt monsters, that would be unjust! If she did not sell dishes and drinks made with fantastical in-game ingredients, that would be against all rules!","There's no way that's allowed! No way at all! Absolutely no way!","As for the price? It was a reference price calculated by the game system based on her inn's popularity and wealth stats. Wu Guanyue thought it worked perfectly well.","This was a win-win situation. The burly wandering cultivator had barely finished his first bowl before he was leaning forward eagerly. \"Give me three more!\"","He immediately fished a silver coin out of his money pouch.","He chugged down three more bowls of Sprite in big, hearty gulps, and only then let out a long, contented sigh, looking like he had reached peak bliss.","It was wonderful, absolutely wonderful. After drinking it, all the summer heat was swept away, and he felt nothing but cool, sparkling refreshment.","And it only cost thirty copper coins a bowl! That was almost impossible to wrap his head around.","The wandering cultivator could not help but ask, \"Shopkeeper, why are you doing this?\"","This Sprite must have used heavenly spiritual herbs even more precious than the frost lotus, yet this young shopkeeper was practically giving it away for next to nothing.","Wu Guanyue: \"?\"","What did that mean? An NPC had just asked her a question that made no sense at all.","She thought for a moment, then answered perfectly matter-of-factly, \"Because everyone needs me!\"","This was a game, after all. The player was the center of the whole world! Even if her in-game setting was just a simple innkeeper, all the NPCs would come to her for help whenever they ran into trouble!","I wonder if there will be a plot where the innkeeper saves the world, ahahaha.","The thought brought a perfectly natural smile to Wu Guanyue's face.","But hearing those words, the wandering cultivator's eyes suddenly went wide.","In this incredibly plain sentence lay such broad-mindedness, such open-minded ease, and such generous, selfless compassion!","This had nothing to do with cultivation level. Anyone who could say something like that was already far nobler than the vast majority of people in the world, as far as this innkeeper was concerned!","The wandering cultivator, Lu Datong, suddenly cupped his fists and bowed deeply, his voice thick with emotion. \"I, Lu Datong, am truly filled with admiration! The innkeeper's great righteousness is beyond praise!\"","At this sight, not to mention Auntie Wei, even several wandering cultivators sitting in other shops could not help but stare wide-eyed.","You have to understand, Lu Datong was a proud, unruly character. The only people he had ever genuinely admired in his life were Wenren Ying, the Meishan's Number One Blade, and no one else. Now he was being so respectful and deferential to a mere innkeeper!","All just because he had drunk that \"Sprite\".","Could this Sprite really have some supernatural quality? Could it really be mixed with some rare heavenly spirit treasure?","Several of the cultivators could not help but wonder that.","After bowing to Wu Guanyue, Lu Datong filled three more bowls of Sprite into his wine gourd and strode away. The other wandering cultivators exchanged glances, and all saw the same thought in each other's eyes — we might as well give it a try!","Thirty copper coins was not the same as two taels of profound silver, after all. They could easily afford that.","And so that day, these poor wandering cultivators who could not afford Calming Heart Pills or Emerald Broth finally got relief from their inner restlessness. They spent the most refreshing, pleasant day of the entire summer, and set off for the secret realm with such clear, energetic spirits that who knew what lucky opportunities they might stumble upon!","And of course, these people all had their own close companions, whom they would eagerly recommend the inn to once they met. We will leave that part of the story aside for now.","Speaking of Lu Datong, the three bowls of Sprite he had filled in his wine gourd were not for himself to drink — he was bringing them to Brother Wenren.","Brother Wenren was Wenren Ying, and Wenren Ying was Meishan's Number One Blade.","At that moment, Wenren Ying was walking alone in the Bingyi Secret Realm.","He was a tall, broad-shouldered man carrying a long blade on his back. The blade had no scabbard, only wrapped haphazardly in a piece of cloth. He wore a wide-brimmed hat pulled low over his face, so no one could see his eyes. All you could make out was the faint stubble on his jaw, which made him look a little down on his luck, a little wild and unconstrained.","The icy wind, sharp with shards of frozen crystal, blew against him, flapping his rough cloak.","Wenren Ying suddenly stopped in his tracks, and said in a lazy, unhurried tone, \"You can come out now.\"","From the rime-covered pine forest behind him, a man stepped out in long strides. He was clad in a fiery fire rat fur coat, and the killing intent in his eyes burned hotter than the flames stitched onto his garment.","\"Are you Wenren Ying?\"","\"I am.\"","\"Good. Draw your blade!\"","\"Why should I?\"","\"I heard you're a good-for-nothing with a shattered spirit mansion, yet you still call yourself Meishan's Number One Blade. I've been dying to test your skills!\"","Wenren Ying could not help but let out a helpless laugh at those words.","But the man had already roared and channeled his full power!","The north wind howled. The ground trembled. Snow piled feet high shot up into the air, and beneath the swirling, flying frost, a stone wall formation three full feet thick snapped shut around Wenren Ying, trapping him inside.","Wenren Ying stood perfectly still within the stone wall formation, not a single muscle tensed.","Wenren Ying's spirit mansion was shattered to begin with — he could not even use fire-aligned spells. Even if he could, the man lying in wait for him was an earth-aligned spiritual root, and in the five elements cycle, fire could not overcome earth.","The advantage is all mine! The earth-aligned cultivator thought smugly, and could not resist wasting a few more words.","\"You're as good as dead. I'll do you a favor and leave you a piece of advice — in your next life, mind your own business!\"","The second his words ended, all he saw was a flash of white light!","The earth-aligned cultivator heard a low hum in his ears, and the blade light was already slicing through the air towards him.","In the next instant, Wenren Ying was standing right in front of him. He looked down at the man, and said in a calm, indifferent voice, \"I'll leave you a piece of advice too...\"","A thin line of blood slowly appeared across the earth-aligned cultivator's throat.","The last thing he heard in his life was Wenren Ying's cold, flat voice —","\"You'd be better off dead.\"","Blood spurted high into the air, sending the cultivator's head flying three full yards above the ground.","But far more scarlet and brutal than the gushing blood were Wenren Ying's eyes, hidden beneath the shadow of his hat brim.","No human could ever have eyes like that."]},{"number":9,"title":"Chapter 9","paragraphs":["Wenren Ying returned from the secret realm at dusk. After entering the city, he did not head toward the bustling main street, but went straight back to the small courtyard he rented in the western part of town.","From a long way off, Lu Datong’s rough, hearty voice could already be heard.","“Brother Wenren! Brother Wenren, what have you been busy with today? I’ve been waiting ages!”","Wenren Ying asked, “Do you need something?”","Lu Datong laughed and offered him a wine gourd. “Brother Wenren, I found something good today... Come on, give it a taste.”","Wenren Ying’s senses were far sharper than those of ordinary people. The moment the wine gourd was opened, he immediately felt a frosty chill wafting from it. He frowned and said bluntly, “I told you not to go to the trouble. Nothing in the city that can calm the mind is of any use to me.”","Wenren Ying’s spiritual mansion was shattered, and the spiritual energy in his dantian and qi sea was difficult to control. Yet he was unwilling to cripple his meridians just to obtain relief. Thus, the spiritual energy of heaven and earth still circulated through his meridians, while his damaged golden core relied on that energy to forcibly sustain its operation.","It was practically a miracle.","But only Wenren Ying knew how painful that miracle was. The golden core circulating within his ruined spiritual mansion leaked core fire. If others merely had to endure the dryness caused by core fire in summer, then he could practically be said to be suffering the punishment of being roasted alive on heated bronze.","Of course, he had tried various ways to ease the pain... but there was another problem: no matter how effective something was, using it every day would eventually render it useless.","Frostglory Lotus and Everfirm Ice had long since stopped working for him.","Who would have thought that Lu Datong would say, “This stuff is very particular! Ice-cold to the core, spirits soar! ‘Ice-cold to the core, spirits soar’—you know what I mean, Brother Wenren? Ah, whatever! You’ll understand once you try it!”","With that, he stamped his foot and forcefully shoved the wine gourd into Wenren Ying’s arms.","Wenren Ying: “...”","Wenren Ying was like a consumptive who had suffered from a chronic illness for years and tried every medicine there was. After hearing people praise some new remedy to the heavens, he was already completely numb to it.","He merely said, “Just leave it there. I’ll try it when I have time...”","Lu Datong immediately grew anxious. “Brother Wenren, just take one sip—only one sip! If it doesn’t work, come find me! You won’t even try it—is that because you don’t—”","In his haste, he nearly blurted out one of the crude lines he usually used to pressure people into drinking at banquets...","The commotion had already drawn the attention of several people in the alley, all of whom were looking their way.","Wenren Ying: “...”","How embarrassing.","“All right, all right, I’ll try it. Just stop tugging at my clothes.”","He tilted his head back and took a sip...","His expression suddenly froze.","This stuff...!","The flavor was certainly novel. When the bubbles burst across his tongue, they brought with them an indescribably refreshing sensation.","But to Wenren Ying, something else mattered far more—","This stuff actually worked!","The moment the Sprite entered his throat, it brought with it a frosty chill. His body had never experienced anything like it. Almost instantly, the restless muscles began to twitch involuntarily, while the surface of his magma-hot skin seemed to receive an enormous shock and erupted in gooseflesh.","His body was hotter than other people’s, so naturally, its reaction to this mind-soothing coldness was also more pronounced.","Sprite... Sprite...","This truly was a heavenly treasure he had never seen or used before!","He lowered the wine gourd and immediately asked, “Which shop did you buy this from?”","Lu Datong could not help laughing. “The shop is on Qihua Road. It’s run by an innkeeper with a heart for the greater good...”","Wenren Ying obtained a whole gourd of Sprite, and that night, he finally managed to sleep soundly.","The next day, he set out for Qihua Road to investigate the inn selling Sprite—and to meet the great expert who was supposedly saving all living beings.","He had visited Qihua Road before. It was an extremely desolate place; even the rats there were probably thinner than rats anywhere else.","Yet when he arrived that day, Qihua Road was unexpectedly bustling!","Two wandering cultivators were fighting!","“I got here first!”","“I clearly got here first!”","“The stuff belongs to me!”","“What an arrogant claim! You say it belongs to you, so it does? We’ll settle this with our fists!”","“Fine! Let’s do it!”","This sort of scene would have been perfectly appropriate in a secret realm. Every cultivator who came to Meishan had something they wanted to obtain. Once they encountered one another in the secret realm, who would willingly hand it over? Even if it meant fighting to the death, they would fight first and worry about the consequences later!","But this was Qihua Road...","...What exactly were they fighting over? Could it be rats even thinner than those elsewhere?","With both hands folded over his saber, Wenren Ying leaned lazily against the mouth of an alley and watched the commotion.","The two wandering cultivators were poised on the verge of drawing blood. They were just about to start fighting when a young girl with two braids suddenly ran out of the neighboring inn. With righteous conviction, she declared, “No fighting! No fighting! What are the benefits of Sprite? Whoever gives the best answer gets some!”","(*)","Wenren Ying: “...”","Wenren Ying: “...?”","The two wandering cultivators immediately began shouting over each other.","One said, “One sip of Sprite and you’re cool to the core, refreshed and ready to explore secret realms!”","The other said, “Sprite down the throat, spiritual meridians flow; core fire vanishes, and the spirit platform clears!”","One hurriedly added, “I’ve had a fiery constitution since I was little. How could I possibly manage without Sprite?”","The other declared, “I have a fire spiritual root. Without Sprite, how could I survive the summer?”","The adorable and lively girl nodded sagely. “They’re both very reasonable. The shop made plenty of Sprite today, so you can each have a share!”","She then handed each of them a bowl. The two men smiled, letting bygones be bygones. They laughed, clinked their bowls together, and drank their Sprite, while the girl stood to one side with a satisfied smile.","Wenren Ying: “...”","Seeing the two cultivators fight so fiercely over a drink of Sprite, the passersby could not help becoming curious. They all came over to buy a bowl as well.","The girl once again called out with the solemn air of an old shopkeeper, “Don’t push! Don’t push! Everyone gets some Sprite!”","Wenren Ying: “...”","Wenren Ying was fairly certain he had never been rendered this speechless in his entire life.","So this was the... great expert Lu Datong had mentioned?","He stood in the corner with his arms around his saber for a while, then suddenly let out a laugh. After that, he strode forward and joined the queue in front of the inn.","He was certainly curious about what heavenly treasure Sprite was made from, but he was not so shameless as to snatch someone else’s secret recipe. Besides, as good as Sprite was, it would probably only work for him this summer. Why pry into the secret? He could simply buy it.","Wenren Ying was a famous figure on Meishan. Wherever he appeared, there were always people who recognized him.","“That’s... Wenren Ying?”","“What’s that kid doing here?”","Two cultivators who happened to be passing by whispered to each other.","Wenren Ying suddenly turned around and flashed them a smile, revealing two rows of dazzlingly white teeth.","“Having some Sprite!”","“...”","“...”","The two cultivators said nothing at all and ran away as fast as they could.","Still, word of Wenren Ying drinking Sprite on Qihua Road quickly spread throughout the city. As a result, Wu Guanyue discovered that the number of customers had risen yet another level that day—and so had her popularity points!","Sure enough, advertising was incredibly effective!","Once again, I’m in awe of the game’s freedom! Once again, I’m in awe of the power of real-time AI computation!","And the game’s management system is genuinely a lot of fun!","It feels just like playing “O Fang’s Night Sparrow Diner”—you have to be quick-eyed and quick-fingered, combining all kinds of dishes and drinks, then serving each customer the perfect pairing before their patience runs out. It gives you this wonderfully relaxing, mind-emptying sort of experience...","It’s utterly addictive! I can’t stop!","After several days of happily grinding away in this relaxed atmosphere, Wu Guanyue’s inn finally leveled up!","【Inn Details】","【Name: Ah Ah Ah Oh Oh Oh Uh Uh Uh Let Me See What This Game’s Longest Name Is, I Need to Pad It Out, Pad It Out, Pad It Out, As If the Emperor Himself Had Arrived—Inn】","【Inn Level: LV.2 (You now have a small handful of regulars)】","【Inn Popularity: 105\\1,000 (Everyone traveling along Flagflower Road has heard of your inn)】","【Inn Revenue: 13,000\\100,000 (Although it looks like a lot, these are only copper coins)】","【Owner Details】","【Owner: Wu Guanyue】","【Level: LV.2 (Your strength and the inn’s fate are inseparably linked)】","【Acquired: [Skill Proficiency · Rapid Food Delivery]!】","【Rapid Food Delivery: You no longer need to leave the serving station. With a single “whoosh,” you can toss a dish directly toward the customer, sending it along a perfect arc right to their table!】","【Acquired: [Skill Proficiency · Rapid Fertilization]!】","【Rapid Fertilization: Once your fertilizer enters the soil, it takes effect immediately, eliminating the need to wait and shortening the time until harvest. However, take note: if the fertilizer has not been fermented beforehand, it will trigger the [Root Burn] effect, damaging the plants!】","【Unlocked: Building Mode!】","【Building Mode: You can now renovate your inn more conveniently. With a single thought, you can activate it. Everything inside the inn is now yours to command!】","Yay!","(*) The Jinkela ad slogan is here. From now on, I won’t write out the inn’s full name every time. If I keep doing that, I really will just be padding the word count."]},{"number":10,"title":"Chapter 10","paragraphs":["***","In simulation and management games, building and decorating are indispensable elements. Full-dive games are no exception. But surely a full-dive game wouldn’t make players actually plaster walls and apply putty, right? That’s exactly what Building Mode is for: letting players decorate to their heart’s content!","There’s no need to do anything by hand. Just activate Building Mode, and you can freely change the inn’s decorations, furnishings, and facilities through the control panel!","Combining the twenty taels of silver Wang Er had given her earlier, Wu Guanyue now had thirty-three taels in hand. She took out thirty of them and went to the carpenter on Qihua Road to order six wooden tables, twenty-four benches, and five wooden beds. This would increase the maximum number of diners the inn could accommodate, while also furnishing the guest rooms a little.","However, the guest rooms still needed [Wooden Cabinets], [Tables], and [Chairs] before they could meet the minimum requirements for opening. She was still short quite a bit of money—and had plenty of grinding left to do...","First, she had to get the food business up and running!","As for the other two new abilities, Quick Delivery was certainly convenient. As for Rapid Fertilization and Composting Root Burn... Well, considering that the BOSS she was about to face was a tree demon, that skill seemed like it might be very useful.","Wu Guanyue leaned over the counter with her chin in her hands, deep in thought.","It was already late, and the inn was about to close for the night. Only two tables of guests remained. Wuyun was running back and forth across the main hall, sweeping up dust with its tail and belly (?) while occasionally letting out smug little meows.","Wang Er was still huffing and puffing away at his chores. To save money, Wu Guanyue hadn’t bought [Flour]. Instead, she had bought [New Wheat] and made Wang Er grind it in the back courtyard...","He really had become a donkey now!","Wenren Ying walked in from outside and said casually, “Good evening, Little Shopkeeper Wu!”","The moment Wu Guanyue saw Wenren Ying, her eyes lit up.","“Ah!”","A special guest with a star rating over his head!","Of course, not all guests were created equal. The longer a star-rated guest stayed at the inn and the better their reviews, the more positive bonuses they brought to the establishment. Wu Guanyue still remembered that on the second day after she started selling Sprite, Wenren Ying had been the very reason the inn’s popularity had suddenly shot up.","Therefore, maintaining good relationships with star-rated guests was absolutely the correct way to play the game!","Wu Guanyue suddenly pulled a cinquefoil from her sleeve.","Cinquefoils were common wildflowers in Meishan during the summer. They could be gathered in large quantities in the wilderness, and their function was similar to daffodils in Stardew Valley: they could be given to NPCs to raise their affection.","【[Wu Guanyue] gave [Cinquefoil] to [Wenren Ying]. May your friendship last forever!】","Wenren Ying: “............?”","Huh? Why wasn’t he accepting it? Did he not like it?","【[Wu Guanyue] gave [Salt-Baked Matsutake] to [Wenren Ying]. May your friendship last forever!】","Wenren Ying: “............?”","He rejected it again?","Wu Guanyue immediately forgot about the side quest she had originally been working on and began taking all sorts of things out of her inventory to give him, trying to figure out what kinds of gifts Wenren Ying liked.","Thus, Wenren Ying watched as the shopkeeper in front of him tilted her head, her twin ponytails swishing from side to side, then started pulling various objects out of her storage pouch in an attempt to give them to him...","And the more he refused, the more tightly her brows furrowed. The speed at which she swapped out the gifts also grew faster and faster.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","A huge cold-sweat bubble appeared over Wenren Ying’s head.","Seeing that she was about to try giving him every single item she owned, Wenren Ying hurriedly accepted the object she was currently attempting to hand over.","“Thank you, thank you. I like it very much.”","The entire inn fell silent.","Several wandering cultivators sitting in the corner stared at him in astonishment. The owner of the neighboring pancake shop, who had been leaning against the counter, wore an equally incredulous expression. Even Wu Guanyue was frozen in place, her mouth as round as her eyes.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Very, very slowly, Wenren Ying turned his head to look at the plate in his hands.","...Intestine sashimi.","Wenren Ying: “..................”","By then, Little Shopkeeper Wu had already dashed to the counter with astonishing speed. She opened her business log and began scribbling furiously.","“Wenren Ying... likes... intestine sashimi...”","Wenren Ying: “...Hey, don’t write everything down in that lousy notebook of yours.”","In any case, Wu Guanyue had successfully obtained some vital information. Hooray!","She calmly put away her business log, filled a bowl with Sprite for Wenren Ying, and activated her new skill, [Quick Delivery]!","There was a sudden “whoosh,” and the bowl of Sprite landed in front of Wenren Ying without spilling a single drop!","“Nice!”","Lu Datong, sitting nearby, shouted his approval.","“Excellent! Absolutely excellent! Shopkeeper, your aim and control are truly remarkable. That was an eye-opener! Brother Wenren, why don’t you show the shopkeeper how it’s done?”","“Show us! Show us!”","The other guests began cheering him on.","Wenren Ying seemed a little helpless, but he disliked ruining other people’s fun. He suddenly tipped his head back and drained the Sprite in one gulp. Then he flicked his hand, and with another “whoosh,” the empty bowl landed on Wuyun’s head.","Wuyun, now balancing a stack of bowls on its head, let out a serious series of meows and scampered toward the back courtyard—where Nuclear-Powered Donkey Wang Er was washing dishes...","“Wuyun can do it too! Wuyun can do it too!”","The other guests started cheering again.","Wow! What a great atmosphere!","Wu Guanyue was delighted. She kept using Quick Delivery without pause. Soon, the sounds of “whoosh, whoosh, whoosh” and “nice, nice, nice” rang out nonstop, while plates and bowls flew through the air above the inn.","After a while, Wuyun returned with another pile of dirty dishes on its head, meowing in confusion.","Wu Guanyue: “?”","Wu Guanyue followed Wuyun to the back courtyard and took a look.","There was no one there.","Only a huge pile of empty bowls remained. Wang Er, who had still been sitting there and huffing away as he washed dishes half an hour earlier, had somehow vanished!","Wu Guanyue was shocked.","Her Nuclear-Powered Donkey!!!","At the same time, her quest panel updated!","【Quest · Side Quest: The Missing Employee (NEW!)】","【Quest Details: Your employee, Wang Er, has suddenly disappeared... Ask the people nearby if they saw him!】","This was the first side quest in the game!","She had no idea whether the rewards would be generous... Regardless, she had to get moving!","“Hello, my employee Wang Er suddenly disappeared. Did you happen to see him just now?”","Wu Guanyue ran to the front of the inn and asked the guests who had been inside.","【Wenren Ying (frowning): “Your employee has gone missing? I’ll take a look.”】","The tall NPC rose to his feet and headed toward the back courtyard. After a while, he returned.","【Wenren Ying (thoughtful): “There weren’t any traces left behind... It feels like he followed someone of his own accord. Little Shopkeeper Wu, did anything happen here?”】","【Would you like to tell him about the Yongfeng Bank incident?】","Of course she chose yes.","Wu Guanyue: “Mumble mumble, mumble mumble.”","【Wenren Ying: “I see. So Wang Er was taken away by Qian Shi'an... Qian Shi'an seems to have a monster for a master. Since he took Wang Er away, Wang Er is probably in grave danger. He deceived you before—are you looking for him?”】","Of course she was!","This was the player's side quest!","With her hopes pinned on the quest reward, Wu Guanyue put on a stern expression and said to Wenren Ying, “Regardless, this concerns a human life. Whether he’s alive or dead, we need an answer!”","Wenren Ying paused.","He couldn’t help glancing at Wu Guanyue. The young innkeeper’s expression was utterly serious, and her glasslike eyes were so clear, filled with genuine concern for Wang Er’s life.","Wenren Ying couldn’t help admiring her inwardly.","As expected of Shopkeeper Wu—she truly was a person of honor and righteousness!","In all his life, he had admired righteous people most of all!","He said, “Very well. I’ll make inquiries on your behalf. Since I’ve taken this matter on, there’s no way I won’t be able to find him.”","Shopkeeper Wu’s eyes immediately lit up again... and then she stuffed another plate of large-intestine sashimi into Wenren Ying’s hands!","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","Righteousness aside, was there perhaps something slightly... er... wrong with the way she thought?","Here it comes. Even the male lead can’t escape being victimized."]},{"number":11,"title":"Chapter 11","paragraphs":["Where, exactly, had Wang Er gone?","Wenren Ying’s guess had been correct. It was Qian Shi’an who had taken him away.","That day, after spending quite some time making calculations, Qian Shi’an had finally managed to determine Wu Guanyue’s origins through the layers of obscuring mist. He then instructed Wang Er to trick Wu Guanyue into going to Red Pine Forest, where he intended to have his master’s disciple’s disciple, the Living Pine Tree, deal with her.","But who could have imagined that Wu Guanyue would actually return safe and sound?!","If she had returned safe and sound, then naturally the Living Pine Tree could not possibly still be alive!","By all rights, the moment she came face-to-face with the Living Pine Tree, there should have been no chance of her surviving. Could it be that cockroaches really did have a far more tenacious vitality than other insects?!","What was more, Wang Er had betrayed him, and Wu Guanyue now knew the whole truth!","Qian Shi’an was instantly drenched in sweat... Faced with such a formidable insect demon, there was nothing he could do. All he could do was scramble up the mountain and beg his master, Daoist Master Songfeng, to intervene!","Daoist Master Songfeng was a monster with a habit of eating people. Naturally, Qian Shi’an could not go to him empty-handed. Resenting Wang Er for betraying him, he relied on his miraculous concealment technique to steal Wang Er away from Wu Guanyue’s inn!","At that moment, in a secret grotto-heaven on Mount Huiming, an old Daoist was sitting in meditation with all five points of contact raised toward Heaven.","The old Daoist wore simple robes and looked vigorous and sharp-eyed. Every strand of his hair had turned silver-white, yet his back was as straight as a pine tree. A horsetail whisk rested in his hand.","Qian Shi’an’s voice came from outside the cave.","“Master, your disciple has come to visit!”","The old Daoist was none other than Daoist Master Songfeng.","Daoist Master Songfeng kept his eyes closed, his breathing long and even.","Only after a long while did he slowly say, “Come in.”","Qian Shi’an immediately entered, knelt down, and respectfully knocked his head against the floor three times.","Daoist Master Songfeng said slowly, “Go on, then. What trouble have you gotten yourself into this time?”","Qian Shi’an’s eyes filled with tears. “Master! Your disciple has been wronged!”","He then poured out the whole story of Wu Guanyue to Daoist Master Songfeng, item by item, like beans spilling from a sack.","Qian Shi’an said, “That Wu Guanyue refused to repay her debt. When my men went to collect it, she actually humiliated them in public!”","Daoist Master Songfeng sighed. “Why can people under Heaven never let go of wealth and possessions—of these worldly things?”","Qian Shi’an continued, “That Wu Guanyue is cruel and ruthless. Her shop assistant was a witness to the loan her grandfather took, yet she actually wanted to beat him to death over it!”","Daoist Master Songfeng sighed. “Why do people under Heaven never understand the principle that those who share the same roots should not turn their blades against each other?”","Qian Shi’an said, “That Wu Guanyue, relying on her own abilities, even charged into Red Pine Forest and killed the Living Pine Tree!”","Daoist Master Songfeng sighed. “Why do people under Heaven always... Hmm?! Who did you say she killed?!”","Qian Shi’an replied, “The Living Pine Tree! Ah, if only you had seen the scene when I arrived...”","Daoist Master Songfeng leaped up from his meditation cushion like a monkey whose tail had been stepped on and began cursing furiously.","“How dare that little wretch?! What is she, to think she could kill my disciple’s disciple? Does she think I, Old Pine, don’t exist?!”","After cursing for quite some time, Daoist Master Songfeng finally asked, “What is Wu Guanyue’s origin? What is her background?”","Qian Shi’an hurriedly replied, “She claimed to be from the Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect. As for her origins, she said she was the Handsome Cockroach Who Flies and Burrows. I made a divination, and I believe she is an insect demon.”","Daoist Master Songfeng snorted. “What Wind Spirit Moon Shadow Sect? There is no such sect anywhere in the entire Divine Firmament Prefecture! And an insect demon is even less likely. Any insect that encountered my grand-disciple would have no choice but to beg for death! You’re still a child and were fooled by her, but this old Daoist is not senile!”","Qian Shi’an nodded so vigorously that his head nearly fell off. “Your instruction is absolutely correct, Master. Your instruction is absolutely correct. This disciple was foolish and was deceived by that Wu Guanyue.”","Daoist Master Songfeng paid him no further attention and immediately began making calculations with his fingers...","But as he continued, his brows gradually knitted together.","Because he could not calculate anything either.","After a moment of contemplation, he asked, “Did that girl say anything else?”","Qian Shi’an frowned as he thought. “In answer to your question, Master, she did mention another name that I couldn’t understand at the time. It sounded like... Coca-Loca.”","Daoist Master Songfeng mused, “Coca-Loca...”","Qian Shi’an said, “Thinking back on it now... the first name Wu Guanyue gave was Coca-Loca. Only afterward did she hurriedly change her answer.”","Daoist Master Songfeng nodded. “Yes, yes... She must have let the truth slip at first, then hastily made up some nonsense to cover it up... Let me calculate it!”","With that, he began working out the divination once more.","Qian Shi’an held his breath and focused his attention. He could feel the Daoist energy surging around Daoist Master Songfeng, profound and wondrous beyond compare. Even if he studied for another hundred years, he would never grasp the essence of such divination skills.","“Ha!”","Daoist Master Songfeng suddenly let out a thunderous shout!","Qian Shi’an hurriedly looked over, only to see Daoist Master Songfeng with his hair standing on end, his rage soaring, his fury blazing, and his eyes glaring murderously... For some reason, his face even seemed to have turned an eerie red.","“You filthy bastard! You son of a turtle! You damned mongrel! How dare you toy with me... Take that!”","Daoist Master Songfeng was so furious that he struck out with one palm, sending the heavy hibiscus-frozen-stone table in front of him flying. With a loud bang, the stone table shot out of the grotto-heaven and directly crushed the bound Wang Er outside into Wang Er paste.","Daoist Master Songfeng, meanwhile, stormed away in a fury.","Qian Shi’an stood there dumbfounded, unable to recover for quite some time.","What... exactly was this “Coca-Loca”? How could it have enraged Daoist Master Songfeng so thoroughly?","Wang Er’s life had ended in such an inexplicable fashion, but in the end, it was the result of his own actions.","Wu Guanyue, naturally, knew nothing about what had happened in the shadows. She was still diligently carrying out her side quest—belike, asking every person she met whether they had seen her shop assistant...","That was because the side quest’s description still read: “Ask around and see.”","Wu Guanyue: Serious.jpg","Wu Guanyue: Earnest.jpg","That evening, when the inn was nearly ready to close for the night, a Daoist wearing robes and carrying a horsetail whisk suddenly walked in.","This Daoist was, of course, Daoist Master Songfeng.","After being driven into a fit of rage by that “Coca-Loca,” cursing furiously and swearing to teach Wu Guanyue a lesson, Daoist Master Songfeng had lost no time in coming to find her.","When he arrived at Flag Blossom Road, he saw a worn blue-stone path with a few scattered pedestrians walking along it. Several small shops stood on either side of the road, one of which was... that whatever-it-was inn.","Daoist Master Songfeng approached the entrance. Inside, the place was small and plain, with only six or seven elmwood tables. A handful of guests sat scattered around them—but they were all people of low cultivation, not worth a second glance from Daoist Master Songfeng.","Then he saw a young woman standing behind the counter. Her hair was tied into two high ponytails, and she was supporting her cheeks with both hands, wearing a vacant expression as though she were lost in thought.","Her cultivation... was actually nonexistent!","A mortal?","No, impossible. A mortal could never have killed the Living Pine Tree.","Very well. He would personally meet her and see what she was made of!","Daoist Master Songfeng snorted, swept aside his Daoist robe, and strode through the door.","Wu Guanyue heard the commotion and looked up—then immediately widened her eyes!","A... a star-rated guest!","Aside from Wenren Ying, the inn had finally welcomed its second star-rated guest... and he was also a three-star guest. Clearly, he was someone Wu Guanyue ought to treat with great enthusiasm!","Wu Guanyue immediately dashed over to the star-rated guest, came to a sudden stop, and stood up straight with impeccable poise!","Then, as usual, it was time to give him a round of gifts to raise his favorability!","Wu Guanyue began rummaging around in her sleeve—","【[Wu Guanyue] gifted [Salt-Baked Matsutake] to [???]. May your friendship last forever!】","【[???]: “............?”】","The star-rated guest did not accept it. Instead, a long string of ellipses and question marks appeared above his head.","But that was fine. Through interacting with Wenren Ying, the player had already become very familiar with this process, so she calmly continued trying different gifts.","【[Wu Guanyue] gifted [Stir-Fried Pine Nuts] to [???]. May your friendship last forever!】","【[???]: “............!!!”】","【[Wu Guanyue] gifted [Pine Frost Candy] to [???]. May your friendship last forever!】","【[Wu Guanyue] gifted [Pine Blossom Cakes] to [???]. May your friendship last forever!】","【[Wu Guanyue] gifted [Ever-Burning Pine Resin] to [???]. May your friendship last forever!】","Daoist Master Songfeng could only watch as Wu Guanyue rapidly cycled through the items in her hands, displaying each and every part of his disciples’ and grand-disciples’ corpses to him one by one...","Damn it! She was deliberately provoking him!","No"]},{"number":12,"title":"Chapter 12","paragraphs":["Bravo! Bravo! This is absolutely preposterous!","This audacious little bastard not only beat his disciples and grand-disciples to death, but even went so far as to suck the living pine tree dry and wipe it clean!","Daoist Master Songfeng was absolutely seething with rage!","So from Wu Guanyue's point of view, all she saw was this star-rated guest's head, after spitting out strings of ellipses, question marks and exclamation marks one after another, starting to pop up a whole line of cross-shaped anger icons!","Huh! He's actually mad!","Who would have thought gifting things could trigger a rage response... This had to be a brand new game mechanic. The ever observant and summary-minded Wu Guanyue immediately sprinted back to the counter at a hundred-meter dash and started scribbling furiously in her business log.","\"Gifting... too many... hated gifts... makes guests angry...\"","But that was exactly the same way she had tried gifting things to Wenren Ying the other day... He had kept refusing the whole time, but never once got mad.","Wu Guanyue kept writing: \"Wenren Ying... nice... the white-bearded Daoist... mean...\"","White-bearded Daoist Songfeng: \"............\"","Daoist Master Songfeng's fury was practically burning right over the top of his head! He had always had a fiery, explosive temper. If he could swallow this provocation from Wu Guanyue, he'd be willing to write his own name backwards!","Daoist Master Songfeng bounded to his feet in one leap. Mid-air, he shot toward Wu Guanyue like a flash of lightning. His movements were so swift, his body technique so fast, that a faint afterimage lingered where he had just been standing, and none of the loose cultivators sitting in the corner even realized anything was amiss!","WHEEE——!","A strange whistling sound of a flying object suddenly rang out over the inn!","[Wu Guanyue] has used the skill [Quick Food Delivery]!","Since he doesn't like pine-related items, maybe I should try some other dishes... Wait where did the guest go?!","A plate spun straight toward Daoist Master Songfeng.","Daoist Master Songfeng wasn't just all hot temper, either. His Daoist title \"Songfeng\" literally means \"the strength of green pine, the swiftness of a gale\", a testament to how unbelievably fast his movement skills were.","Yet Wu Guanyue didn't even lift her head. With a casual flick of her wrist, she intercepted him dead in his tracks.","\"Whoa — that's the spirit!\"","Daoist Master Songfeng's fighting spirit was roused instead. He let out a wild yell, shot his hand out from under his Daoist robe, and precisely clamped down on that plate whipping through the air.","Squelch!","His fingers sank right into something soft. A faint, distinct scent drifted up to Daoist Master Songfeng's nose.","Slowly, so very slowly, he looked down at what he had just grabbed.","... Raw large intestine sashimi.","Daoist Master Songfeng: \"............\"","Daoist Master Songfeng: \"..................\"","A giant cross-shaped anger icon popped up right over Daoist Master Songfeng's head.","Wu Guanyue: \"?\"","A giant question mark bubble popped up over Wu Guanyue's head.","He accepted it, but still doesn't like it?","... Ugh, what a impossible-to-please NPC!","He looked like such a kindly white-bearded old man at first, but who knew he had such a weird, cranky temper!","Wu Guanyue's own fighting spirit was stoked too — in for a penny, in for a pound. She'd already gone this far, she was determined to figure out what gifts he liked today. His favorability was already at zero, there was nowhere to go but up, this was the perfect time to go all out!","Wu Guanyue: (╬◣ω◢)","Wu Guanyue's eyes suddenly sharpened.","WHEEE——!","With one arm around the wooden crate, she twisted her wrist and sent another plate flying.","[Wu Guanyue] has used the skill [Quick Food Delivery], and gave [Wild Mountain Apricot] to [???]!","WHEEE WHEEE WHEEE——!","[Wu Guanyue] has used the skill [Quick Food Delivery], and gave [Grilled Crucian Carp] to [???]!","[Wu Guanyue] has used the skill [Quick Food Delivery], and gave [Green Plum Syrup] to [???]!","[Wu Guanyue] has used the skill [Quick Food Delivery], and gave [Toasted Pancake Strips] to [???]!","The sound of flying plates being tossed rang out nonstop through the inn. Over that oddly catchy whirring noise, another sharp wind cut through the air — it was Daoist Master Songfeng, darting back and forth across the inn at top speed!","He was leaping around so fast that afterimages of him lingered everywhere in the room, dazzling all onlookers and leaving them gasping in awe!","But no matter how agile his footwork, no matter how tricky the angles he took, Wu Guanyue's plates kept haunting him like vengeful ghosts!","She didn't even look, didn't even aim. She just kept throwing, and every single plate landed perfectly right in the path he was about to take.","Since when did a character this skilled pop up in Meishan? How come he had never heard of her?!","Daoist Master Songfeng's eyes were bloodshot by now!","After what felt like ages, the two finally came to a stop — the reason being that Wu Guanyue had run out of every single item she had to test.","Wu Guanyue stood behind the counter, looking on at Daoist Master Songfeng with a calm, impassive expression.","Daoist Master Songfeng was huffing and puffing, the fingers of his hand still sticky with... uh, the undigested bits from that raw large intestine sashimi.","Ugh... this feels like it's burning my roots!","Daoist Master Songfeng's face was stony with rage, as he glowered at Wu Guanyue.","\"Bravo!\" Lu Datong, who was sitting in the corner, suddenly cheered at the top of his lungs.","\"Bravo! Bravo!\"","The rest of the guests joined in the cheers, clapping their hands wildly.","After all, Shopkeeper Wu flying plates of food across the inn to guests had long become a beloved signature sight of the place. On a normal day, when guests were in a good mood, they'd play along and catch the flying plates for fun...","And just like that, the inn was filled once more with the cheerful, lively sound of everyone yelling \"bravo\"!","Daoist Master Songfeng: \"............\"","Daoist Master Songfeng: \"..................\"","Daoist Master Songfeng was furious!","These brainless, good-for-nothing slobs, did they think he was some street performer putting on a show for loose change?!","This was the final straw he could never tolerate!","Daoist Master Songfeng's face darkened. With a flick of his wide sleeve, he went to flip over the elm wood table right in front of him!","Earlier, Daoist Master Songfeng had flipped the stone table in his cave, crushing Wang Er flat into Wang Er paste... Now, in his towering rage, he was about to hurl that elm table straight at Lu Datong and bash him to death.","Lu Datong was far stronger than Wang Er, but against a great demon with Daoist Master Songfeng's profound cultivation, the difference was negligible. If that elm table smashed right into Lu Datong's body, his internal organs would be sent flying right out of his mouth.","And Lu Datong didn't have the faintest clue how much danger he was in!","At this critical, do-or-die moment where there was no possible way to dodge, a game system notification suddenly rang in Wu Guanyue's ear —","[Your pre-set closing time has arrived. Would you like to close up the inn?]","Ah! It was already closing time!","The game had separate operating hours and after-hours periods. During operating hours, guests would come in one after another, and the player had to serve them. During after-hours, the player needed to clean up the inn, go out to forage for ingredients, and cook new dishes, among other things.","Wu Guanyue had failed her NPC gifting run, and she was feeling a little dejected. She really didn't want to look at that grumpy white-bearded Daoist for a while... Closing up the inn sounded perfect.","But one last step before closing —","Activate Build Mode!","This was a game bug that Wu Guanyue had discovered. Since he had to wipe down all the grimy tables and chairs after closing up shop... all he needed to do was activate build mode right before closing, one-tap collect all the furniture, then place them back out again, and they would be spotless instantly!","[Wu Guanyue has activated Build Mode!]","At that exact moment, the furious Daoist Master Songfeng's sweeping sleeve wind had already reached the elm wooden table right beside him!","The elm table did not budge an inch.","An extremely mysterious, ancient power instantly enveloped the entire inn, freezing every part of it in place at that very moment. Every bowl and chopstick, every table and chair, every single thing was now fully under the innkeeper's complete control.","The expression on Daoist Master Songfeng's face froze.","(*) Excerpt from Jin Yong's *The Smiling, Proud Wanderer*, explaining the Songfeng Sword Technique of the Qingcheng School."]},{"number":13,"title":"Chapter 13","paragraphs":["***","In that instant, something changed.","A moment ago, he had merely stepped into an ordinary little inn. But now, at this very moment, the place had been transformed completely!","It had become Wu Guanyue’s domain!","Once a cultivator reached a certain level, they could naturally reshape their surroundings. A cultivator with an earth spirit root could turn soil into walls or raise lofty buildings from flat ground in the blink of an eye. A cultivator with a water spirit root could turn a desert into a lake or transform parched land into a muddy swamp.","At even higher levels, they could do as they pleased to an even greater extent. For instance, water had flowed downhill since ancient times, yet a great master of water could make a waterfall flow upward.","Of course, no matter how powerful a cultivator was, they must never imagine that they could stand against the natural might of Heaven and Earth. Even the greatest masters could only act freely within a certain range.","That “certain range” was known as a domain.","“Within this domain, I am Heaven!”","Why were there scattered secret realms all across the Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands? Because those secret realms were domains left behind by great masters after they ascended. The largest secret realm near Meishan, the Bingyi Secret Realm, had been left behind by Fairy Gushe ten thousand years ago.","But a domain was something only an Earth Immortal could create. Could it be that Wu Guanyue was...?!","Daoist Master Songfeng sucked in a cold breath. He was practically breaking out in a cold sweat!","No... Wait. Calm down. Calm down, Songfeng. If Wu Guanyue were an Earth Immortal, why had she been fighting that good-for-nothing Qian Shi'an on equal terms?","Daoist Master Songfeng had no ordinary background. He was not some wild demon who had gained sentience deep in the mountains. His true form was a magical treasure known as the Seven-Treasure Pine. His former master had been Yan Chongyang, the Sword Lord Taibai and former sect master of the Xuantian Sect on Yuntai Peak!","His horizons were anything but narrow. He had seen more than a few Earth Immortal experts. Thus, after his momentary panic, he quickly regained his composure and carefully examined Wu Guanyue.","Wu Guanyue stood behind the counter, propping her head up with one hand as if she were daydreaming...","No matter how he looked at her, Daoist Master Songfeng could not detect the slightest trace of someone who had attained the Dao.","Instead, there was a faint... somewhat mysterious aura...","Somewhat mysterious...?","Somewhat... mysterious...","That trace of mystery leaking from Wu Guanyue suddenly felt familiar to Daoist Master Songfeng. With one hand hidden beneath his voluminous sleeve, he rapidly performed a divination...","Then his entire body abruptly stiffened!","It was Soulfire!","That faint, mysterious aura was the aura of Soulfire!","The world of the Nine Provinces had been formed from the body of Great God Pangu. It was said that Pangu’s heart, liver, spleen, lungs, and kidneys had become the five elements of metal, wood, water, fire, and earth. These five elemental energies were also the source of power for cultivators.","But there were indeed other sources of power in the world...","Soulfire, for example!","Soulfire refined from human souls could unleash tremendous power. Compared to the forces of yin, yang, and the five elements, this power was far easier to control. It was an absolutely forbidden art in the Nine Provinces and Eighteen Lands, one that had vanished without a trace for a full thousand years.","The last time Daoist Master Songfeng had seen someone use such a forbidden art had been a thousand years ago...","It had been his master, the Sword Lord Taibai, who had given his life to suppress that heretic demon!","This divination had revealed far more than he had wanted to know. Daoist Master Songfeng was once again sweating profusely.","—No matter who Wu Guanyue was, anyone capable of understanding such a forbidden art was absolutely not someone to be trifled with.","Forget it. Just forget it... There was no need to avenge the living pine tree. If it was inferior to its opponent, whom could it blame?","And so, Wu Guanyue watched as the star-rated guest’s obviously furious gaze suddenly became clear and serene!","【Old Man Azurewood bowed deeply. “I have long heard that there is a great expert hidden among the common folk in Meishan City. I have wanted to come and seek your guidance for quite some time. Now that I have finally met you, I see that your reputation is well deserved. I am Old Man Azurewood. A pleasure to meet you.”】","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","So that had been the legendary challenge-match scenario!","It all made sense now. In a xianxia world, opening an inn naturally meant encountering this sort of thing. And, more importantly—","The player’s popularity had become high enough that NPCs had already heard of her?!","Wu Guanyue’s heart bloomed with joy. Imitating Old Man Azurewood, she bowed deeply and cheerfully greeted him.","“I am Wu Guanyue. I’ve long heard of you as well.”","Old Man Azurewood continued bowing. “My apologies for my previous disrespect~~”","Wu Guanyue continued bowing. “You’re too kind~~”","Lu Datong bowed deeply. “I’m impressed, I’m impressed!”","The two people who had been bowing to each other stopped and turned around in unison to look at him.","Lu Datong said emotionally, “Using martial arts to make friends—that is the true spirit of us cultivators!”","And so...","“Good!”","Lu Datong shouted his approval.","“Good! Good!”","The other guests also shouted their approval. The entire inn was once again filled with a cheerful atmosphere...","Daoist Master Songfeng: “............”","Daoist Master Songfeng forced a stiff smile. “Since it is getting late, then I shall...”","“Shopkeeper Wu, there has been some progress regarding what happened to your shop assistant, Wang Er.”","That was Wenren Ying, who had just strode into the inn.","Daoist Master Songfeng: “!”","His ears practically stood straight up at once.","Wenren Ying glanced at the unfamiliar white-bearded Daoist. His eyes seemed to narrow slightly beneath his bamboo hat before he shifted his gaze away without revealing anything.","Wu Guanyue looked up at him. “Mm-hmm. Where is Wang Er? Where is Wang Er?”","Wenren Ying folded his arms around his saber and leaned against the doorframe. “Someone saw Qian Shi'an taking him up Mount Huiming.”","“Mount Huiming? Isn’t that the place where tree demons are said to appear?”","“That old bastard Qian Shi'an really is beyond contempt. He clearly intends to kill someone!”","“That place is extremely dangerous. Shopkeeper, are you still going to look for him? I’m afraid Wang Er is already in grave danger.”","The guests all began asking questions.","【Quest · Side Quest: The Missing Shop Assistant (Updated)】","【Quest Details: Someone saw the owner of Yongfeng Money Exchange, Qian Shi'an, taking your shop assistant, Wang Er, up the mountain... Tree demons are said to haunt Mount Huiming. It remains uncertain whether Wang Er is still alive. Will you go up the mountain to search for him?】","Did she even need to think about it?","Wu Guanyue clenched both fists and declared resolutely, “I’m going up the mountain to find him! No matter what happened in the past, no matter how much he once wronged me or my grandfather, he is still a living human being! There’s no need for anyone to try to dissuade me. I must see him alive or see his corpse! I absolutely will not allow Wang Er to disappear without a trace! Wang Er, just wait! Your shopkeeper is coming to save you!”","In that instant, Shopkeeper Wu’s figure seemed so tall and noble. A holy radiance appeared to surround her, and everything about her seemed to embody a righteous soul and a noble character!","“Good!”","This deeply moving scene compelled Lu Datong to shout his approval.","“Righteous!”","“She’s truly righteous!”","“Those who are benevolent are invincible! This is what it means to be benevolent and invincible!”","The guests were all touched by Wu Guanyue’s magnanimity and began praising her one after another. The inn was once again filled with a cheerful atmosphere...","Daoist Master Songfeng: “............”","Daoist Master Songfeng: “..................”","Good grief!","This woman was far too righteous!!","The problem was that he had killed Wang Er!!!","Daoist Master Songfeng, who had not broken into a sweat in many years, began sweating profusely for the third time that day...","He truly had never imagined that killing such a timid, useless mortal would somehow bring him such calamity!","He had already planned to withdraw, but who could have known that Wu Guanyue would cling to him like a ghost, refusing to let him off no matter what!","Damn it...","If someone wants me dead, am I supposed to just sit here and wait to be slaughtered?","Wu Guanyue might indeed know how to wield forbidden arts... but Daoist Master Songfeng was no pushover either! This inn was her home turf, but Mount Huiming was his territory. If they really went to Mount Huiming, it was still anyone’s guess who would end up suffering!","With that thought, Daoist Master Songfeng made up his mind.","He beamed and said, “Shopkeeper Wu is truly righteous. Old Man Azurewood is deeply impressed. In that case, please allow Old Man Azurewood to lend you a hand!”","The gaze beneath Wenren Ying’s bamboo hat suddenly fixed on his face like a bolt of cold lightning!","Yet his expression remained relaxed. He merely said, “I am Wenren Ying. A pleasure to meet you.”","Old Man Azurewood continued to smile. “I have naturally heard of the illustrious Meishan’s Number One Blade... A pleasure to meet you as well.”","Wenren Ying asked again, “May I ask where you came from, Old Man Azurewood, and where you are headed?”","Old Man Azurewood was still smiling. “I came from where I came from, and I’m going where I’m going.”","Wu Guanyue suddenly appeared with a fishing rod slung over her shoulder, looking exceptionally cheerful. “What are you two rambling on about? Skip, skip, skip it all! Hahahahahaha! Come on, let’s go—we’re setting out right now!”","Old Man Azurewood: “???”","Wait, what? That fast?!!","Hadn’t you only just found out that Wang Er had gone to Mount Huiming?! You don’t even need to prepare? You’re leaving immediately? Are there really people in this world who do things like this?! You don’t need to get ready, but he does!!!","Wu Guanyue answered him with a clear, guileless gaze.","—The quest has already updated! How could she not push forward immediately? Hurry, hurry, hurry! I wonder what kind of reward she’ll get for her nuclear-powered donkey... Er, this is her first side quest in the game!","Old Man Azurewood: “............”","Old Man Azurewood: “..................”","A huge ellipsis bubble appeared above Old Man Azurewood’s head.","【[Old Man Azurewood] has joined [Wu Guanyue]’s adventuring party. They will never abandon one another, and will share life and death!】","Wenren Ying: (laughing.jpg)","Wenren Ying: (thumbs-up.jpg)","For some reason, Wenren Ying was inexplicably having a great time...","【[Wenren Ying] has joined [Wu Guanyue]’s adventuring party. They will never abandon one another, and will share life and death!】","“Woof! Woof! Grrr-woof!!”","Wuyun came charging out of nowhere, baring its triangular mouth and letting out a battle cry brimming with fighting spirit!","【[Wuyun] has joined [Wu Guanyue]’s adventuring party. They will never abandon one another, and will share life and death!】","Yes!","Adventure! Adventure! Adventure!","If you opened an inn in a xianxia world, you had to have this sort of team-up-and-beat-the-monsters segment. Otherwise, how could it seem sufficiently magnificent and wondrous?","Filled with heroic spirit, Wu Guanyue swept her fishing rod through the air and shouted, “Let’s go!”","Wu Guanyue suddenly leaped into the air and landed on Wuyun’s back in a one-legged golden-rooster stance!","Beneath the setting sun, Wuyun’s four paws pounded across the ground so fast they blurred. With a whoosh, it carried her away until both of them vanished from sight. In front of the inn, the fading afterimage of a girl standing like a golden rooster seemed to linger in the air...","Wenren Ying: “............”","Old Man Azurewood: “............”","Wenren Ying: “............?”","Old Man Azurewood: “............?”","The two men, each wary of the other, had probably synchronized their thoughts for the first time.","The End"]},{"number":14,"title":"Chapter 14","paragraphs":["***","Daoist Master Songfeng had taken the alias Old Man Azurewood. He had originally planned to set up an inescapable net on the mountain and make sure Wu Guanyue would never return once she came. Who could have guessed that Wu Guanyue understood the principle that speed was of the essence? The moment she learned Wang Er’s whereabouts, she did not hesitate for even a second. Now, immediately, this very instant, she was going to storm Mount Huiming!","At this moment, Wu Guanyue, now accompanied by her party, was making her way through the wilderness.","【[Wilderness Map · Mount Huiming] is now open. Come explore!】","【Mount Huiming: It is said that a thousand years ago, Sword Lord Taibai battled the Hundred-Eyed Demon Lord here. The shattered Huiming Mirror transformed into a thousand bright pools scattered throughout the mountain, giving the place its name.】","When exploring the wilderness in an RPG, what was the most important thing?","Why, looting everything in sight, of course!","However, the player had already experienced the game’s rich item system to her heart’s content in the outskirts of Meishan City. Her inventory slots were also quite limited, so she wouldn’t recklessly yank up every single thing she saw.","In the game, items the player had never collected before would be highlighted. The player could also keep her eyes fixed on an item for three seconds to view its description, allowing her to decide whether it was worth picking up.","Wu Guanyue walked at the very front, searching for every highlighted item within sight.","And so, the moment Old Man Azurewood saw Wu Guanyue enter the woods, her expression suddenly changed!","All at once, her eyes became so sharp and clear, her expression so capable and calculating. Her gaze swept over every tree and shrub in the forest, like a hawk circling in the sky—or the keenest, most agile hound of the Underworld!","Suddenly, her wise and discerning gaze locked onto an unremarkable-looking mountain tree.","【Jade Lychee: Named for its crystal-clear, jade-like flesh. Possesses powerful restorative effects.】","What was this? It seemed like a very good ingredient!","Wu Guanyue hefted her axe. Chop, chop, chop!","【Obtained: [Jade Lychee Wood] ×10】","【Obtained: [Jade Lychee Fruit] ×3】","Then she switched to a shovel and dug down hard!","【Obtained: [Jade Lychee Sapling] ×1】","Daoist Master Songfeng: “!!!”","His century-old jade lychee tree!!!","Damn it! This was a five-hundred-year-old jade lychee tree! It had absorbed the spiritual energy of heaven and earth in this place for centuries, producing fruits with flesh as smooth and lustrous as white jade. Not only were they fragrant and succulent, eating them was also greatly beneficial for nourishing one’s meridians and strengthening one’s foundation!","He usually couldn’t bear to eat the things, yet this woman had actually chopped it down! She had chopped it down!!!","Daoist Master Songfeng’s heart bled as he stared at Wu Guanyue’s unconcerned back, his eyes turning red.","Wu Guanyue continued her search—","【Obtained: [Wood Salt] ×7, [Saltwood Sapling] ×1!】","【Wood Salt: Precious crystals found on thousand-year-old saltwood trees. Can enhance the cultivation of cultivators with wood spiritual roots.】","【Obtained: [Fire Jujube] ×5, [Fire Jujube Sapling] ×1!】","【Fire Jujube: A crystal-clear fruit with orange-red energy flowing through its flesh. The essence of solar fire, it requires a little spiritual energy to activate.】","【Obtained: [Heavenly Nectar Vine] ×2!】","【Heavenly Nectar Vine: It is said that even the celestial immortals above the Ninth Heaven enjoy wine brewed from this plant’s nectar.】","Wenren Ying suddenly said, “Strange. Why does it sound like someone’s grinding their teeth? Is there a rat nearby?”","Daoist Master Songfeng slowly—very slowly—raised a hand and calmly pressed it against his cheek, restraining the sound of his own teeth grinding.","The corner of Wenren Ying’s mouth curled into a mysterious smile. “It’s quiet now... Even the vermin fear the Daoist master’s might! By the way, why do you look so awful, Daoist master?”","Daoist Master Songfeng: “............”","The vein at Daoist Master Songfeng’s temple throbbed violently.","Just then, Wu Guanyue suddenly spotted something!","Daoist Master Songfeng’s heart clenched. He felt as if he were facing a formidable enemy!","Wu Guanyue suddenly sprang into action! Her movements were as nimble as a gust of wind as she charged toward the spot she had noticed. Her hand shot out so quickly that it left afterimages. In the blink of an eye, she had snatched up the object she wanted and raised it high above her head!","Th-that was—","【Obtained: [Square Feces]!】","【Square Feces: Droppings left behind by an iron-eating beast.】","It was... the contents of a large-intestine sashimi platter!!!","Old Man Azurewood: “............”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wu Guanyue: “!!!”","What was this? Ammunition!","The ultimate boss she would have to face later was a tree demon! If she didn’t collect ammunition now, when would she?","And so, she began gathering frantically!","Old Man Azurewood and Wenren Ying stared dumbfoundedly as Wu Guanyue cheerfully collected the feces scattered across the ground. The two of them fell into silence at the same time.","But when had the player ever cared about NPC opinions?","This was ammunition!","Wu Guanyue: (★ω★)!","Her hands were cupped around the fertilizer, and her eyes shone like stars. Her expression was extraordinarily satisfied, extraordinarily blissful...","Daoist Master Songfeng: “............”","Daoist Master Songfeng: “..................”","Hmph. What an idiot!","Old Man Songfeng thought with utter disdain.","Just then, Wu Guanyue’s sharp eyes spotted something else!","There was an earthworm writhing on the ground!","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","A veteran player of Stardew Valley could never see an earthworm and simply ignore it—she absolutely had to dig it up and see what it was!","Wu Guanyue didn’t give it a second thought. She brought her hoe down in one stroke!","Blood-red tentacles shot out in an instant!","Wenren Ying moved at the same moment.","A streak of sword light condensed into a single line!","Fast, sharp, precise—the blade cleaved through the air, its shriek as piercing as a ghost’s wail. The bloody tentacle was severed in midair.","Only then did Wenren Ying’s boots touch the ground. He had already placed himself in front of Wu Guanyue.","Her view was blocked by the cloak he had sent billowing into the air, and Wu Guanyue fell into thought for a moment.","Wenren Ying’s lips were pressed into a tight line. The easygoing temperament that had remained unruffled even when stuffed with large-intestine sashimi had vanished from him. In its place was something cold and hard.","He said in a low voice, “It’s a Bloodvine. The beast is good at hiding. See if you can find any more.”","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","So that was what it was!","Although she didn’t know whether the Bloodvine counted as a plant or a monster, the player’s [Highlight Display] could be set to show one specific type of item. It was a convenient function designed to make gathering in the wilderness easier.","Then let’s search for Bloodvines right away!","Wu Guanyue willed it, and the scene before her eyes immediately changed. Every Bloodvine hidden beneath the ground began flashing brightly. There were actually quite a lot of them in this area, practically forming a minefield. If Wu Guanyue hadn’t dug up the first one just now, she really might have been caught off guard and lashed by one of these things.","Wuyun, facing a formidable enemy, let out a hiss!","Wu Guanyue, facing a formidable enemy, pointed accusingly!","Daoist Master Songfeng, facing a formidable enemy, made no sound at all!","Obviously. These Bloodvines had been cultivated by him.","To be honest, he hadn’t expected Wenren Ying to recognize them either, because Bloodvines were an extraordinarily rare kind of evil creature.","This thing has been lying dormant underground, not leaking a single wisp of demonic aura. Let alone Wenren Ying... even if Perfected Renhua, the elder of Xuantian Sect, showed up right now, he might not be able to spot it!","But somehow, Wu Guanyue managed to find every last one of them without missing a single one!","Who on earth is Wu Guanyue?!","If finding the first one could be written off as pure luck, then after that... with just a quick sweep of her gaze, she didn't let a single one slip past!","Right then, Wenren Ying moved through the ground blood vines as easily as chopping melons and vegetables, finishing them off in the blink of an eye.","No way! He can't stay with these two people any longer!","If he keeps hanging around these two disasters, who knows when his secret will be exposed!","In the flash of a lightning bolt, Daoist Master Songfeng made up his mind.","He suddenly took a step back, and his foot landed right on something — the next instant, blood-red tentacles shot out from the ground and stung Daoist Master Songfeng.","\"AAAAAHHHH!!!\"","Daoist Master Songfeng let out a bloodcurdling scream and collapsed heavily onto the ground.","Wu Guanyue and Wenren Ying both stopped what they were doing and turned around to look at him.","Old Man Azurewood (face twisted in pain): \"No... this old Taoist has been hit... (coughs up blood)\"","Wu Guanyue: \"............\"","Wu Guanyue: \"!!!\"","Wu Guanyue was completely stunned! Wha — what?! Her teammate is already heavily injured! This is only the first wave of trash mobs in this dungeon! Isn't he going down way too fast?!","Wu Guanyue's eyes went wide, clearly utterly shocked and flustered by the turn of events.","Wenren Ying, who was always known for his warm-hearted nature, on the other hand, just crossed his arms over his blade and looked at Old Man Azurewood leisurely.","Old Man Azurewood (face ashen): \"You... don't worry about me... saving people is the priority... (coughs up blood)\"","Old Man Azurewood has submitted a request to leave the party to Wu Guanyue. Do you agree?","Whoa now...","He actually wants to leave the party? This whole partying thing feels like it hasn't served any purpose at all.","Wu Guanyue sank into thought.","Wait, this game has really well-written story content, it never does things half-baked. The choice she makes right now will most likely shape the direction of the plot later on.","If she agrees to let Old Man Azurewood leave the party right now, his entire personal storyline will probably get cut off directly, and it's even possible that when she comes back later, she'll find Old Man Azurewood's corpse nearby — that's absolutely unacceptable for a player!","Wu Guanyue: \"No way! Don't say another word! I will never abandon you at a time like this. That's my principle!\"","Wu Guanyue spoke out in a voice full of righteous kindness!","Old Man Azurewood (tears welling up in his eyes): \"Shopkeeper Wu's great righteousness... this old Taoist will remember it... But my injuries are far too severe... I'm afraid I'll only slow you two down... (coughs up blood)\"","Old Man Azurewood's life is hanging by a thread. Do you want to give him an item?","Oh right... so this is a leech that's here to collect!","RPG games really do work like this sometimes. You have to give a character a few items in a row to push the story forward properly. It's super annoying, but there's no way around it.","What item should she give him to restore his health?","Wu Guanyue opened her backpack. Because she was going to explore a new map, she had cleared out her backpack ahead of time so she could bring back more loot... Right now her backpack is totally full of precious items like jade lychees, fire dates, and jade wine vines.","...She doesn't want to give any of them away.","She hasn't even gotten to test out their special effects yet, and there's barely any of them. The thought of handing them all over to this leech is the last thing she wants to do.","Just then, her peripheral vision landed on the item that she had the most of in her backpack.","Wu Guanyue: \"!!\"","A little lightbulb suddenly lit up over Wu Guanyue's head.","She immediately pulled a square-shaped piece of dung out from her sleeve, held it out politely, and asked: \"Daoist, can you eat shit to get your health back?\"","Old Man Azurewood: \"............\"","Old Man Azurewood: \"..................\"","Old Man Azurewood jumped up and yelled at the top of his lungs: \"You shameless bastard! You little runt! You worthless scum! How dare you! This is the last straw! I'm going to fight you to the death!!!\"","And there we go, the setup is done, next chapter the real boss fight starts!"]},{"number":15,"title":"Chapter 15","paragraphs":["***","In the midst of his fury, a cold gleam flashed into being!","A streak of white light suddenly split from the sleeve of Daoist Master Songfeng. It was astonishingly sharp—and unbelievably fast!","Of the countless martial arts techniques under heaven, only speed was truly impossible to overcome. Cultivators could certainly use spiritual energy to protect themselves, but first they had to have enough time to react!","Daoist Master Songfeng’s sword was already thrusting toward Wu Guanyue’s brow!","The sword-light arced like a rainbow!","Wenren Ying gave a thunderous shout, and his blade flashed into view!","Shadow-Splitting, Sky-Rending!","But Wu Guanyue’s provocation had come far too suddenly, completely beyond his expectations. He was standing some distance away from her, while Daoist Master Songfeng’s speed was actually no slower than his own!","As a result, he was too far away to come to her rescue!","“Get out of the way!” Wenren Ying roared.","But it was already too late!","The sword-light had arrived! That icy gleam seemed to have grazed across her brow—","At that instant, when everything hung by a thread, the player’s superhuman reflexes came online once again!","[Using Proficiency Skill—Pickpocketing!]","Her body suddenly shot backward like a kite being yanked by its string.","Daoist Master Songfeng’s sword-light clung to her like a parasite, pursuing her relentlessly!","A pitch-black blade descended through the air, intercepting the sword-light. Daoist Master Songfeng let out a strange cry, his sword trembling as it became entangled with Wenren Ying’s saber!","“Shhk!”","Wenren Ying’s cloak had been pickpocketed by Wu Guanyue!","[Obtained: Wenren Ying’s Cloak ×1]","[Wenren Ying’s Cloak: Very rough, but softened by long use...]","Wenren Ying: “............”","While speechless, Wenren Ying had already exchanged more than a dozen blows with Daoist Master Songfeng.","Daoist Master Songfeng executed a “Cloud-Turning Flip,” drifting several yards away. With his left hand forming a sword seal and his right hand holding his sword aloft, he balanced on one leg and assumed the opening stance of “Pine Welcoming Guests.”","His expression, however, was hideous with rage as he demanded, “You! When did you discover me?!”","Wenren Ying stood with his saber in hand.","His figure was tall and powerfully built. Simply standing there, he radiated an oppressive presence impossible to ignore.","Beneath his bamboo hat, his eyes fixed coldly on Daoist Master Songfeng. Then he suddenly smiled, revealing teeth as white as snow.","“You smell of blood.”","Fresh blood.","Wenren Ying was more sensitive to the scent of blood than most. The moment he saw Old Man Azurewood, he had immediately realized that the man had killed someone not long ago—and not a cultivator, but an ordinary civilian.","Cultivators who embarked upon the path of martial enlightenment and gained the ability to resonate with heaven and earth did not do so in order to bully ordinary people.","A cultivator who had just killed a mortal—could he really be a righteous man? Why had he come up the mountain with them to rescue someone?","To claim he had no ulterior motives? Wenren Ying wouldn’t believe it even if his toes did the thinking.","He smiled. “Our little shopkeeper, Wu, also thought there was something wrong with you from the beginning... Didn’t you, Shopkeeper Wu?”","Although he had no idea how she had figured it out... Old Man Azurewood had already crossed paths with Wu Guanyue before he went to the inn. Presumably, she had noticed something was off even then.","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Wu Guanyue wore an expression of sudden realization and could not help sighing. “So that’s how it is. The undercurrents are truly surging.”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wait, you didn’t notice?!","So just now, you had genuinely been planning to use feces to heal Old Man Azurewood and bring him back from the brink of death...?","Wenren Ying: “..................”","A huge cold-sweat bubble appeared above Wenren Ying’s head.","Daoist Master Songfeng sneered. “Hmph... Today, I’ll send you underground to accompany Wang Er!”","Since he had been exposed anyway, he might as well fight them to the death!","It wasn’t that he could not fight. He simply had not wanted to, fearing that a battle would leave him seriously weakened.","But if they truly forced him into a corner, he had nothing to fear from anyone!","“Waaah—!”","Daoist Master Songfeng let out a bizarre cry. The tip of his sword trembled, sending out ten thousand blossoms of sword-light, like a torrential white rain sweeping down from the heavens and crashing straight toward Wenren Ying and Wu Guanyue!","Wenren Ying shouted, and his blade-light flashed like black lightning!","Everyone said, “Though you draw a saber to cut the water, the water continues to flow.” But Wenren Ying’s saber had already cleaved through that dense curtain of rain. With a single stroke, it was capable of taking his opponent’s head!","That was precisely why he could roam across the Nine Provinces despite being a cripple with a shattered spirit palace: his perception of spiritual energy and his grasp of the perfect moment to strike had both been honed to the pinnacle.","The cold edge of his saber had already brushed against Daoist Master Songfeng’s throat...","Yet a strange light flashed through Daoist Master Songfeng’s eyes.","Not good!","The instant the blade sliced across Daoist Master Songfeng’s throat, Wenren Ying sensed that something was wrong. He immediately twisted his body and performed a “Hawk-Turning Flip,” but it was already too late!","The sword-light pierced through Wenren Ying’s shoulder, spraying blood like an arrow.","And yet Daoist Master Songfeng’s head... remained perfectly intact atop his neck.","The saber had indeed cut into his throat—but what it had struck was not human flesh.","The skin on Daoist Master Songfeng’s face and neck had transformed into patches of tree bark.","The bark was so coarse and so tough that even Wenren Ying could not sever it with a single stroke.","Wenren Ying stared coldly at his neck.","There was indeed a gash there, but what flowed from it was not blood. It was sap.","The wound was slowly healing. Suddenly, the soil beneath their feet began to tremble, as if poisonous snakes were writhing beneath it...","But what emerged from the earth were not snakes. They were roots—gnarled, twisted roots coiling over one another!","Dense masses of roots spread outward from Daoist Master Songfeng, driving deep into the soil and drawing nourishment from the earth.","Daoist Master Songfeng burst into laughter. “Wenren Ying! So what if they call you the Number One Saber of Mount Mei? Go on, try breaking my Tree-Skin Technique! And even if you manage it... I have plenty of ways to recover!”","Wenren Ying stared coldly at Daoist Master Songfeng.","Blood was still flowing from his shoulder.","His shattered spirit palace prevented him from circulating his energy to heal his wounds. It also left him unable to use protective qi to shield himself.","Suddenly, he spat on the ground with an extremely vulgar “Ptooey!”","In the next instant, his blade-light surged forth like an angry tide!","Daoist Master Songfeng cried out, and another storm of white light erupted like driving rain!","Before the player could even act, the NPCs had already started fighting among themselves!!!","This was Wu Guanyue’s first time experiencing the game’s combat style firsthand. Her previous battle with the living pine tree did not count. The game’s combat style was actually more like Hollow Knight...","It featured dazzling martial techniques and spectacular footwork, while the full-dive gaming experience gave this real-time combat an even greater sense of impact!","Blades flashed and swords clashed! Thunder boomed like a cataclysm!","Within the depths of the forest, the leaves shuddered and fell from the trees beneath the force of the blade-wind, only to be shredded by sword-light in the blink of an eye. The fragments whipped toward Wu Guanyue’s head and face, bringing the icy, murderous atmosphere right against her skin!","Blood sprayed through the air! The crimson gleam was... hauntingly beautiful.","The blood had soaked Wenren Ying’s clothes, making the fabric cling heavily to his body. It displayed with brutal honesty the rhythm of his breathing and the contraction and expansion of his muscles, filling her with a strange, feverish rush of adrenaline.","Cold and heat. Death and life. An icy blade and blazing flesh...","That was the combat style of this game.","【[Old Man Azurewood] used [Spell: Tree Bark Technique]. Armor +100!】","【[Wenren Ying] was afflicted by [Negative Status: Spirit Mansion Shattered]. Armor reduced to zero!】","【[Old Man Azurewood] was hit by [Wenren Ying]’s [Horizontal Chop]. HP -158!】","【[Old Man Azurewood] used [Spell: Earthly Rejuvenation]. HP +160!】","【[Wenren Ying] was hit by [Old Man Azurewood]’s [Sword Art: Verdant Waves, Pine Wind]. HP -130!】","But this was no time to appreciate the style... His teammate was already on the verge of being beaten to death!!!","Granted, in terms of combat ability and the style of his techniques, Wenren Ying was definitely superior. But—","Daoist Master Songfeng laughed loudly. “Gotcha! This old man can heal!”","Without even turning his head, Wenren Ying shouted sternly, “Get out of here!”","This Old Man Azurewood was no ordinary tree demon!","Its roots had burrowed deep underground, drawing nutrients from below and allowing it to heal its wounds at any time. Wenren Ying had indeed considered severing its roots... but they were buried deep beneath the earth. In the middle of a battle, how could he possibly find the time to dig them up?! It wasn’t as though he had an earth spirit root!","So all he could do was tell Wu Guanyue to leave!","The girl was still very young. She was nowhere near the age at which she ought to die.","But how could Wu Guanyue possibly leave?","How outrageous! This NPC had started a group fight without bringing the player along and was trying to solo the boss!","And did he even have what it took to solo it?!","After witnessing the fight just now, the player had already gained a complete understanding of Old Man Azurewood’s characteristics—","Disgusting! That was the only word for it!","It was the kind of disgusting boss that combined high attack, high defense, and self-healing! The kind of disgusting boss players would sum up on the forums with one piece of advice:","The best strategy is not to fight it!","There were only two ways to deal with a disgusting boss like this. The first was to break through its defenses. The second was to interrupt its self-healing.","And the player’s plan was crystal clear!","Interrupt the self-healing!","Wu Guanyue remained calm and composed as she shouted, “Brother Wenren, I’m coming to help!!!”","Wenren Ying’s expression changed instantly. “Don’t come over!”","But it was already too late!","Wu Guanyue had already made her move!","Suddenly, countless hidden weapons flew from Wu Guanyue’s hands like flowers scattering from the heavens!","The projectiles were brown, square-shaped...","Those—those were—!","【[Wu Guanyue] used the skill [Rapid Food Delivery], sending [Square Feces] ×100 to [Old Man Azurewood]!】","【[Wu Guanyue] performed the [Job Action: Fertilizing] on a plant, triggering the [Passive Effect: Rapid Fertilization]!】","It was poop! It was actually poop!!!","But it had arrived at exactly the right moment!","Under the effect of [Rapid Fertilization], the square feces were refined the instant they came into contact with the soil!!!","“AAARGH!!!!”","Daoist Master Songfeng suddenly let out a scream that shook heaven and earth!","【[Wu Guanyue], having failed to perform the prerequisite action [Composting], triggered the [Root Burn] effect!】","None"]},{"number":16,"title":"Chapter 16","paragraphs":["***","Heavenly Maiden Scattering Flowers!","Fertilizer filled the sky, carried on fierce winds, and hemmed Daoist Master Songfeng in from every direction!","Plants absorbed nutrients through their roots. The reason Daoist Master Songfeng had been able to act so arrogantly was precisely because of his technique, “Spring’s Return to the Earth.”","But now—the technique had been broken!","Daoist Master Songfeng had already entered the inn, and the special insignia marking him as a star-rated guest was still hovering above his head. Wu Guanyue’s divine skill, [Quick Delivery], ensured that every handful of fertilizer landed on him with pinpoint accuracy!","Wenren Ying was no pushover either—","His blade flashed through the air!","[[Old Man Azurewood] was hit by [Wenren Ying]’s [Horizontal Slash]. HP -158!]","[[Old Man Azurewood] used [Spell: Spring’s Return to the Earth]. Critical failure!]","[[Old Man Azurewood] was hit by [Wenren Ying]’s [Horizontal Slash]. HP -298!]","[[Old Man Azurewood] used [Spell: Spring’s Return to the Earth]. Critical failure!]","[[Old Man Azurewood] was hit by [Wenren Ying]’s [Horizontal Slash]. HP -398!]","[[Old Man Azurewood] used [Spell: Spring’s Return to the Earth]. Critical failure!]","The blade in Wenren Ying’s hand seemed less like a weapon than the fang of some vicious beast. Other than killing his opponent, he had not a single thought in his mind!","When that savage blade flashed once more, Daoist Master Songfeng finally caught sight of the eyes hidden beneath Wenren Ying’s bamboo hat—","They were crimson as fresh blood and as merciless as a beast’s.","A terror that made his heart and gall split apart suddenly seized Daoist Master Songfeng. He could barely keep hold of his sword.","Life and death were decided in the space of a breath. How could one afford to be distracted in a duel?","“Ahhhhhhhhhh!”","Daoist Master Songfeng let out a scream that shook the heavens—","His entire body had been split in two by Wenren Ying. Then, before anyone could react, Wenren Ying plunged his blade into the man’s body and carved out the spiritual core from his spirit palace.","Daoist Master Songfeng struggled wildly!","But it was already over. So what if he had cultivated for a thousand years? Once his core had been cut out, he could not survive even another fifteen minutes!","“You... you’re... so... vicious...”","The light in Daoist Master Songfeng’s eyes faded completely.","The corner of Wenren Ying’s mouth twitched ever so slightly. There seemed to be a sharp, mocking edge to that smile.","Daoist Master Songfeng collapsed to the ground and breathed his last.","Wenren Ying flicked his blade. The beads of blood became crimson agates before sinking into the soil and vanishing.","The wind gradually died down.","Leaves rustled and fell, landing damply in the bloodstained earth.","Wenren Ying’s body suddenly swayed.","The supreme stimulation of the life-and-death battle was slowly ebbing away. The wounds left by the swords that had stabbed and twisted through him had torn his flesh open, sending blood streaming down his body. A web of agonizing pain ensnared him, making his chest heave and his breathing grow as harsh and heavy as a beast’s.","Supporting himself, he slowly made his way outward, taking one step after another.","A pair of soft, warm arms caught him.","Wenren Ying lowered his head and saw Wu Guanyue’s two tightly braided pigtails.","She must have run over at full speed—the two ponytails were still bouncing.","She tilted her head up, her eyes opened wide, looking as though she were facing a great enemy.","“Brother Wenren! You’ve only got a sliver of HP left!!!”","...Only a sliver of HP? Was she saying that he was badly injured?","What a strange way of putting it.","Wenren Ying could not help smiling. “I’m fine.”","When facing an enemy, he often displayed an icy hardness that made people’s hearts tremble with fear. But when he was not holding a blade, he was actually a man who smiled easily.","“I’ll help you!” Wu Guanyue said.","Wenren Ying looked down at her. “Then I’ll trouble you, Little Shopkeeper Wu.”","Wu Guanyue’s lips tightened into a serious line, and she nodded solemnly.","She slowly led Wenren Ying away from the area where she had—er, scattered flowers like a heavenly maiden. Following the sound of running water, they reached a clear stream and found a large tree sturdy enough to lean against. She helped Wenren Ying sit down beneath it to rest.","Wenren Ying closed his eyes. His lips were pale, and he looked as though he no longer had the strength to lift even a finger.","His voice was somewhat hoarse. “Little Shopkeeper Wu, please fetch me a Rejuvenation Powder. It’s inside my lapel.”","Wu Guanyue did not reach for his lapel.","Instead, she slipped a hand into her sleeve and rummaged around with a rustle. From her inventory, she pulled out a [Jade Lychee] and held it to Wenren Ying’s lips.","Items in the game were divided into five grades: white, green, blue, purple, and orange. The five colors corresponded to the descriptions ordinary, excellent, rare, treasured, and peerless.","[Rejuvenation Powder] was the most common kind of hemostatic medicine, a white-grade ordinary item.","The [Jade Lychee], meanwhile, was a blue-grade rare item. Its healing effect was much stronger and should have been enough to restore him to full health!","Yet Wenren Ying said, “Keep it for yourself.”","Wu Guanyue: “?”","Wu Guanyue stared at him in confusion.","Wenren Ying smiled. “My spirit palace is damaged. This thing is too potent for me. I can’t handle such a powerful supplement.”","The dantian, or spirit palace, was where cultivators circulated and stored the spiritual energy of Heaven and Earth. Within the spirit palace, that spiritual energy was refined to purity and then drawn upon whenever needed.","But Wenren Ying was different. His spirit palace was completely incapable of storing spiritual energy...","The [Jade Lychee] was a powerful tonic to others, but to him, it was arsenic capable of making his body explode from within.","Wu Guanyue fell into deep thought...","Oh, she understood now. Wenren Ying had no mana bar.","When other cultivators were injured, they could spend mana to restore their HP. But he could not. He could only wait for his health bar to recover naturally.","...Wasn’t that a little too tragic?","Wu Guanyue crouched beside Wenren Ying with a tense expression and stared at him.","Wuyun poked its head out from nearby and let out a series of heartbroken meows.","Wenren Ying smiled. “You don’t need to look at me like that. I helped you simply because I wanted to. And I killed Old Man Azurewood because I had an urge to kill. The way I ended up like this was also my own doing...”","His voice gradually dropped away, while his painful breathing grew heavier.","Wu Guanyue: “Mm...”","Wu Guanyue stared at him, sinking into thought.","Wenren Ying couldn’t heal himself, but could someone else heal him?","Hmm...","Did players have any healing skills?","...Apparently not.","But now that she thought about it, hadn’t he just said something important?","“Too weak to handle a powerful tonic”... Hmm, too weak to handle a powerful tonic.","In other words, he couldn’t consume the [Jade Lychee] because its item grade was too high?","Then what about lower-grade items? Could he use those?","After all, he could drink the soda she had made from green-grade [Living Pine Needles]!","Concerned about her teammate, Wu Guanyue immediately opened her backpack and checked the items she had.","Hmm... Whether it was [Fire Jujube] or [Jade Nectar Vine], they were all blue-grade items. It was also her own fault for being too picky—she had always ignored anything too ordinary...","There was, however, one thing that possessed an excellent green quality rating. Hmm... Whether it worked or not, it was worth a try!","With an expression full of concern, Wu Guanyue pulled [Square-Shaped Excrement] ×1 from her sleeve and held it out in front of Wenren Ying.","“Brother Wenren, can eating poop restore your HP?”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","A large, cross-shaped vein bulged on Wenren Ying’s forehead.","***","【Quest · Side Quest: The Missing Shop Assistant (Completed!)】","【Quest Rating: ★★★☆☆】","【Quest Details: From Old Man Azurewood, you learned that Wang Er had already died... Perhaps you could have done better, but in the end, this was not your fault. You had done everything you could for Wang Er.】","【Quest Rewards: [Rare · Green-Tide Sword] ×1, [Rare · Pinewind Sword Technique] ×1, [Rare · Spring Rejuvenation] ×1, [Collector’s · Huiming Mirror] ×1, [Collector’s · Seven-Treasure Pine Inner Core] ×1】","In short, the game’s very first side quest was complete!","Although the quest’s overall rating was only three stars because Wang Er had already died, the rewards were still quite generous!","Not only did they include three blue-quality items, but there were even two purple-quality items!","【[Collector’s · Huiming Mirror]: You obtained this item from Old Man Azurewood’s cave dwelling. Three lines of tiny characters are engraved on the back of the mirror: The first reveals true forms, the second locks onto souls, and the third illuminates cause and effect.】","【[Collector’s · Seven-Treasure Pine Inner Core]: The inner core left behind by Daoist Master Songfeng after his death. It looks like a seed... Perhaps you could try planting it?】","Since the description said it could be planted... then why not give it a try?","Wu Guanyue planted the seed in the backyard of her own inn.","As for the [Huiming Mirror], it sounded like some sort of demon-revealing mirror.","Thinking of the three question marks after Wuyun’s species classification, Wu Guanyue suddenly grabbed Wuyun, who had been curled up asleep on top of her quilt.","Wuyun: “Mii... mii...”","Wuyun let out a faint, feeble cry.","【Wuyun: A creature that does not know what it is, and therefore frequently makes suspicious noises.】","【[Wu Guanyue] used [Huiming Mirror] on [Wuyun]. Identification: Great Success!】","【Name: Wuyun】","【Species: Mirage Beast】","【Level: LV.1】","【Description: A young mirage beast that somehow ended up here...】","【Mirage Beast: Capable of creating incredibly realistic illusions and luring unsuspecting cultivators who wander inside to exhaust all their spiritual energy... Their cultivation increases by feeding on this energy. A rather wicked and exceedingly rare demon beast.】","Wuyun: OωO","The wicked Wuyun opened its round eyes. At that moment, it was chasing after Wu Guanyue’s foot, apparently planning to bite it if it managed to catch it.","Hmm... It really was wicked. But that could be set aside for now.","Daoist Master Songfeng’s death naturally advanced the completion of the main quest.","“Have you heard? Qian Shi’an seems to have run away.”","“That bastard did every evil thing under the sun... and he even claimed our shopkeeper owed him money!”","“Hey, wasn’t it said that he had a demon for a master?”","“Hmph! That demon master was chopped up by our shopkeeper and Big Brother Wenren!”","“They’re that powerful?”","“Shopkeeper, you’re an expert! Forgive us for not recognizing you sooner!”","The guests loudly discussed the matter in the inn’s main hall, conveniently raising the inn’s popularity value as well.","【Quest · Main Quest: Pay Your Debts (Completed!)】","【Quest Rating: ★★★☆☆】","【Quest Details: Just who was Daoist Master Songfeng? And why did he possess two treasures of such astonishing power? These questions occasionally troubled you in the dead of night. Still, you successfully defended your inn, and wasn’t that enough?】","【Quest Reward: [Perhaps... Take a Look at Your Feet? (LV.1)]】","Wu Guanyue’s heart suddenly skipped a beat.","The quest reward was written in such a bizarre way that she stared at it for a long time before suddenly logging out of the game.","In an instant, the quaint and elegant immortal city vanished, replaced by the pale ceiling of a hospital room.","Wu Guanyue immediately threw off the covers.","“Hey, Little Yue, what are you doing?”","The caregiver, who had been playing on her phone, was startled by the sudden movement.","Wu Guanyue paid her no attention. She merely stared fixedly at her own feet.","They were little more than skin and bones... Long-term paralysis had caused the muscles in her legs and feet to atrophy, leaving them thin and weak. She could not lift the front of her feet, and her toes always pointed downward. To a healthy person, this would look extremely strange.","But Wu Guanyue had long since grown used to it.","She stared at her feet as her heart pounded faster and faster.","Then—her foot suddenly moved.","Using all the speed she could manage, she put her game helmet back on. The game’s main quest had been updated!","【Quest · Main Quest: The Lotus Tournament!】","【Quest Description: The annual sect tournament at Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven is about to begin. It is both a grand event for Meishan City and the inn industry’s peak season! During this quarter, earn more money and popularity, and upgrade the inn to LV.4! Become a hot property where every room is in high demand!】","【Quest Reward: [Granted according to rating]】","This chapter has been revised a little, so I recommend rereading it!!!"]},{"number":17,"title":"Chapter 17","paragraphs":["***","Who would have thought that completing the main quests in a game could actually affect reality!","Wu Guanyue was completely dazed by this pie that had fallen from the sky!","Why was this happening? Could it really be that a brain-computer game could stimulate the electrical signals in her muscles? Had technology truly advanced to this degree? If they had such incredible technology, why hadn’t they put it into clinical use immediately instead of turning it into a game and selling it?","Question after question arose, but not one of them remained in Wu Guanyue’s mind for even a second. At that moment, she had only one thought—","Then she had to grind like crazy!!!","Who cared why it was happening? Her leg had moved! Her leg had actually moved!","Who among people like Wu Guanyue had never dreamed of a deity answering their prayers? Now that one really had—if she didn’t seize the opportunity at once and instead wasted time asking questions, what kind of person would that make her?","The quest! Her quest!","This time, she absolutely had to get a five-star rating!","Wu Guanyue sprang up and darted out the door. She moved so fast she seemed quicker than a dark cloud!","Wuyun, who had been curled up on the bed chasing his tail, looked up. “?”","By then, Wu Guanyue had already reached the inn’s main hall.","Since she had just logged out of the game, management mode had automatically taken over. “Automatic management” meant that guests took whatever they wanted and left the money on the counter afterward.","At this moment, two or three tables were occupied in the hall, with people eating and drinking.","A new customer entered and craned his neck to examine the menu board on the wall.","Lu Datong called out, “Sprite thirty copper, baked flatbread four, chilled mixed flatbread six! Stir-fried flatbread’s next door—go over there if you want it!”","The new customer said, “Oh... oh. Then I’ll have a Sprite and a chilled mixed flatbread.”","Without even looking up, Lu Datong said, “Sprite’s over here—help yourself. Flatbread’s over there. Six copper for ten; pick them yourself.”","The new customer fell silent.","Then he exclaimed, “Wait, the customers have to do it themselves?!”","A thin, tall regular sitting nearby laughed. “Come on. The innkeeper’s selling a bowl of Sprite for thirty coppers. What more do you want? The jade-green cold soup at the Xihua Old Shop isn’t something you can afford either!”","The new customer thought it over and decided the man seemed to have a point. He rubbed his nose and shuffled over to serve himself.","Wu Guanyue came rushing down from upstairs—","“Little Boss Wu’s here,” Lu Datong said. “Want something to drink?”","“Lu Datong, Lu Datong, do you know about the Lotus Tournament—”","In short, the first step was to gather background information!","Lu Datong had not yet answered when his companion, Sun Deng, burst out laughing. “Know about it? Old Lu came to Mount Mei specifically to enter the grand competition and fight for—ow!”","Lu Datong drove an elbow into him. “Get lost! Eat your food!”","Only then did he turn back to Wu Guanyue. “Little Boss Wu, you don’t know about the Lotus Tournament?”","Of course Wu Guanyue didn’t know. Although there were all sorts of NPCs in Mount Mei City, what player had the time to interact with every one of them?","Still, it didn’t matter. Lu Datong alone was enough to explain the background to her.","Shenxiao Prefecture revered the Shenxiao Sect above all others. Beneath it were the Nine Peaks and Thirty-Six Grotto-Heavens. Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven was one of those Thirty-Six Grotto-Heavens. Its current master, Verdant Cloud Adept, was a highly accomplished disciple of the Xuanti Sect of Yuntai Peak, one of the Nine Peaks, and now governed all of Mount Mei.","Oh. Got it. An immortal-cultivation version of the feudal system.","The Shenxiao Sect was like the Son of Heaven of the Zhou dynasty, the Xuanti Sect was a feudal lord, and Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven was a scholar-official beneath that lord. The difference was that, in this immortal-cultivation version, the bonds were formed through master-and-disciple lineages.","Thus, the Nine Peaks and Thirty-Six Grotto-Heavens were considered the orthodox cultivation traditions of Shenxiao Prefecture. The other clans and sects might possess considerable strength, but ultimately, they could not be counted among the top tier.","The Lotus Tournament was the grand competition through which Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven selected its inner disciples. Since the champion was decided on the Lotus Platform atop Flying Peak on the final day, the event was popularly known as the “Lotus Tournament.”","After five years as an outer disciple, one had to participate in this competition. Those who failed had to leave the sect and make their own way in the world. Since Shenxiao Prefecture respected the martial path, the first several rounds of the competition were held on platforms set up throughout the city, allowing the common people to learn from the fights.","For that reason, the Lotus Tournament was the grandest event in Mount Mei. Whenever it took place, countless people came from far and wide to watch the arena matches.","This year, there was something even more special about it.","Verdant Cloud Adept had personally declared that he would give wandering cultivators throughout the realm an opportunity. Thus, this year’s Lotus Tournament had opened its doors wide, allowing wandering cultivators to compete on the same stage as disciples of the grotto-heaven.","As a result, there were far more outsiders in the city than usual. For the inn business, this was the busiest of peak seasons. All the major inns were rubbing their hands together, waiting to make a fortune during the grand event.","So that was how it was...","Wu Guanyue pondered.","Then, what she needed to do next was visit all the different parts of the city and see what kinds of products her competitors were preparing to offer.","With Wuyun perched on her head, Wu Guanyue prepared to head out.","Lu Datong had nothing else to do, so he volunteered to accompany her.","Lu Datong had once cultivated in a minor sect, but the sect had later been destroyed in an attack by demons and evil spirits, leaving him a wandering cultivator. After drifting from place to place for years, he heard that Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven would be accepting wandering cultivators this year as well. That was what had brought him to Mount Mei.","After arriving in Mount Mei City, he had spent his time both searching secret realms for rare treasures on behalf of Yuelai Inn and waiting for the sect competition to begin. Because of this, he was something of an insider in the inn business and could explain many things to Wu Guanyue.","[Lu Datong: “Our employer recently asked us to look for red bi feathers. I guess they’re preparing to attract guests with fire spiritual roots.”]","[Lu Datong: “Red bi birds can command fire. You can’t eat their feathers, but you can burn them to extract true-fire essence. Someone with a fire spiritual root can sit inside and meditate while circulating their breath. It’s very useful!”]","So that was how it worked.","[Lu Datong: “That young fellow who was with me, Sun Deng—Boss, you remember him, right? He does the same kind of work. He works for the Xihua Old Shop over there. Recently, they’ve all been in the Bingyi Realm looking for Bingyi swallows!”]","[Lu Datong: “Bingyi swallows can guide water through the meridians. Their nests can be processed into water silk, and fabric woven from water silk—tsk! It’s incredibly cool! The Xihua Old Shop uses it to make bed curtains.”]","So that was how it worked.","It seemed that everyone was mainly preparing to cater to cultivators with water spiritual roots.","There were seven or eight inns along a single street, and each had its own signature guest rooms. Some claimed to possess ice beds that were ideal for meditation and cultivation. Others advertised freshly caught fire prawns from the Suwen River.","Wuyun stared at the prawns, drooling...","Wu Guanyue felt as though rain were pouring down before her eyes.","But in any case, she couldn’t afford them.","A bowl of fire-prawn noodles cost two hundred Shenxiao copper coins, while the cheapest five-colored spiritual-root rooms at Yuelai Inn started at three taels of Tongxuan silver, with no upper limit.","The sky gradually darkened. One by one, the lotus lanterns beneath Yuelai Inn’s upturned eaves lit up. The pale glow shining through more than a hundred windows illuminated the bustling building until it resembled a jade palace in the clouds, magnificent beyond compare.","The two of them turned from the main street onto a side road, where there were far fewer people.","Two elegantly dressed people passed them, chatting as they walked.","“Yuelai Inn has a brazier for burning red bi feathers... Let’s stay there for now.”","“All right, all right! I’ve had enough of squeezing into a crowded dormitory up on the mountain! Hurry up—there won’t be any rooms left if we’re late!”","“We’ll practice the Lihuo Heart Formula later. We can’t focus only on enjoying ourselves and neglect our cultivation!”","A pair of outer-sect senior and junior brothers from Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven passed by Wu Guanyue and entered the Welcoming Inn.","Watching them walk away, Lu Datong suddenly let out a sigh. “Comparing yourself to others is enough to drive a man mad...”","A new side quest suddenly appeared before Wu Guanyue.","[Side Quest: Lu Datong’s Troubles]","[Details: Your regular customer, Lu Datong, is also taking part in this Lotus Grand Tournament. He has always been a bold and forthright man, but you’ve noticed that he may not be as confident as he appears. What is troubling him?]","Wu Guanyue looked at him thoughtfully.","Lu Datong noticed her gaze and suddenly smiled. “Little Shopkeeper Wu, don’t get the wrong idea. It’s not that I envy them for being rich. It’s just...”","“That bitch thinks she’s so impressive because her cultivation is high and looks down on the rest of us. What a damn dog! She thinks she can enter the inner sect just because she knows how to cultivate? Dream on!”","“I respect people who work hard at cultivation, but what does that Ye woman mean by looking down her nose at everyone? I’ll put it plainly: if she wants to enter the inner sect, she can forget about it!”","A noisy group suddenly came into the side lane.","Every one of them was dressed in fine silks, though there were naturally different ranks among them. A crowd of young men and women surrounded the young man in their midst. He was drunk and cursing loudly, while the people around him chimed in with insults.","Lu Datong frowned and pulled Wu Guanyue to the side to let them pass. He had no desire to cause trouble.","Who could have imagined that one of them would spot him at a glance?","“Isn’t that Kexin’s opponent?”","The man immediately pointed at Lu Datong and shouted.","The drunken young man being surrounded turned to look. “Really?”","The man who had spoken quickly replied, “Of course! Oh, right, Senior Brother She, he seems to be a servant from Kexin’s family too!”","The drunken young man froze for a moment, then burst out laughing. “Come on, Kexin. Give him a hundred taels of silver and tell him to withdraw on his own!”","The crowd shoved forward, pushing out a timid-looking boy. He was none other than Zhao Kexin, the son of Boss Zhao, owner of the Welcoming Inn.","Lu Datong was not a servant of the Zhao family, nor would he give up the sect tournament for a hundred taels of silver.","This group of wealthy young men and women had seen a poor man and decided to humiliate him, yet their behavior was no different from a pack of dogs barking. Lu Datong’s expression remained impassive. He merely cupped his hands toward Zhao Kexin.","“Young Master.”","Then he said to Wu Guanyue, “Little Shopkeeper Wu, let’s go.”","Unexpectedly, Senior Brother She drawled, “Who said you could leave?”","“Exactly! Exactly! Who do you think you are? Did Senior Brother She give you permission to leave?”","“Kexin, your family servant doesn’t obey orders. What kind of master are you?”","Being humiliated like this in front of his own family’s inn, Zhao Kexin’s face flushed crimson, and he clenched his fists. But how could he possibly have the courage to pick a fight with Young Master Jie?","He suddenly raised his head and glared viciously at Lu Datong before shouting, “Lu Datong! You’re nothing but a... a peasant! My father took pity on you and gave you a living! Do you really think you’re somebody now? I advise you to give up on the sect tournament. You can’t even build your foundation properly, so just be content with earning enough to survive. And you still want to enter the inner sect!”","He paused, then barked, “What are you waiting for? Get over here and apologize to Senior Brother She!”","None."]},{"number":18,"title":"Chapter 18","paragraphs":["It’s starting! It’s starting!","The classic scene from those brain-dead melodramas: the spoiled second-generation rich kid bullying an ordinary person!","Wu Guanyue immediately checked the personal attributes of the group as quickly as she could.","The one who had stepped forward to berate Lu Datong was Zhao Kexin, who was only LV.3—first level of Foundation Establishment. As for the Senior Brother She surrounded by everyone, his name was She Wenjie, and he was LV.5—Foundation Establishment at the Great Perfection stage.","Of course, that wasn’t the important part. The important part was their identities.","There was the grandson of the Pure Wanderer, the nephew of the Swordplay Grandmaster, the daughter of the Violet Cloud Primordial Lord... But the most impressive of all was She Wenjie. His identity was the grandnephew of True Immortal Cuiyun.","Ah, no wonder Zhao Kexin had no status at all among this group. Compared to them, his identity as the Young Master of the Yuelai Inn really was nothing to brag about!","Well... this was probably when the player was supposed to step in, right?","Normally, the ordinary person being bullied would be honest and submissive. Aside from turning beet red, he wouldn’t be able to utter a single word...","Wu Guanyue checked her inventory and prepared to put an end to this melodramatic bullying skit!","Who could have expected that Lu Datong would neither turn red in the face nor be left speechless?","He stared at Zhao Kexin and grew louder and louder, his voice booming like a great bell. “Young Master, we cultivators cultivate our true hearts. Cowering and picking on the weak is hardly anything to be proud of! I, Lu Datong, will tell you this much: if you’ve got a grievance, go to the person who caused it! Now, please move aside!”","With that, he couldn’t even be bothered to spare the shameless little brat another glance. He reached out and shoved him aside.","The principles of this world were actually quite simple. They were right there in people’s hearts. Whoever stood on the side of justice could hold his head high—and it had nothing to do with his identity.","Lu Datong strode away with his head held high, while Zhao Kexin’s face turned red as a fully cooked shrimp.","The young dandies from the immortal sects also looked embarrassed, so they egged him on even more.","“Kexin, you’re just going to take that?!”","“Go on, Kexin! Teach him a lesson!”","“If you can stand it, I certainly can’t!”","Zhao Kexin could endure it no longer. With a strange cry, he drew the treasured sword at his waist. A glint of cold steel flashed as he thrust it toward Lu Datong’s back!","Yet Lu Datong seemed to have eyes in the back of his head!","Clang!","The sword struck the blade of his saber!","With a move called “Taibai Parrying Sword,” Lu Datong blocked the attack. His entire body turned halfway around with the momentum, and with a loud shout, the Eight-Slash Saber in his hand came chopping down toward Zhao Kexin’s head!","How could Zhao Kexin ever have encountered such a deadly move? He was so frightened that he froze, even forgetting to activate his protective qi.","Smack!","That was the sound of Lu Datong’s saber striking Zhao Kexin’s face.","At the last moment, Lu Datong flipped his wrist and used the flat of the blade to give Zhao Kexin a solid slap!","Zhao Kexin’s face had already been red enough, but now an even redder, swollen mark slowly appeared across it. He stood there dumbfounded, seemingly unable to comprehend what had just happened... Yet the burning pain on his cheek wrapped him in an overwhelming sense of humiliation.","Lu Datong couldn’t be bothered with him. He sheathed his saber and walked away.","But—wait! Something was wrong!","A furious light suddenly flashed in the drunken eyes of She Wenjie!","Lu Datong’s refusal to act meek and submissive had clearly reminded him of something—or someone—he found intensely irritating.","From Wu Guanyue’s perspective, the color of the name above his head suddenly changed from yellow, indicating neutrality, to red, indicating hostility!","Not good!","She Wenjie erupted into action, snatching the sword from the person beside him!","How could Lu Datong have expected someone to be so unreasonable? After teaching Zhao Kexin a lesson, he had already sheathed his saber... but a cold glint was already upon him!","She Wenjie moved like rippling waves, his sword singing like a dragon!","Lu Datong shouted and reached for his saber—but he was already a step too late!","She Wenjie’s cultivation was deeper than his. With the richer spiritual energy circulating through him, his speed was naturally faster as well!","However, something was even faster than him: Wu Guanyue’s hand!","The moment she noticed that his name had turned red, Wu Guanyue had already made her move!","[Using Initial Proficiency Skill—Pickpocket!]","Wu Guanyue chose to pickpocket the sword from She Wenjie’s hand!","[Pickpocket failed!]","Given the difference in their levels, failure was only to be expected!","[[Wu Guanyue] gave [Square-Shaped Manure] to [She Wenjie]. May your friendship last forever!]","But that was all right. The instant she used the Pickpocket skill, she had switched to her inventory screen—and then, without a word, stuffed She Wenjie’s hand full of fertilizer!","“Go, Wuyun!” Wu Guanyue shouted. “Charge!”","Wuyun, who had been perched on top of her head the whole time, let out a series of yowling meows and pounced forward!","Wu Guanyue’s Pickpocket skill could generate an enormous amount of momentum. Wuyun itself was a pitch-black clump of aquatic weeds that moved with incredible speed. The fact that it could carry someone as large as Wu Guanyue and still run so quickly was proof enough of its astonishing velocity!","A clump of black aquatic weeds shot forward like lightning and slammed into She Wenjie’s hand before his sword could pierce Lu Datong!","Everyone knew that a swordsman’s hand had to be clean and dry when gripping a sword. Otherwise, the sword would slip...","This was true not only in the real world, but in the world of cultivation as well!","Sliiip!","The sword flew out of She Wenjie’s hand!","She Wenjie stared dumbfounded at his own hand.","Lu Datong stared dumbfounded at that hand... and at the smug little Shopkeeper Wu!","The change had happened so quickly—and was so bizarre—that She Wenjie hadn’t even processed it yet. His hand was sticky. His hand was sticky with... with... with something that seemed to be...","“Ah! Senior Brother, your hand has—mmph!”","“Shut up! Don’t say it!”","She Wenjie: “...”","She Wenjie: “......”","She Wenjie let out an enraged roar. “You! How dare you—!”","“Wuyun! Charge, charge, charge, charge!!! Lu Datong, bear with me for a second! Just bear with me!!!”","Standing on one leg atop that clump of black aquatic weeds, Wu Guanyue grabbed Lu Datong and hoisted him high over her head!!!","Ha! She wasn’t going to get tangled up with these dandies and their powerful backgrounds. Hit them, then run! Time to make her escape!","“Meow meow meow meow meow—!”","Wuyun sprinted wildly on all four paws. With two people riding on its back, its body had been flattened into something resembling a long-haired rug, yet it still moved so fast that afterimages trailed behind it. With a whoosh, it carried them out of sight!","In the side alley beside the Yuelai Inn, the fading afterimage of a young girl standing on one leg while holding a burly man overhead seemed to linger in the air.","She Wenjie roared furiously, “Stop! Stop right there—!!”","“Senior Brother, calm down! Wipe it off first! Wipe it off!”","“I’ll put a Cleansing Talisman on Senior Brother—!”","Wuyun had been carrying Wu Guanyue and Lu Datong with the intention of running all the way back to Qihua Road, but Lu Datong kept insisting that they stop and let him down.","There was nothing for it. Wu Guanyue had to put him down halfway there.","“Lu Datong, don’t you think this is much faster?”","Lu Datong: “......”","He cupped his hands and said solemnly, “Little Shopkeeper Wu, I owe you one today. If you hadn’t been there, I’d have been in serious trouble when that bastard suddenly lost his mind!”","Wu Guanyue declared righteously, “It’s nothing! I’m here to set the world straight!”","Lu Datong: “............?”","But then he thought about Little Shopkeeper Wu’s move... Well, it hadn’t done much damage, but the humiliation had been devastating. Unfortunately, not many people had witnessed it. Otherwise, She Wenjie would probably be known for a long time as “the guy who had a handful of manure shoved into his hand.”","At the thought, Lu Datong suddenly burst out laughing.","But... why exactly did Little Shopkeeper Wu carry so much manure in her storage pouch? And she ran an inn and sold food, too...","Lu Datong: “............”","The gap-toothed grin vanished from his face at once.","He earnestly advised her, “Little Shopkeeper Wu... Don’t use that move when there are a lot of people around in the future... It’s bad for the inn’s reputation...”","Indeed, it was bad for the inn’s reputation... because Wu Guanyue discovered that her inn’s popularity had dropped by one.","It was Lu Datong! Lu Datong had figured out something he absolutely should not have figured out!","Ahaha... Ahaha...","Forget it. There was no point dwelling on that. It was time to investigate the side quest.","Wu Guanyue asked, “Why did Zhao Kexin say you can’t even build your foundation properly?”","Lu Datong was clearly a higher level than Zhao Kexin—he was LV.4.","Lu Datong was silent for a moment before saying, “I came from a minor sect, so my fundamentals were shaky. I’m not precise enough in controlling spiritual energy, and my foundation platform has never been perfect... Zhao Kexin is nothing special, but She Wenjie is far stronger than me.”","At that, he seemed somewhat unhappy.","However, he quickly waved his hand and said, “Little Shopkeeper Wu, I still have things to do, so I’ll be off. See you around!”","Lu Datong cupped his hands toward her and strode away.","Wu Guanyue held Wuyun in her arms and stared thoughtfully at his retreating figure.","After a while, she turned her thoughtful gaze toward Wuyun.","Wuyun: OωO","Wu Guanyue asked, “Wuyun, did you get manure stuck in your fur?”","Wuyun: “............”","Wuyun: ◣ω◢","Wuyun suddenly became angry.","***","The side quest could wait for now. The most important thing was figuring out how to complete the main quest.","Wu Guanyue’s little inn had only five guest rooms in total. Completing the “impossible to find a room” requirement in the quest description should have been fairly easy...","But this concerned Wu Guanyue’s paralyzed legs. There was no way she could treat the matter so flippantly!","The system required the inn to reach at least LV.4 during the Lotus Tournament. Increasing the inn’s level required sufficient revenue and popularity. Her current level was LV.2, and killing Daoist Master Songfeng had brought her another increase in popularity. Her current popularity was (508/1,000).","The popularity requirement for Level Four was 100,000...","That was basically equivalent to making sure everyone in Meishan City had heard of her inn.","It was practically a mission demanding that someone ascend to the heavens in a single bound...","Wu Guanyue’s brows furrowed tightly as she came back to her senses from the ecstatic joy of having a pie fall from the sky.","So the quest description wasn’t wrong. If she wanted to become a famous inn known throughout the city within a single quarter, she had to ride the Lotus Tournament’s popularity wave as hard as she could!","Ride it for all it was worth!","Clearly, the Yuelai Inn, the Xihua Old Inn, and every other inn in the city had come to the same conclusion... They had all begun offering guest rooms that could assist with cultivation.","So how could she stand out among all those specialized rooms?","Wu Guanyue fell into deep thought.","Wuyun was drenched from head to toe. It had just finished washing all its fur and was now crouching on the floor, shaking itself vigorously and spraying water droplets everywhere.","Wu Guanyue glanced at Wuyun.","Hmm. Wuyun was a mirage beast... What were the defining traits of a mirage beast...?","Wu Guanyue pulled out her bestiary and began looking through it.","[Mirage Beast: Capable of creating extremely realistic illusions and luring cultivators who stumble into them into exhausting all their spiritual energy... Their cultivation increases precisely by relying on this process. A rather evil and rare type of demonic beast.]","Hmm? Wait a moment. Why did this description sound so familiar?","Huh?! Wasn’t this basically a game developer?","Game developers could create extremely realistic environments and lure players who wandered in to grind until midnight... Their income increased precisely by relying on this, making them a rather evil and rare type of demonic beast!","Wait!","Didn’t that mean that if she could get Wuyun to create a game that was both educational and entertaining, one that could help cultivators improve their cultivation, then the inn’s popularity would shoot up like a rocket?!","FPS games helped train hand-eye coordination... So, in the immortal cultivation world, using games to improve one’s precision in controlling spiritual energy was theoretically entirely possible!","Wu Guanyue stared at the kitten shaking out its fur.","Wuyun: ◣ω◢","Wu Guanyue’s voice turned sweet and syrupy. “Wuyun, you’re the cutest little kitty in the whole wide world~~~~~”","Wuyun: OωO!","Oh no! She was up to something!","No..."]},{"number":19,"title":"Chapter 19","paragraphs":["The very next instant after Wu Guanyue made that outrageous request of Wuyun, the game displayed a system notification—","[Unlocked: Built-in Minigame!]","[Built-in Minigame: Want to play a round of Gwent? How about a game of Tavern Brawl? Or perhaps an exhilarating round of Zhunimo Racing? None of those are available! So, what will your built-in minigame be...?]","[Unlocked: Game Room!]","[Game Room: Place Wuyun inside a guest room, and the guest room will automatically be upgraded into a game room. Guests can play your built-in minigame inside!]","Wow! It really worked?!","[What kind of built-in minigame would you like to design?]","[(Enter manually)]","Hmm...","After thinking it over, Wu Guanyue wrote down her answer.","[Dark Souls III]","[............]","The game’s system notification was actually just a long string of ellipses.","[What kind of built-in minigame would you like to design? (Please describe your requirements in detail)]","Wu Guanyue spoke with perfect clarity and fluency. “I hope to design a game that will greatly train cultivators’ agility, powers of observation, and indomitable spirit! Of course, more importantly, after playing my game, everyone should become hopelessly addicted and develop an inexplicable attachment to me... Ahem, I mean, to the inn! In the end, I’ll be drowned beneath a mountain of money and popularity points!”","[............]","The game’s system notification once again produced a long string of ellipses.","But this time, it did not ask her to start over.","[Analyzing requirements...]","[Generating game...]","[Acquired: Cat Mario ×1!]","[Cat Mario: A side-scrolling platform game beloved by players around the world... Well, it should still be beloved, right?]","Wu Guanyue: “............?”","A question mark slowly appeared above Wu Guanyue’s head.","...Why Cat Mario?","Cat Mario differed from Mario by only a single character in its name, but the actual gaming experience was worlds apart...","In simple terms, Cat Mario was a game of torment—a pure game of torment that had transcended all lowly pleasures!","Whenever you jumped upward, there was a high chance you’d smack your head on a hidden block and die. Whenever you passed a pipe, there was a high chance some strange creature would spring out and bite you to death. Even if you managed to land safely, the ground might suddenly collapse beneath you and kill you.","In short, unless you died at least a hundred times, you could forget about ever reaching the finish line!","Um... Would people from an immortal cultivation world really enjoy something like this...?","Wu Guanyue fell deep into thought.","But since this was cultivation, tempering one’s Dao heart through the frustration of dying countless times was probably necessary... right?","She couldn’t keep making excuses for it. ORZ...","Still, this was the only game Wu Guanyue had acquired. Even after she kneaded and fussed over Wuyun again and again, the minigame design process had already ended...","Wuyun was filled with fighting spirit. He raised his little paw, and the pink pads on it slowly spread open like blooming flowers.","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Pretending that she, too, was filled with fighting spirit, Wu Guanyue raised her fist.","Excellent! Very spirited!","At that very moment, a pine sapling was growing in the inn’s rear courtyard.","This was no ordinary pine tree. It had grown from the inner elixir of a Seven-Treasure Pine.","When Wu Guanyue saw the words “Seven-Treasure Pine,” she had not reacted in the slightest. But in truth, if anyone else had heard that name—Wenren Ying, Lu Datong, She Wenjie... even Verdant Cloud Adept—not a single one of them would have remained unmoved.","That was because the Seven-Treasure Pine had once been one of the treasures belonging to Sword Lord Taibai.","Sword Lord Taibai had once been the sect master of the Profound Heaven Sect on Yuntai Peak. He was a hero who had sacrificed himself to suppress the great demon Hundred-Eyed Demon Lord. The place where he had suppressed that great evil creature was said to lie among the countless mountains of Mount Mei.","The Seven-Treasure Pine itself possessed the power to revive the dead and restore flesh to bare bones.","That was also why, despite having his inner elixir ripped out, he had still managed to preserve a fragment of his soul and transform into this tiny sapling.","At that moment, Daoist Master Songfeng’s consciousness was gradually returning...","The bone-deep hatred remained buried within his heart. All that hatred had transformed into a yearning—a pure and simple yearning—","I want to bloom!!! I want to sprout!!!","He had suffered such grievous injuries! Who knew how many years it would take him to recover!","And Wu Guanyue poured a ladleful of fertilizer over his head every single day...","He had to leave this place as soon as possible... He absolutely had to leave this place as soon as possible...","He needed to find someone to rescue him...!","Daoist Master Songfeng used the very last trace of spiritual energy in his entire body to send out a distress signal.","The tiny pine sapling began to sway despite the absence of wind. Suddenly, a streak of white light shot out from between its branches and vanished into the night over Mount Mei.","The streak of white light flew higher and farther, all the way to distant Yuntai Peak. It plunged into the mist-shrouded Profound Heaven Sect and landed in the hand of Perfected Renhua, Yan Shouyi.","Perfected Renhua was a blood relative of Sword Lord Taibai and one of the five great elders of the Profound Heaven Sect. The master of Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven, Verdant Cloud Adept, belonged to the generation below him.","Perfected Renhua glanced at the streak of white light and frowned.","The Seven-Treasure Pine had taken human form. Who knew what kind of trouble it had gotten itself into?","Forget it... After all, it was a treasure left behind by Sword Lord Taibai. He should bring it back safely.","Yunsheng and Yingfeng could make the trip.","His fingers moved slightly, and two streaks of white light flew out from the grotto-heaven, heading in two different directions.","One of them flew toward a small town plagued by demonic cultivators.","Chu Yingfeng stood there.","He was a pale young man dressed in black, standing utterly motionless like a sculpture untouched by the passage of time.","He was watching the fish in the stream... He watched them with such concentration that it seemed nothing in the world could stir his heart.","The sun gradually sank toward the horizon, bathing the sky in blood-red light.","From the dense forest behind him, someone suddenly emerged in complete silence.","The man was tall and powerfully built, yet his concealment technique was excellent. When his feet touched the ground, he made even less sound than a mysterious leopard from the Hidden Netherlands.","When the man saw Chu Yingfeng’s back, an utterly terrifying hatred flickered through his eyes.","Suddenly, he attacked!","More than a dozen streaks of bloody light shot toward Chu Yingfeng’s back. At the same time, from among the branches above Chu Yingfeng’s head, more than a dozen multicolored, foul-smelling winds pounced down upon him!","The bloody light was no light at all, but blood pests capable of sucking a person dry in an instant. And the foul-smelling winds were no winds either, but Mangshan pit vipers with poison potent enough to kill on contact!","Both of these things could kill without a sound in an instant. They were the reason so many people in the town had died—the demonic cultivator possessed both of these deadly treasures!","Chu Yingfeng was surrounded!","The bloody light and venomous winds completely enveloped him. Even the slightest contact—even the tiniest graze—would be enough to kill him. Even as a disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect, he would never survive this day!","Yet, within the bloody light and venomous winds, ten thousand points of sword light suddenly burst forth!","The countless sword rays resembled silver blossoms and waves of snow. From within the great ring formed by the interweaving blood and venomous wind came a terrifying sound of flesh and blood being torn apart.","In the next instant, the sword light had already reached the demonic cultivator’s eyes!","The demonic cultivator’s pupils had shrunk to pinpoints with terror!","The sword light abruptly halted, stopping right before his eyes. Its bone-chilling cold seemed to have pierced straight through his eyeballs.","Yet even colder than the sword’s aura were Chu Yingfeng’s dark eyes, frozen with ice.","Staring at him, Chu Yingfeng said coldly, “Didn’t I tell you not to use the same tricks against me?”","His voice was hoarse and low, like a rusted blade being drawn from its sheath.","A bead of cold sweat slowly emerged from the tip of the demonic cultivator’s nose.","His lips trembled as he murmured, “You... you did...”","“Didn’t I also tell you that if you used a move I’d already seen against me, I would kill you?”","Cold sweat had already soaked through the demonic cultivator’s back.","Suddenly, he could no longer hold himself up. He fell to his knees and begged for mercy. “Please spare me, Immortal Master! Please spare me! I’ve already used everything I know, yet I still couldn’t defeat you. Please, Immortal Master, let me live!”","Chu Yingfeng studied him with great concentration, his gaze no different from the one he had cast upon that fish moments ago.","His wrist turned slightly, and the sword light illuminated his eyes.","A short while later, a young disciple of the Xuantian Sect hurried over.","He was holding something in his hands. Approaching respectfully, he said, “Senior Brother Chu, a letter from the Elder.”","Chu Yingfeng reached out to accept it. As he lowered his head to read, a lock of black hair slipped down, making his face appear especially pale.","The Elder... wanted him to go to Mount Mei and investigate the matter of the Seven-Treasure Pine.","...Another tedious task. He did not know whether it would be enough to stir his interest.","Chu Yingfeng said nothing and slowly walked away.","Only after that oppressive presence had receded into the distance did the young disciple’s rigid back gradually relax.","Unable to resist, he turned to look at Chu Yingfeng’s departing figure.","Senior Brother Chu... a once-in-a-century genius within the sect.","He was too gifted, making him the foremost disciple of his generation. He was so gifted that after seeing any technique just once, he could use it freely himself.","The young disciple glanced at the demonic cultivator’s gruesomely mutilated corpse nearby and could not help shivering.","And precisely because he was too gifted, everything he saw seemed to him to be without challenge or difficulty... That was why he had developed this bad habit of toying with his prey.","None."]},{"number":20,"title":"Chapter 20","paragraphs":["***","Even developing a minigame within a game couldn’t make it succeed with a “whoosh!” in an instant.","On Wu Guanyue’s list of hired workers, Wuyun’s status had changed to [In Development, Please Don’t Rush].","Er... why does this suddenly feel so much like a day job?","Whatever. She would just leave it at that for now!","Before the game was finished, Wu Guanyue naturally still had plenty of daily activities to grind through.","For example, she needed to order furniture from [Carpenter Zhang Wulang].","To open the guest rooms to customers, she had to place the four basic pieces of furniture: a [Wooden Bed], [Wooden Cabinet], [Wooden Table], and [Wooden Chair]. The bed and cabinet were large items and therefore relatively expensive. Beds cost four taels each, while cabinets cost five taels apiece.","However, when Wu Guanyue had previously ordered tables, chairs, and benches for the main hall, she had already ordered some wooden beds. She could go pick them up now, while the cabinets could be replaced with wooden chests. After all, the point was simply to give guests somewhere to put their belongings!","That brought the cost down considerably.","After grinding away for several days and selling some unneeded items at the pawnshop, Wu Guanyue finally managed to gather enough basic furniture for all five guest rooms.","She opened [Build Mode] and began decorating the rooms!","She put the bed on the east side... then moved it to the west... and finally put it on the south side...","Wu Guanyue: “............”","There were only a few pieces of furniture to begin with. It didn’t seem necessary to fuss over them so meticulously...","Once the decorating was complete, she received the guest rooms’ initial rating!","Thus, the rooms received their first-ever evaluation.","[Rating: ★☆☆☆☆]","[Evaluation: Simple and ordinary guest rooms. Every now and then, a porter working in the city might come stay for a night.]","It was an extremely low rating, to put it mildly...","Of course, Wu Guanyue’s core competitive advantage didn’t lie in the guest rooms.","But then again, would Cat Mario... er... really work?","Forget it. She would grind through some other quests first!","The Chronicles of Running a Xianxia Inn had no dead season. Every day, there were countless things waiting for players to do!","Go to the kitchen to prepare dishes, open the doors for business, set the inn to automatic management, head to the backyard and give the Seven-Treasure Pine a spoonful of fertilizer, go to the outskirts of the city to chop trees and gather flowers and other resources... and finally, never forget to visit the important characters and raise their affection levels!","With a loud bang, Wu Guanyue swaggered into Wenren Ying’s home!","Naturally, Wenren Ying’s front door was firmly locked, but that didn’t matter. The player’s affection level with him had already reached three hearts.","The game’s affection system was highly similar to Stardew Valley’s. Once affection reached two hearts, the player and the NPC were considered friends, and the player could freely enter the NPC’s room!","And Wu Guanyue and Wenren Ying were, of course, already friends!!!","Their friendship had been forged after the Battle of Huiming Mountain. That exhilarating battle had allowed Wu Guanyue to witness his magnificent and brutally violent fighting style, while it had shown Wenren Ying how fast and nimble Wu Guanyue could react in an emergency.","These were undoubtedly qualities one could admire, and at the time, his affection for her had risen to... two hearts.","Er...","He really was stingy.","But then again, when Wenren Ying had run around investigating matters on her behalf and joined her on Huiming Mountain without a second thought, his affection level had only been half a heart.","Half a heart was enough to make someone go that far for another person?","In a certain sense, he was actually a remarkably generous man.","At that very moment, the generous Wenren Ying was sitting in his little courtyard, slowly wiping down his blade with a cloth.","Wu Guanyue walked in with an expressionless face and handed him a golden deutzia blossom.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying hesitated for a moment before tactfully saying, “Little Shopkeeper Wu, thank you for coming to see me. But could you please stop picking the lock to get into my house?”","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","Wu Guanyue’s eyes flew wide open, and she stared at him as if she couldn’t believe what she had just heard!","Wenren Ying: “............?”","Her expression shifted several times, and she stood there looking somewhat dazed.","Finally, she drew a notebook from her sleeve and began writing in it with a stiff expression.","“Wenren Ying... doesn’t like... me... coming to his house with gifts...”","She left with a faintly aggrieved look.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","For some inexplicable reason, Wenren Ying suddenly felt a little guilty... and began shifting restlessly in his seat.","Wu Guanyue, however, quickly forgot all about the incident. After all, completing the main quest was far more important than raising affection!","At present, she was standing outside a teahouse.","The teahouse was bustling with people coming and going, and the noise was deafening. Yet no matter whose voice it was, none could overpower the sharp crack of the storyteller’s clapper.","Of course, a storyteller in a xianxia world wouldn’t be talking about the Three Kingdoms or Water Margin. He would be telling tales of the various sects, as well as the most fashionable topic of the moment: the Lotus Tournament.","Today, the storyteller was recounting the tale of a swordsman who had climbed to the summit in his pursuit of the Dao.","He had not been born into a prestigious family, nor had he come from wealth. His parents were merely a menial worker and a cook employed at an inn. If nothing unexpected had happened, he would have grown up to be an entirely ordinary young man.","But then, an accident occurred.","A group of spoiled young disciples from an immortal sect got drunk at the inn. After an argument, they began fighting. When cultivators clashed, how could ordinary people withstand it? The young man’s father, a menial worker, had his bones crushed throughout his body by the force of spiritual energy and died on the spot.","When the boy found out, he did not say a word.","But the next time that group of spoiled disciples came to the inn, the boy carried a butcher’s knife upstairs, chopped off the head of the culprit, and tossed it from the third floor down to the first as if he were throwing a flower ball.","Afterward, he sat down in the middle of the inn’s main hall and ate and drank to his heart’s content, waiting for someone to come arrest him.","As it happened, Perfected Renhua of the Profound Heaven Sect passed by the area at that very moment. Moved by the boy’s fierce determination to avenge his father and astonished by his once-in-a-thousand-years spiritual aptitude, he took the boy and his widowed mother back to the Profound Heaven Sect. The boy then became Perfected Renhua’s final disciple.","It was said that he was not yet a hundred years old, yet had already reached the pinnacle of the Golden Core realm and would soon step into the Xiantian realm.","His name was Chu Yingfeng.","Though Chu Yingfeng was still young, his seniority was astonishingly high. He was actually of the same generation as Verdant Cloud Adept, Lord of Meishan. Truly, he was a peerless genius!","However, there seemed to be something extreme in Chu Yingfeng’s personality. The way he killed people was practically more sinister than that of an evil cultivator. It was said that on one occasion, he had butchered an evil cultivator like a master chef dissecting an ox... slicing the flesh thinner than roast duck!","The reason he was so extreme was precisely because he had no equal.","“Does everyone know that Chu Yingfeng, that unorthodox disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect, has arrived at Meishan?”","“What?! Is that true?”","A wave of astonishment swept through the teahouse.","The storyteller shook his head and swayed from side to side as he continued, “Naturally, he’s here to watch the Lotus Tournament. Those of you taking part in the competition must be sure to bring glory to our Meishan... Speaking of this year’s Lotus Tournament, the outer disciples of Verdant Cloud Grotto Heaven...”","The storyteller was about to move on to introducing the contestants, but the audience wasn’t interested in that at all. They clamored for him to say more about Chu Yingfeng.","Hmm...","Wu Guanyue pondered this.","He seemed to be quite a prominent figure... He was probably a story character who had some connection to the player, right? After all, the player was the center of the world. Even if they went out and encountered a dog, that dog ought to be the beloved pet lost by some high-ranking official!","However, she hadn’t come to the teahouse today to listen to storytelling. She had come to find the storyteller—to buy an advertisement!","Advertisements were great. Advertisements were wonderful. Last time, it was because she’d hired two wandering cultivators to perform a live-action Jinkela commercial outside her inn that she’d made a name for herself!","This time, she planned to do the same thing again.","If she wanted her reputation to spread throughout Meishan City, putting on live-action commercials only on Qihua Road clearly wouldn’t be enough. So she had come to Meishan City’s center of public opinion to find the biggest self-media influencer in this xianxia world!","At that moment, the storyteller finished his tale.","Wu Guanyue walked over and began interacting with him.","[Silver-Tongued Wu (polite smile): “I hear you wanted to speak with me? Please, go ahead.”]","Wu Guanyue: “Yes. I’d like you to promote the new game rooms at our inn!”","Whether or not people liked Cat Mario, as long as she could get the message out that “The Inn With the Ridiculously Long Name Nobody Can Be Bothered to Read Has Something New,” she could still gain popularity points!","After all, popularity points were calculated based on “how many people know about the inn,” not “how many people approve of the inn.”","This was the player’s path to self-rescue!","[Silver-Tongued Wu (polite smile): “Certainly, certainly. I have a price list right here. Would you like a straightforward advertisement, or would you prefer me to weave your guest rooms into a story and promote them subtly, like rain nourishing the earth?”]","Wu Guanyue: “The subtle one!”","[Silver-Tongued Wu (polite smile): “Ten taels of silver.”]","Wu Guanyue: “...”","So expensive!","She had just gone completely broke buying furniture. Even if she sold the player, she couldn’t scrape together ten taels of Tongxuan silver right now!","Maybe subtle advertising cost more because it required writing a story?","Wu Guanyue: “Then let’s do the straightforward kind!”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “Ten taels of silver.”","Wu Guanyue: “...”","Wu Guanyue: “Can’t you make it a little cheaper...?”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “I’m afraid not, Shopkeeper. I have a whole family to support too, you know~”","Wu Guanyue: “Why don’t you come and try it for free? If you find it interesting, then...”","Silver-Tongued Wu cut her off with a hearty laugh.","“All right, all right. Really, if you don’t have the money, why are you trying to buy an advertisement? You don’t need this right now. Just focus on running your inn, all right?”","Silver-Tongued Wu was a pure, money-minded businessman, someone who had completely abandoned all higher pursuits. One look at this young girl, and he could tell she couldn’t afford the fee. Her inn was on Qihua Road too... What kind of godforsaken place was that?","Instead of wasting time haggling with her, he might as well gather more stories about Chu Yingfeng. That was what the audience actually liked listening to!","Silver-Tongued Wu gave a perfunctory laugh and left.","Wu Guanyue’s attempt at self-rescue had failed, and she left as well, all fluffy and dejected...","However, not long after she returned to the inn, someone walked in from outside.","He was a pale young man dressed in black. Standing in the doorway, he stared at the inn’s signboard with a pair of pitch-black eyes. Even after noticing the densely packed little characters on it, his expression did not change in the slightest.","The setting sun illuminated his face, emphasizing the hard lines of his jaw and the air of coldness and inhuman detachment about him.","And the name floating above his head was...","Chu Yingfeng!","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","Sure enough, he was an important story character! Speak of the devil, and he appears! The player really was the center of the world!","Wu Guanyue was in an excellent mood. She greeted him with a bright smile.","“Welcome, esteemed guest. Are you here for a meal, or would you like a room?”","Chu Yingfeng’s gaze slowly settled on her face, studying her as though he were examining her very carefully.","Only after a moment did he speak in his unhurried voice.","“I’m here to ask about someone.”","“Mhm, who are you looking for?”","“Daoist Master Songfeng.”","The instant those words fell, a new side quest suddenly appeared before Wu Guanyue’s eyes!","[Quest · Side Story: Every Footprint Leaves a Trace]","[Quest Details: When you killed Daoist Master Songfeng, you probably never imagined that someone would come looking for you... The genius swordsman Chu Yingfeng of the Xuantian Sect is searching for Daoist Master Songfeng. How will you conceal the traces you left behind?]","He was a hidden red-name character!!!","Wu Guanyue was utterly stunned. This red-name character was the highest-level one she had seen so far—an entire LV.8... Wasn’t this game’s difficulty getting a little ridiculous?!","No, she had to find a way to keep him calm!","Chu Yingfeng stared at the young shopkeeper before him with a pair of pitch-black eyes, utterly devoid of emotion. No one knew what he was thinking.","The shopkeeper had round eyes. Suddenly, she smiled at him, revealing two tiny dimples.","“Daoist Master Songfeng? I’ve never heard of him! But I can help you ask around... Oh, that’s right. Our inn has game rooms where you can try a high-difficulty side-scrolling platformer. No one has managed to clear it yet. Would you like to give it a try, guest?”","Chu Yingfeng narrowed his eyes slightly.","High difficulty...?","The aura of the Qibao Pine was indeed nearby... Could this “game room” be a trap?","But...","That was exactly what he wanted.","He would see whether this person could finally make things interesting enough that he wouldn’t be bored.","Chu Yingfeng stared at Wu Guanyue and slowly nodded.","“I’ll take a room.”","The next chapter will be out at midnight! It’s a big one, so don’t miss it~"]},{"number":21,"title":"Chapter 21","paragraphs":["***","Chu Yingfeng walked up the inn’s stairs.","The shopkeeper walked ahead of him, the two braids at her sides bouncing up and down. The black cat perched motionless atop her head, its tail swaying in time with her steps.","Chu Yingfeng’s eyes, dark and gleaming as lacquered stars, quietly watched that long, black tail, as though he were studying it with great concentration.","The inn was old. Every step on the stairs sent dust drifting down.","The guest room was just as worn and spartan. A wooden bed stood against the western wall, and aside from it, the room contained nothing more than a table and a stool. There was not even a teapot on the table. No one knew how long it had been since anyone had stayed here.","Chu Yingfeng did not care about such things. In truth, there were very few things he cared about at all.","He stood in the middle of the room, looking down at the shopkeeper without moving.","The shopkeeper picked up the cat from her head and set it on the table. The black, long-haired lion of a cat sat upright with perfect dignity, its eyes wide as copper bells and its tail beating incessantly against the tabletop.","Wu Guanyue: “Wuyun, do your best!”","Wuyun let out a suspicious noise. “Gwooo gurg?”","Wu Guanyue: “......”","Wu Guanyue looked doubtful. “...Is making a noise like that a bad sign?”","Wuyun: “Meow meow meow meow meow!”","Wuyun once again produced a voice brimming with fighting spirit! Suddenly, great clouds of white mist began billowing from its body, as though it were a pot of water coming to a boil.","Wu Guanyue turned and smiled at Chu Yingfeng, speaking in a honey-sweet voice. “All right, honored guest. We’re about to begin...”","Chu Yingfeng stared at her expressionlessly. He clearly saw a sly glimmer flash through her almond-shaped, round eyes...but he did nothing.","So it was about to begin?","He was actually rather curious to see how she intended to deal with him.","If he had guessed correctly, this dark mass of seaweed before him was actually a mirage beast.","Mirage beasts were descendants of dragons. Ancient texts said that when Nuwa led the gods to the Ninth Heaven, Zhulong, the progenitor of dragons, ascended with them. Without their dragon ancestor to preside over it, the Dragon Kingdom of Mount Zhong gradually declined and vanished over the course of several thousand years. The dragon’s descendants disappeared along with it. Nowadays, only two dragon bloodlines still left any trace of their existence: the jiaolong and the mirage beast.","Jiaolong loved to whip up wind and waves, while mirage beasts loved to create illusions.","It was said that when people sailed across the sea, they would sometimes glimpse distant immortal mountains. Travelers crossing deserts might occasionally see oases far away. Those illusory mountains and oases were the work of mirage beasts.","Once a person entered a mirage beast’s illusion, the beast would lure them into exhausting every last bit of spiritual energy in their body. In the end, they would die of exhaustion—and the refined spiritual energy processed through their spiritual core would become nourishment for the mirage beast’s cultivation.","There was no doubt that this was a dangerous and evil creature. Yet Chu Yingfeng made no move. He simply allowed the white mist to engulf him.","The inn before his eyes was...well, still an inn. Only now, a...water screen had appeared before him.","Images gradually emerged across the screen.","They were bizarre images—not lifelike in the slightest, nor vivid. The sky was represented by one enormous expanse of unchanging sky blue, while the bricks were depicted as a single unvarying strip of brown.","Even someone whose hands had been chopped off and who was forced to draw with their feet could have produced something better.","...Was this really a mirage created by a mirage beast? Did it not feel embarrassed?","Three elegant little characters slowly appeared on the water screen:","Cat Mario.","At the very edge of the brick path stood a...cat...standing upright on two legs.","This was...Cat Mario?","Chu Yingfeng coldly locked eyes with the ugly upright cat, inexplicably finding it irritating.","Cat Mario: (=??ω??=)","Wu Guanyue’s voice rang out at just the right moment. “Honored guest, try focusing your mind and infusing it with spiritual energy!”","Chu Yingfeng narrowed his eyes.","He did, in fact, try injecting a thin thread of spiritual energy into the water screen.","Suddenly, Cat Mario moved!","It turned out that he could use spiritual energy to control Cat Mario, making him move forward and jump.","This was indeed a novel experience for Chu Yingfeng. He had never seen anything like it before, and it made him pay slightly more attention.","Ahead of Cat Mario, several white balls were moving toward him. A number of platforms floated in midair as well. Although Chu Yingfeng was an ancient man who had never encountered a side-scrolling platform game, he possessed the intelligence of a normal human being, and thus reached his conclusions with ease.","The platforms could be used as footholds, while the white balls were his enemies. However, Cat Mario could only move forward and jump; he could not attack.","Chu Yingfeng possessed a strong desire to attack and disliked dodging whenever possible. So he tried jumping on one of the white balls. Sure enough, he stomped it to death.","...That felt good.","Chu Yingfeng proceeded comfortably, stomping three white balls along the way. He climbed onto one platform suspended in midair, then continued forward until he reached a green, pillar-shaped object.","Chu Yingfeng could not be bothered to figure out what it was and simply walked forward as usual.","...A white ghost suddenly shot out of the pillar and collided with him, killing him.","He returned to the starting point.","Chu Yingfeng narrowed his eyes.","So the green pillar was a trap.","Chu Yingfeng remained perfectly calm and started over.","After passing the trap, he found a broad, level road ahead. At the end of the road was a cliff, with an identical stretch of road on the other side.","Since Chu Yingfeng possessed the normal intelligence of a normal human being, he knew that he was supposed to jump here.","...That was it?","He was already beginning to feel bored.","Although this sort of “game” was certainly something he had never encountered before, he did not find it particularly interesting or difficult.","He guided Cat Mario forward and jumped at precisely the right moment—","...He died.","There was a hidden brick directly above the spot where he had jumped. His head struck it, sending him straight down into the ravine.","He returned to the starting point.","...So Cat Mario also had hidden traps like this.","Chu Yingfeng remained perfectly calm and started over.","This time, when he reached the same spot, he naturally did not make the same mistake. Since there might be hidden bricks above him, he would jump earlier and reveal them all in advance.","With that thought, Chu Yingfeng jumped again—","...He did not die.","—But some people may be alive in body while already dead inside.","He had guessed correctly: there were indeed more hidden bricks above him. Yet the moment he struck them, they spat out countless poisonous mushrooms, completely clogging the path ahead!","Chu Yingfeng: “......”","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","...He died.","He returned to the starting point.","He felt the first stirrings of torment.","Veins bulged across Chu Yingfeng’s pale hands, twisted roots buried beneath frozen soil.","This time, Chu Yingfeng became truly serious.","***","Chu Yingfeng had become serious, but Wu Guanyue was the one who was shocked!","She had originally planned to take advantage of Chu Yingfeng’s attention being absorbed by Cat Mario and carefully investigate the side-quest area. But when she opened the quest interface, she accidentally opened the favorability interface instead.","And then she discovered that Chu Yingfeng’s favorability... had actually gone up by one heart!","Wu Guanyue: “???”","Wu Guanyue: “??????”","Question-mark bubbles kept popping above Wu Guanyue’s head.","Good heavens! How could anyone playing Cat Mario not only avoid losing their mind and flying into a rage, but also develop extra feelings for the person responsible for it?!","Wu Guanyue fell into deep thought...","Hmm...","Still, this increase in favorability did give Wu Guanyue a few other ideas.","If the player became friends with him, perhaps she could obtain more information from him and complete the side quest more effectively?","Not bad, not bad. This was indeed a viable method! Given how outstanding Chu Yingfeng’s character model was, players could reasonably assume that he was someone with whom an important relationship could be developed!","Just as she was thinking this, the sound of someone coming downstairs drifted over from the stairwell. It turned out to be Chu Yingfeng, carrying Wuyun downstairs.","Chu Yingfeng stared at Wu Guanyue with his pitch-black eyes. “It’s stuck.”","Wuyun lay limply across Chu Yingfeng’s shoulder, turning itself into a long feline scarf.","It weakly mewed, “Meow... ugh... meow...”","Wu Guanyue listened carefully to Wuyun’s explanation, then solemnly raised her head and explained to Chu Yingfeng, “Wuyun says it can’t eat another bite.”","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng: “..................”","Oh... Mirage beasts grew their cultivation by absorbing the pure spiritual energy of others. This particular mirage beast was still very young, so it couldn’t absorb very much.","Chu Yingfeng stared at Wuyun.","Wuyun, having eaten itself sick, was draped over him and dry-heaving.","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng: “............Extend the room.”","He took a silver ingot from inside his robe and slowly placed it on the counter.","Wu Guanyue slowly tucked the silver ingot into her pocket, then slowly took a golden potentilla flower from her robes and held it out to him.","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng neither moved nor accepted it. He simply stared at her expressionlessly.","...Did he not like it?","Of course, that was perfectly normal. Golden potentilla was merely the most ordinary flower one could pick up by the roadside, while Chu Yingfeng was an important NPC in a side quest—and, according to the game’s overall setting, he was also a legendary figure.","To win over someone as remarkable as him, one naturally had to identify his preferences and cater to his tastes!","So then... what did Chu Yingfeng like?","Everything left a trace. Since the game had provided a way to raise favorability, there had to be clues hidden somewhere!","Wu Guanyue furrowed her brows. Her brilliant mind rapidly went over every detail since Chu Yingfeng’s first appearance. The biggest clue was—","He liked Cat Mario!","Just what kind of normal person liked Cat Mario?","Just what kind of normal person would have their sanity tormented by Cat Mario and then actually gain favorability afterward?","All the clues pointed to the same answer!","There was only one truth—","He was a masochist! Chu Yingfeng was a masochist!!","Then it was obvious what kind of gift would raise his favorability!","Wu Guanyue’s gaze suddenly sharpened. She dashed into the backyard and snatched up the whip used to beat the donkey.","【[Wu Guanyue] has given [Ordinary Whip] to [Chu Yingfeng]. May your friendship last forever!】","Chu Yingfeng: “............?”","A question mark appeared above Chu Yingfeng’s head.","He lowered his head and stared expressionlessly at the whip. Then he suddenly reached out and took it, giving it a casual flick.","The long whip cracked through the air with a mighty gust, striking like a venomous dragon bursting from its lair!","On a table not far behind him stood a candle, its flame trembling and dancing. Chu Yingfeng swept the whip sideways. The tip brushed across the flame, which suddenly grew brighter and steadier.","It turned out that he had used the whip to snap off the candle’s overgrown wick.","It was easy enough to use the force generated by a weapon to blow out a flame. It was not particularly difficult to use pure spiritual energy to snuff out the wick, either. But Chu Yingfeng had not used even the slightest trace of spiritual energy. With nothing but astonishing control and eyesight, he had used the whip as a pair of scissors to trim the excessively long wick inside the flame.","Many cultivators, after entering the Dao and learning to wield the power of the heavens and earth, came to believe that overwhelming force could solve every problem. They no longer valued the basic skills of martial artists...","Chu Yingfeng, however, clearly was not one of them.","He placed the whip on the counter and said slowly, “Flexible weapons are much harder to control than rigid ones. If you wish to master this art, you might practice like this.”","Then he casually lifted Wuyun, who was still dry-heaving around his neck, and placed it on the counter before turning around and walking away at an unhurried pace.","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue stared blankly at the bright, steady flame.","She propped her chin in both hands and lay across the counter, seemingly lost in thought.","***","The next day, Wuyun had recovered from its indigestion.","Wu Guanyue grabbed Wuyun and stretched it like a strand of dough.","Perhaps it was just her imagination, but Wuyun seemed to be able to stretch a little farther than before...","Wuyun: “Meow! Rrow!”","Wuyun sounded delighted, its tail spinning like a propeller.","Chu Yingfeng was still in his room. He would probably be asking Wuyun to keep him company again soon. Naturally, Wu Guanyue wasn’t about to miss such a perfect opportunity to raise his favorability.","First, she would organize the information she currently had!","Wu Guanyue pulled out her business journal and began writing and scribbling in it.","So when Wenren Ying entered through the door, he saw Wu Guanyue muttering to herself.","“Chu Yingfeng... doesn’t like... golden potentilla...”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","A long string of ellipses appeared above Wenren Ying’s head.","Yesterday, Wu Guanyue had picked the lock and entered Wenren Ying’s home to give him a gift. Wenren Ying had tactfully expressed that such enthusiasm—resembling a home invasion—was really quite unnecessary...","As a result, Wu Guanyue had left looking utterly dejected...","She had left...","She had really left...","Wenren Ying: “............”","For some inexplicable reason, Wenren Ying felt a little guilty.","Why did his conscience feel guilty? There hadn’t been a single thing wrong with what he had said, had there?","And yet he simply couldn’t let the matter go...","To put it bluntly, he suspected that Little Shopkeeper Wu probably wasn’t human.","He had already realized that Little Shopkeeper Wu was actually quite clever. She reacted quickly, and when dealing with enemies, she was decisive. Some of her methods were difficult to evaluate...","But those methods had undeniably produced excellent results...","At the same time, she was almost completely ignorant of worldly affairs and lacked even the most basic common sense. As a result, she often appeared rather dazed.","So... she probably didn’t understand that she couldn’t pick the lock and enter someone else’s home... right?","That was what Wenren Ying told himself, but the more he thought about it, the more he suspected that he had been too harsh.","That was why he had come to the inn first thing this morning to check on Wu Guanyue.","But the moment he arrived, he saw Little Shopkeeper Wu wearing her usual serious expression, writing and drawing in her little notebook. And what she was writing about was... someone else’s preferences.","Chu Yingfeng... He knew that name. A disciple of the Xuantian Sect, who had recently come to Mount Mei. Could it be that he had stayed at Little Shopkeeper Wu’s inn last night?","Wenren Ying strode through the doorway, the wind stirred up by his cloak making quite a racket.","But Wu Guanyue was still scribbling away furiously, as if she hadn't heard a single thing.","\"Chu Yingfeng... likes playing... Syobon Action... the more you play, the more his favorability goes up... is that true?\"","Wenren Ying: \"............\"","One of Wenren Ying's hands rested on the counter, and two of his fingers tapped it gently.","Wu Guanyue lifted her head, glanced at him, and said, \"Ah! Wenren Ge!\"","Wenren Ying couldn't help but laugh. The moment he smiled, the overly sharp, cold line along his jaw instantly softened.","But right after that, Wu Guanyue ignored him again, burying her head in her writing once more.","\"Chu Yingfeng... seems to... really like... whips...\"","Wenren Ying: \"............\"","Wenren Ying: \"............??!\"","What kind of wild, inappropriate remark was that?!","Wasn't Chu Yingfeng the personal closed-door disciple of Elder Renhua? Since when did the Xuan Tian Sect's atmosphere become so depraved?!","What on earth did Chu Yingfeng come over to do last night! Little Shopkeeper Wu doesn't have much common sense to begin with, he can't let that brat corrupt her!","The brows under Wenren Ying's wide-brimmed hat furrowed, and even the line of his jaw turned unapproachable and frosty again.","Wenren Ying coughed twice and spoke up, \"Little Shopkeeper Wu, this...\"","Wu Guanyue, already familiar with the process, switched the shop's operation mode to automatic management.","Wu Guanyue said, \"Wenren Ge, I'm really busy right now. If you want something to eat, go get it yourself in the kitchen!\"","Then she went back to her deep, focused thinking.","Wenren Ying: \"............\"","Wenren Ying adjusted his wide-brimmed hat down a little.","That was his unconscious habit every time he didn't know what to say...","He looked at the extremely earnest Wu Guanyue, wanting to speak yet holding back, holding back yet wanting to speak again. Finally he let out a long sigh, resigned himself to his fate, and headed to the backyard to find something to eat.","He had been to the inn's backyard plenty of times before.","He walked familiarly into the kitchen. The fire in the bake kiln was still burning, and a warm baking aroma drifted out from inside. What was being baked today wasn't flatbread.","Wenren Ying waited patiently for a while, then used the fire tongs to take all the items out one by one and set them on the chopping board.","The things baking in the kiln today weren't flatbread, but round, plump... um, steamed buns?","No, they didn't quite look like steamed buns. They were much bigger than regular steamed buns, with cuts sliced into their surfaces with a knife. Right now their crusts were crispy and hot, giving off a warm, original wheat aroma that made people's hearts feel light just looking at them.","Of course they weren't steamed buns. This was Wu Guanyue's new recipe - kiln-baked bread!","Kiln-baked bread was a simple, rustic kind of bread. It didn't have an extremely moist texture, but when eaten hot, the crust was crispy while the inside was soft.","These past few days, Wu Guanyue had also bought milk from Li Dalang. Using milk together with the tail of the Spiral-Propeller Wuyun, she successfully got a new ingredient - butter!","Here, it was apparently called \"cooked ghee\".","Combining cooked ghee with wild garlic gave her garlic-flavored cooked ghee - and it was exactly because she got this ingredient that Wu Guanyue thought of making bread.","Kiln-baked bread paired with garlic butter, that couldn't possibly taste any better~~","Right now, Wenren Ying had figured out this way of eating all on his own. He cut open a bread and spread the garlic-flavored cooked ghee evenly over it...","Wu Guanyue pushed the door open with a clatter. Very naturally, she picked up the garlic cooked ghee bread on the chopping board, all the while talking to herself.","\"Will Chu Yingfeng like this...\"","Wenren Ying: \"............\"","Wenren Ying: \"..................\"","Wenren Ying's figure suddenly shifted. Wu Guanyue only felt the saponin fragrance from his cloak brush past her, and the next instant, the plate in her hands was in Wenren Ying's grasp.","Wenren Ying wore a faint, amused smile as he said, \"Little Shopkeeper Wu, is this for the guest upstairs? Let me deliver it for you.\"","Wu Guanyue looked up at him.","Wenren Ying was very tall. Standing in front of her like this, Wu Guanyue felt like she was entirely in his shadow. His broad, solid back blocked most of the sunlight streaming in from outside. Even though it was daytime, it gave her a feeling of being in dim, soft light.","Wu Guanyue: —ω—","A very tolerant look suddenly appeared on Wu Guanyue's face.","\"Wenren Ge, don't be silly,\" she said in a very mature, grown-up tone. \"Don't fight me for favorability points.\"","Right after that, she stood on tiptoe to take the small garlic cooked ghee bread back, and walked away humming a cheerful little tune.","Wenren Ying: \"............\"","Wenren Ying: \"...Hey, Little Shopkeeper Wu.\"","Wenren Ying paused for a moment, but eventually lifted his feet and followed Wu Guanyue upstairs to take a look at that guy named Chu Yingfeng.","...His main reason was that he didn't want some disreputable person to lead the common-sense-deficient Little Shopkeeper Wu astray.","Chu Yingfeng was sitting cross-legged, meditating and doing his breathing exercises. As he breathed in and out, a wave of steaming hot... garlic flavor drifted into his lungs.","Chu Yingfeng: \"............\"","Chu Yingfeng slowly opened his eyes.","Wu Guanyue was looking at him with bright, sparkling eyes, holding the garlic cooked ghee bread right under his nose.","A knife-wielding man in a wide-brimmed hat, his arms crossed over his blade, was leaning against the doorframe, silently observing... nobody knew exactly what he was observing.","[How do you ask Chu Yingfeng for information?]","[A. Greet him]","[B. Give him delicious food]","[C. Ask for the intel directly]","The player chooses all three options A, B and C!","Wu Guanyue said full of energy, \"Good morning, guest sir!\"","Chu Yingfeng: \"............\"","Wu Guanyue said sweetly, \"This is for you, eat it, don't stand on ceremony!\"","Chu Yingfeng: \"............\"","Wu Guanyue asked very concernedly, \"About the person we talked about last time that I wanted to find information on, do you have any more intel you can tell me, guest sir?\"","Chu Yingfeng: \"..................\"","Wu Guanyue: \"?\"","No reaction?","Then try using a special communication skill - the sandwich method of communication?","Wu Guanyue said, \"Good morning, guest sir! About the person we talked about last time that I wanted to find information on, do you have any more intel you can tell me... this is for you, eat it, don't stand on ceremony!\"","Wu Guanyue: (^▽^*)","Wenren Ying: \"............ Pfft.\"","Wenren Ying thought Little Shopkeeper Wu was so cute... uh, this look of hers where she sort of knew how the world worked was really especially adorable.","Sort of knew how the world worked... uh... sort of knew how the world worked...","He couldn't help laughing, his muscles relaxing, his expression full of joyful cheer.","Wu Guanyue turned around, looked at Wenren Ying with a strange, quizzical expression, then showed that tolerant look again and shook her head in a very mature way.","Chu Yingfeng: \"..................\"","Even though this was the guest room he had paid for, for some reason he felt like he was the one who was totally out of place here...","Wenren Ying smiled and said, \"Guest sir, this is a new dish our Shopkeeper Wu just invented. It is incredibly delicious, why not give it a try?\"","Wu Guanyue's eyes suddenly widened a little, glistening as she looked at Wenren Ying.","Wenren Ying smiled back at her, showing his white, neat teeth.","Chu Yingfeng: \"..................\"","[Chu Yingfeng's favorability towards Wu Guanyue has decreased!]","[Chu Yingfeng's favorability towards Wenren Ying has decreased!]","Wu Guanyue: \"............\"","Why did the favorability suddenly drop all of a sudden?","Men's hearts are as unfathomable as the bottom of the sea...","Oh well, she could think of ways to raise it slowly later.","Wu Guanyue sighed, put her hands behind her back, and left.","Before she left, she made sure to tuck the garlicky crispy bread roll into Wenren Ying's hands.","As for Wenren Ying, he did not seem to mind at all that this was something she had given to someone else only to be rejected. He took a bite straight away, and ended up scalding his tongue.","The two of them left Chu Yingfeng's room one after the other.","When they got downstairs, Wenren Ying's expression turned serious. \"Who is that kid looking for?\"","Wu Guanyue whipped her head around so fast her two braids flew into the air. \"He's looking for Daoist Master Songfeng... That's why winning Chu Yingfeng over is so important. Don't go messing things up, Big Brother Wenren!\"","Oh... so that was why Little Shopkeeper Wu cared so much about Chu Yingfeng's preferences all this time? It was only because he was tracking down Daoist Master Songfeng's whereabouts?","Wenren Ying couldn't help but chuckle to himself again.","Hearing that the disciples of the Azure Sky Sect were investigating Daoist Master Songfeng did not make Wenren Ying the slightest bit nervous.","He just stroked his chin and said, \"Don't worry. I'll handle this matter. That Seven Treasures Pine Seedling in your backyard, I have a top-tier concealment treasure that I can use on it... But I don't feel at ease with Chu Yingfeng staying here at your place. How about this, I'll move in for the next couple of days. You still have empty rooms at the inn, right?\"","Hearing those last words, Wu Guanyue lifted her head and looked at Wenren Ying thoughtfully.","Big Brother Wenren Ying was as composed as could be, acting perfectly proper, not a single hint of other ulterior motives in sight.","Meanwhile, back in Chu Yingfeng's room, Wuyun was squatting on the wooden table of the guest room, its eyes wide as copper bells, staring at Chu Yingfeng with a perfectly dignified expression.","Great, today's round of Cat Mario has officially started.","[Chu Yingfeng's affection for Wuyun has increased!]","***","Wu Guanyue and Wenren Ying were flirting, Chu Yingfeng was playing games, and Wuyun was absorbing pure spiritual energy... Everyone had a bright, wonderful future ahead of them!","But She Wenjie did not think the same way.","The She clan of Meishan was a renowned immortal clan in the region, and She Wenjie was the grandnephew of Verdant Cloud Adept. His grandfather and Verdant Cloud Adept were blood brothers.","Within the Green Cloud Cave Heaven, he had always lived a life of total indulgence. All those so-called \"geniuses\" and \"prodigies\" all had to fawn over him to curry favor. She Wenjie knew perfectly well that some of them did not actually want to smile and kowtow to him.","But so what? No matter how unwilling they were in their hearts, didn't they still trail after him like dogs, tongues lolling out? Even if they tried to run away, their own families would drag them right back just so he could have his fun!","How could a person who had lived such a comfortable, free-wheeling life as She Wenjie possibly swallow such a humiliating insult?","In broad daylight, that lowly girl had stuffed a handful of that... ugh, filthy stuff all over his hand!","By the time cultivators reached the Foundation Establishment stage, their bodies could refine and absorb all foreign substances they consumed, leaving no residue behind. She Wenjie could not even remember the last time he had encountered something so gross and unclean!","How dare she? How dare she do that to him!","The incident had happened in the side alley of the Laiyue Inn, and there had not been many witnesses, but the burning humiliation was impossible for She Wenjie to brush off. That very same night, he beat Zhao Kexin within an inch of his life, and sent his men out to track down that lowly girl.","He had not realized he had made such a big commotion, and just a moment ago, his older brother She Wenxiu had called him over and given him a severe scolding.","\"The Lotus Grand Competition is a major event for our Green Cloud Cave Heaven. Stay out of trouble and don't stir up any unnecessary chaos!\"","Those words made She Wenjie so furious his insides felt like they were on fire.","A major event for Green Cloud Cave Heaven? That was just She Wenxiu's major event!","She Wenxiu, whose dao name was Master Chongxu, was the top disciple under Verdant Cloud Adept. This year's Lotus Grand Competition was being organized entirely by him.","The Azure Sky Sect's grand competition was going to be held next year, and all the major cave heavens would be sending their selected disciples to compete in duels there. She Wenxiu was running the Lotus Grand Competition at such a critical juncture, and he could not afford to make even the smallest mistake.","What's more, the Azure Sky Sect was sending people to attend this Lotus Grand Competition too.","She Wenxiu sounded all high and mighty with his words, but he just wanted to show off in front of the Azure Sky Sect's representatives, and was calling She Wenjie a useless troublemaker who would ruin his plans!","But even though She Wenjie saw right through what his brother was thinking, he did not dare say it out loud... much less go against him.","After he left She Wenxiu's place, She Wenjie flew into a terrible rage. All the rich, spoiled sycophants around him hung their heads, not daring to utter a single word.","His face twisted with fury, he had his men drag Zhao Kexin over and whip him with a horsewhip right in his own private courtyard.","But even as Zhao Kexin wailed and begged for mercy, his anger did not subside even a little bit.","Just then, a servant came scrambling over to report that they had finished their investigation.","That lowly girl's name was Wu Guanyue.","She ran some shabby little inn in the city, and all her guests were lowly nobodies who weren't even fit to shine his shoes.","Hmph...","That audacious girl who had stuffed filthy gunk all over his hand? He was going to strip her naked and throw her into a pen full of Huo Dou beasts!","No... first, he would stew that cat of hers into cat soup right in front of her, and then throw her to the beasts.","Zhao Kexin was still wailing. He was hanging from the ceiling like a squirming worm.","She Wenjie said irritably, \"Alright, alright. Let him down.\"","Zhao Kexin was tossed onto the ground, his whole body covered in blood. He twitched and trembled, his face soaked through, no one could tell if it was tears or sweat.","She Wenjie smirked. \"Look at the state of you... Go, strip him naked and throw him into the Cold Jade Pond to wash up. Don't let him climb out before it gets dark.\"","One of the spoiled rich followers immediately chimed in. \"You hear that, Kexin? She Wenjie wants you to get nice and clean... Go on, get in there!\"","Zhao Kexin thrashed around frantically in the Cold Jade Pond, but every time he managed to grab onto the edge of the bank, someone would kick him right back in. The crowd cackled and jeered as they watched his sorry state, not stopping to think that prolonged exposure to the water of the Cold Jade Pond would give people a deadly cold poison.","But why would they ever bother themselves with such trivial matters?","Their whole lives had been spent doing whatever they pleased. The Dao and the laws were things they could trample under their feet... in fact, if anyone actually abided by the Dao and the laws, they would just dismiss that person as a lowly commoner.","They, the upper class, lived off of special privileges.","If they didn't run wild and act unscrupulously, how else could they show off how noble they were?","It didn't matter if Zhao Kexin died today or ended up disabled. They didn't care at all, because there would always be someone to clean up their mess for them. They would never face any consequences.","Wu Guanyue was no different.","She was just some nobody who ran a shabby inn. If she died today, or was maimed, who on earth would dare stand up for her?","A ferocious, bone-chilling grin spread across She Wenjie's face.","The new chapter is up! Thank you all so much for the support, I'll be holding a giveaway for everyone in the next couple of days~"]},{"number":22,"title":"Chapter 22","paragraphs":["***","At this moment, the sun was sinking in the west, and the blue-gray flagstones of Flagflower Road were veiled in a layer of golden haze.","It was dinnertime, and the waiters at the various eateries had begun calling out their wares once more.","In the past, even the hawking had been listless and feeble. Now, however, things were slightly different. That Little Shopkeeper Wu had opened an inn in the middle of the road—the... er, the Inn with the Very Long Name? It had attracted quite a few wandering cultivators. Summer had not yet ended, and all the wandering cultivators in the area liked to come here for a bowl of Sprite to soothe the dryness caused by their alchemical fires.","Naturally, more people had begun frequenting Flagflower Road, and the businesses at the other eateries had improved along with them.","Especially the Wei family’s savory crepes beside the inn.","At this moment, the inn was bustling with noise.","All nine tables were occupied, yet there was no one at the counter. As it turned out, Little Shopkeeper Wu had gone out with Wenren Ying, and no one knew when they would return.","Still, the inn did not descend into chaos simply because its proprietor was absent. The regulars calmly helped themselves to the buffet while keeping an eye on one another to make sure everyone paid the proper amount.","“Hey! You’re two coppers short! Don’t try to cheat people!”","“How am I two coppers short? Are you blind? Come count them yourself!”","“Who are you calling blind?!”","“All right, all right, sit down, both of you. Don’t make such a racket in the inn. What kind of behavior is that?”","“Meow~ Meow~~”","Wuyun was contentedly patrolling the main hall... and taking the opportunity to show off her body. Her method of showing off involved stretching herself out until she became a long, sinuous—","Lu Datong asked curiously, “Has Wuyun gotten bigger?”","Wuyun continued to meow demurely. “Meow~ Meow~~”","Of course Wuyun had gotten bigger!","One had to understand that Chu Yingfeng’s comprehension and manipulation of the spiritual energy of heaven and earth were on a completely different level from those of ordinary cultivators. Wuyun had been absorbing his spiritual energy for the past two days, and her cultivation had advanced by leaps and bounds.","Wuyun bounced and leaped around the inn. She no longer looked like a long-haired lion cat so much as a jerboa, hopping one jump at a time upstairs to find Chu Yingfeng.","Just then, a scattering of cold light suddenly tore through the setting sun and evening clouds!","The sound of something ripping through the air approached from afar. It was so sharp, so oppressive, that the person standing high above on those specks of cold light looked down upon everything in the shabby street as though he were gazing at ants he could crush beneath his hand.","Sword flight!","Ordinarily, the only place one could see people flying back and forth on swords was around Flying Peak, where the disciples of the Grotto Heaven resided. In theory, sword flight was forbidden over Meishan City... so what sort of person would dare disregard the rules so completely?","The answer went without saying.","The merchants and pedestrians along Flagflower Road had never witnessed such a scene. Those quick to realize that something was wrong had already slammed their doors shut, hoping to avoid trouble.","She Wenjie and his entourage had arrived in a fury!","One of the lackeys beside She Wenjie spotted the plaque covered in tiny writing and immediately pointed at it.","“Senior Brother, it’s here!”","She Wenjie’s gloomy eyes, filled with malice, fixed coldly upon Wu Guanyue’s inn.","Everyone inside the inn had naturally already sensed the aggressive wave of spiritual energy approaching. They were all martial artists—how could they fail to understand what it meant? One after another, they gripped their weapons.","Lu Datong strode out of the inn and glared furiously at She Wenjie, who stood high above them.","She Wenjie looked down at him coldly but said nothing.","The man beside him spoke in his place. “Where’s that bitch Wu Guanyue? Tell her to get out here!”","They had actually come looking for Little Shopkeeper Wu!","The disciples of the Grotto Heaven hovering in the air all wore white jade crowns and rosy-cloud robes. They were clearly wealthy and influential, and not people one could afford to provoke. What in the world had Little Shopkeeper Wu done to offend such a group?!","Lu Datong roared, “She Wenjie! Have you no shame?! You tried to commit murder in broad daylight and were stopped, yet you still dare come here looking for trouble? Is this how the Meishan She family does things?!”","The Meishan She family!","Sun Deng, standing beside Lu Datong, was stunned.","This man was actually She Wenjie! In Meishan City, even those who had never seen him knew of this notorious young master. He had bullied men and ravished women, and the outrageous things he had done could fill an entire basket. But who could blame him? He was a member of the Meishan She family.","Sure enough, even after Lu Datong cursed him to his face, She Wenjie showed not the slightest trace of shame or embarrassment. The man beside him even smirked smugly.","“Now you know who you’ve offended, don’t you? Since you do, hurry up and get lost. Are you waiting for your grandpa here to break your legs?”","The wandering cultivators holding weapons all went pale. This was someone they truly could not afford to offend. If they lost and were beaten to death, no one would care. But if they won... the She family stood behind him!","Some had already begun retreating silently. Only a handful remained standing defiantly before the inn, blades in hand.","“Lu Datong, what benefits did Wu Guanyue give you to make you risk your life for her?”","“Haha, benefits? What else could there be! Lu Datong, don’t worry. Whatever she gave us, we’re sure having more fun than you ever did.”","“Hey, Lu! Have you ever seen a woman stripped naked and thrown into a pack of Huodou? This time, we’ll broaden your horizons!”","Lu Datong let out an angry roar, and his Eight-Slash twin blades flashed into action!","The blades burned like raging flames as they swept straight toward She Wenjie, who stood at the front!","She Wenjie’s eyes were full of contempt. He merely flicked his sleeve—","The blade edge slashed across the sleeve embroidered with auspicious clouds, producing a strange clang like metal striking stone. Sparks flew from the blade, yet it failed to leave even the slightest mark on the young tyrant.","The garment was naturally no ordinary clothing. It was a Black Silkworm Immortal Garment woven from snow-mountain black silkworm silk, impervious to blades and spears!","Lu Datong had never seen such a magical treasure before. Only after bringing his blade down did he realize that something was wrong. He immediately tried to pull back and defend himself, but She Wenjie’s other sleeve had already swept toward him—","Bang!","That was the sound of Lu Datong crashing heavily onto the ground.","The sleeve had struck him squarely in the chest, as though a thousand-jun hammer had smashed into him. The pain was so intense that he spat out a mouthful of blood!","Wuyun: “!!!”","Every hair on Wuyun’s body stood on end!","Her tail rose high into the air, all four paws drawing tight, while she repeatedly hissed through her bared teeth—","By then, She Wenjie had already ordered coldly, “Cut off his arm!”","Lu Datong lay on the ground, one hand clutching his chest and the other bracing against the floor. Gritting his teeth, he glared at She Wenjie.","One of the young masters beside She Wenjie answered with a cheerful smile. “As you command, Senior Brother.”","A line of cold light appeared in his hand. It was a dagger so sharp it could sever a strand of hair the instant it touched the blade.","The dagger’s chill gleam drew closer to Lu Datong.","She Wenjie suddenly drawled, “Wait. I’ll do it.”","As soon as the words left his mouth, the dagger was already in his hand.","A crazed gleam, a mixture of bloodlust and excitement, flashed through She Wenjie’s eyes.","His hand rose high into the air!","Just then, a blast of wind suddenly shot out from inside the inn!","The gust carried astral energy, striking like a heavy punch.","It came too quickly for She Wenjie to dodge. He could only desperately raise his Black Silkworm Garment—","“Ahhhhhhhhhh—!”","Yet the blast of wind pierced straight through the Black Silkworm Garment and pinned his hand firmly to the ground!","She Wenjie’s agonized scream pierced the heavens!","And just then, a black-clad swordsman slowly—very slowly—walked out of the inn.","The setting sun illuminated his face, yet his features were as cold as the snow on a distant mountain.","“Who dares cause trouble?”","His voice carried a strange hoarseness, like a rusty blade being drawn from its sheath.","Only then did everyone see that the object pinning She Wenjie in place was nothing more than an ordinary chopstick.","Wu Guanyue was in the teahouse at that very moment, staring at Silver-Tongued Wu, the storyteller, with their eyes locked.","Silver-Tongued Wu: “Oh my, Little Shopkeeper Wu, you’re here again! Have you got ten taels of silver today?”","Wu Guanyue’s reply rang out loud and clear: “No!”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “............”","If you’re broke, why are you so proud of it?!","Wu Guanyue: “But I have Chu Yingfeng!”","Chu Yingfeng was her living signboard. As long as she could get that name out there, and supplement it with “a cultivation method recommended by even Chu Yingfeng,” then no matter how tortured everyone felt, they would first wonder whether their own cultivation level was too low instead of criticizing Cat Mario!","Wu Guanyue: Plan successful.jpg","That was why she had come to find Silver-Tongued Wu with absolute confidence.","Sure enough, the moment she said this, Silver-Tongued Wu sucked in a sharp breath and exclaimed, “Oh my! This is incredible! Absolutely incredible, Little Shopkeeper Wu!”","Wu Guanyue nodded with great restraint. “Mm-hmm! Mm-hmm! Exactly!”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “............”","Silver-Tongued Wu suddenly glanced left and right, then leaned close and lowered his voice. “Little Shopkeeper Wu, do you know...”","Wu Guanyue: “Hmm? Know what?”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “...that I’m the Sect Master of the Profound Heaven Sect?”","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Wu Guanyue: =.=","Silver-Tongued Wu really couldn’t help wanting to laugh.","Oh, this Little Shopkeeper Wu! How was she still going on about it?","She actually claimed that Chu Yingfeng was staying at her place. He had to give her credit for having the nerve to make that up!","Chu Yingfeng was an outstanding disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect! In terms of seniority, he was of the same generation as the Verdant Cloud Adept! Someone like that lived in a completely different world from them. Why would he refuse to stay in Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven and run off to that godforsaken inn of hers to play some ridiculous game? She couldn’t even lie properly.","“All right, all right, enough fooling around, Little Shopkeeper Wu! Without ten taels of silver, there’s nothing to discuss!”","Silver-Tongued Wu laughed heartily, still finding time to tease Wu Guanyue. “Though, I have to say, you’re quite talented at making up stories. If you have any good ones—true or false—I’ll pay you for them!”","The Little Shopkeeper’s eyes suddenly lit up. “Really? How much will you pay?”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “............”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “..................”","How could this woman not understand when someone was being sarcastic?!","He couldn’t help rolling his eyes. “All right, Little Shopkeeper Wu. If Chu Yingfeng is staying at your place, then I’ll say Dao Lord Tongxuan is sleeping on the kang in my house... Now go on, go on. I don’t have time to argue with you. I’ve got another story to tell soon...”","As he spoke, he leisurely took a sip of tea.","But who could have expected someone to suddenly rush into the teahouse, shouting excitedly, “Extra! Extra! The She family’s little tyrant got beaten up! Right outside the inn on Qihua Road, west of the city! The one who beat him was the immortal master Chu Yingfeng of the Profound Heaven Sect!”","Silver-Tongued Wu: “Pffft—!”","A mouthful of tea sprayed right out of him!","Wait a second?! Qihua Road?!","There was only one inn on Qihua Road—the one belonging to this Little Shopkeeper Wu...","Its name was far too long to bother remembering.","The Little Shopkeeper suddenly sprang to her feet and shouted in alarm, “What?! Chu Yingfeng and She Wenjie are fighting over a room at my inn?! Stop! Don’t fight over me—hahahahaha!”","Hey, you couldn’t even stop yourself from laughing, could you?!"]},{"number":23,"title":"Chapter 23","paragraphs":["***","The She family's little tyrant had been beaten!","The one who beat him was Chu Yingfeng of the Xuantian Sect!","As the sun set that day, the news spread like wildfire. Apart from the Wu family's teahouse, countless teahouses and taverns were buzzing with the same topic.","Everyone knew that She Wenjie was a tyrant in Meishan City. To speak of nothing else, there was the son of the Zhao family, who ran the Yue Lai Inn. His entering the Verdant Cloud Paradise should have been a joyous occasion, yet She Wenjie had taken a liking to him and treated him like a dog every few days.","The Yue Lai Inn welcomed travelers from all walks of life. Even if Boss Zhao made a fortune every day, before a true immortal sect or aristocratic clan, he was less than an ant.","How could anyone not hate someone like She Wenjie?!","Who would have thought that after doing so many wicked deeds, She Wenjie would finally bring disaster upon himself? He had actually run into Chu Yingfeng of the Xuantian Sect!","As the saying went, those who did too much evil were bound to perish by their own hands!","It would be even better if that bastard were beaten to death!","The usually obscure Qihua Road had suddenly become the center of attention throughout the city.","And at that very moment, on Qihua Road—","The entire street was deathly silent.","The sword trembled lightly with She Wenjie's breathing, giving off a series of low hums.","Chu Yingfeng stood opposite him, his pitch-black eyes devoid of emotion as he looked at him.","He held the sword in his hand. Blood slid down the blade, drop by drop seeping into the cracks between the bluestone paving.","Naturally, it was She Wenjie's blood.","His Black Silkworm Robe had been slashed into tatters. The immortal garment, woven from Snow Mountain Black Silkworm silk, was reduced to nothing more than a scrap of cloth before this man.","And She Wenjie himself... beneath that thin, razor-sharp sword, had been utterly powerless to resist!","It hurt... it hurt so much...","Every inch of his body was in agony. He wished he could simply pass out and be done with it!","She Wenjie was cruel by nature. Normally, the more miserably others screamed, the more delighted he felt... But now he had become just as wretched and bloodied as those people.","Who knew how many were watching his battered, blood-soaked appearance from a distance? Who knew how many were applauding inwardly, wishing he would be chopped into mincemeat right then and there?","When had She Wenjie ever encountered such a thing?","When had She Wenjie ever been reduced to such a sorry state?","Not long ago, he had wanted to chop off Lu Datong's arm... But Chu Yingfeng had pierced his palm with a single chopstick. At that moment, She Wenjie had screamed with enough force to tear his heart apart. Aside from fear, he had felt furious that his privilege had been challenged!","That fury had burned in his chest, leaving him not even the slightest hesitation before he immediately shouted the proudest support he had always relied upon—","“How dare you touch me?! Do you know who I am?!”","The pampered young masters behind him, who had been frightened senseless, were jolted back to their senses by that shout and began yelling at the top of their lungs.","“Who are you?! How dare you cause trouble in Meishan!”","“Do you really think you can afford to provoke the She clan of Meishan?! Kneel down and beg for mercy!”","The black-clad young man's expression did not change in the slightest. Even after hearing the name “the She clan of Meishan,” his muscles remained relaxed.","He said succinctly, “I am Chu Yingfeng.”","Everyone's expressions changed.","Chu Yingfeng!","Chu Yingfeng, disciple of the Xuantian Sect!","Why was he here?!","As a distinguished guest of the Verdant Cloud Paradise, shouldn't he have been staying properly on Flying Peak? What was he doing at this godforsaken little inn?","Yet this utterly absurd thing had happened. And they... not only had they come charging in menacingly, they had even crashed headfirst into the muzzle of a gun and been beaten like dogs by Chu Yingfeng!","She Wenjie's complexion shifted again and again, changing more dramatically than the pools of Five-Color Lake. Anger, shock, fear... So many emotions had converged on his face at once that he looked almost comical.","His elder brother had warned him not to cause trouble at a time like this!","She Wenjie's legs had gone weak. He had almost collapsed onto the ground.","But with so many eyes watching, he simply could not swallow his pride or admit defeat!","So what if he was Chu Yingfeng! He was only the son of a servant and a kitchen maid! His cultivation had improved after entering the Xuantian Sect, but did he really think he could take on a clan that had stood for ten thousand years all by himself?!","He bolstered his courage with these thoughts, stubbornly forcing himself to remain standing. His eyes fixed on Chu Yingfeng with venomous hatred.","These were his true feelings, but he would never dare voice them aloud, afraid of enraging the other man.","Chu Yingfeng regarded him thoughtfully, then suddenly asked, “Did you come looking for the innkeeper?”","He remembered that the innkeeper's name was Wu Guanyue.","She was the person who had invented Cat Mario, and she possessed an exceptionally refined sense of fun. Chu Yingfeng did not dislike her.","On the contrary, he was somewhat curious about her...","Besides, the She clan of Meishan was indeed a formidable opponent for Wu Guanyue to deal with.","Since Chu Yingfeng had already intervened, there was no reason to stop halfway. He had decided to take responsibility for the matter and settle this trouble for Wu Guanyue.","The first step in settling the trouble was to ask what, exactly, had caused the grudge between them.","The large crowd of onlookers standing in the distance all turned their eyes toward She Wenjie.","She Wenjie: “...”","She Wenjie could hardly get a single word out!","What was he supposed to say? What could he say?! That he had come to cause trouble for Wu Guanyue because she had shoved a handful of shit into his hand, and he had held a grudge ever since?!","To be honest, She Wenjie had already blocked that humiliating memory from his mind... Naturally, no one dared mention it in front of him, so everyone had tacitly agreed to pretend it had never happened...","Chu Yingfeng said coldly, “If you don't speak, I'll drag you to Verdant Cloud Adept and have him investigate.”","She Wenjie: “...”","She Wenjie's expression twisted beyond recognition...!","Behind him, the pampered young masters all lowered their gazes, each silently praying that Chu Yingfeng wouldn't remember they were there.","In any case, having seniority had its advantages. Chu Yingfeng was about the same age as them, yet he was Verdant Cloud Adept's junior brother. If he truly pursued the matter to the bitter end—even going to Verdant Cloud Adept—then before half a day had passed, the entire city would know that She Wenjie had been given a handful of... ahem, fertilizer, by Wu Guanyue.","And for the next several hundred years of She Wenjie's glorious life, he would forever and ever be associated with... fertilizer. They would never be separated again.","If She Wenjie could endure such humiliation, he wouldn't be She Wenjie!","He looked exactly like a goose caught by the throat. His mouth was open, yet not a single word could come out!","“Don't fight because of me!!! Don't fight because of me!!!”","With a thunderous roar and clouds of dust, Little Shopkeeper Wu came sprinting over!","With a series of tragic cries, Little Shopkeeper Wu urged them to stop!","The onlookers, like a flock of foolish, vacant-eyed chahas, all turned their heads toward the source of the noise.","Two glossy black braids bounced as the young shopkeeper finally came to a halt. Her round eyes were filled with worry and earnest pleading.","Looking over the scene of the brawl in the inn, she suddenly let out a long, heavy sigh and declared righteously, “She Wenjie! I know you want to play Cat Mario so badly you could die! But a pheasant can never be matched with a phoenix! Your cultivation and character are both terrible. Listen to me—go home. Go home, child!”","What... what...?","Wu Guanyue had suddenly burst onto the scene and rattled off a whole string of incomprehensible words. Of the few things She Wenjie could make out, it seemed she had said that his cultivation was terrible and that he wasn’t good enough to stay at her place and play Cat Mario...","What even was Cat Mario?!","She Wenjie: “......”","What the hell?!","Her guest rooms?! This place was worse than the kennel at his own home! Why would he ever come stay here?!","Yet, to his surprise, Chu Yingfeng seemed to agree wholeheartedly with her and nodded.","“Hmm... This level of cultivation... this temperament... indeed, he’s not quite good enough.”","She Wenjie: “??!”","She Wenjie was so furious he nearly spat blood!","What did you say?! What did you say?! What the hell are you two talking about?!","He practically wanted to leap up and start cursing them out!","Just as he was about to explode, Little Shopkeeper Wu suddenly let out an exceedingly dangerous “Hmm~?”","She bent forward, and her twin ponytails dangled in front of her, swaying gently. Her eyes were wide and round, making her look both pure and lively.","The pure and lively Little Shopkeeper Wu asked doubtfully, “Why are you looking at me like that? Isn’t that the reason? Oh~ I know! Is it because that day I...”","“I’m not good enough for your Cat Mario!!!”","She Wenjie shouted, cutting her off.","Little Shopkeeper Wu still looked suspicious. “Is that so? Senior Brother She is so distinguished and precious... Surely you still look down on our shabby little establishment?”","She Wenjie shouted even louder than before, “I’m not good enough for your Cat Mario! I was wrong from start to finish for fighting so fiercely just to snatch your Cat Mario!!!”","Little Shopkeeper Wu: (*^▽^*)","Little Shopkeeper Wu suddenly smiled, her expression sweet yet helpless. “Oh my... was that really necessary... was it really necessary! Ah, but I suppose I can only blame my Cat Mario for being so astonishingly effective at improving one’s cultivation...”","As she spoke, her gaze darted about before locking precisely onto Wenren Ying, who had just arrived.","Wu Guanyue: Oω<!","Wenren Ying: “......”","Wenren Ying: “............”","To be honest, he really didn’t want to understand so quickly. Sometimes, knowing too much was the source of all a person’s troubles.","Wenren Ying lowered his bamboo hat with one hand and reluctantly picked up the conversation.","“So where can one play such an amazing Cat Mario?”","“Remember, Flagflower Road! Remember the Name-Is-Too-Long Inn run by Little Shopkeeper Wu! Game rooms are five taels of silver per night! Unlimited Cat Mario! We have five rooms in total—first come, first served! First come, first served!”","Little Shopkeeper Wu shouted at the top of her lungs.","“This Cat Mario is actually that miraculous!”","“Isn’t this much better than some Red Pheasant Boshan censers and silk-thread bed curtains?”","“My cultivation hasn’t advanced in ages... Can playing Cat Mario really work?”","“Whatever! I’ll reserve a room first!”","“I’ll book ten days!”","“I’ll rent by the month!”","“I’ll stay here permanently!”","Little Shopkeeper Wu flashed her trademark sweet smile.","She Wenjie: “......”","She Wenjie: “..................”","At long last, She Wenjie finally understood what Cat Mario was..."]},{"number":24,"title":"Chapter 24","paragraphs":["***","Things were already heating up at the inn. At first, everyone was still intimidated by She Wenjie’s authority and didn’t dare cheer too openly. But the moment Little Shopkeeper Wu announced, “Five guest rooms, first come, first served,” many of them could no longer hold themselves back...","Besides, no matter how fierce She Wenjie was, he was still only a spoiled young master from Meishan City.","There were plenty of outsiders in Meishan City these days. They would watch the Lotus Contest and then leave... They weren’t going to stay for long, so who was afraid of offending him?","For a time, the scene became extraordinarily lively. At some point, Little Shopkeeper Wu had climbed onto a table. Her two long ponytails swayed left and right as she hopped about.","“Don’t rush, don’t rush! Everyone will have a room, and everyone will have a place to practice! I’ll just collect the room fees first... Yours after his, his after yours, yours after his...”","She Wenjie: “............”","She Wenjie: “..................”","The muscles on She Wenjie’s face twitched continuously.","The Second Young Master of the She clan of Meishan, She Wenjie, the Little Tyrant of Meishan City—he had actually suffered a silent loss!","But today, this was a loss he had no choice but to swallow!","Seeing that everyone’s attention was no longer on him, Chu Yingfeng also turned and went back into the inn. She Wenjie clenched his teeth, scrambled awkwardly to his feet, and turned to leave.","A long saber suddenly swept out and blocked his path!","The setting sun rolled across the sky. A bone-chilling gleam of snow flashed along the blade, held in a hand with thick joints and protruding knuckles.","That hand was steady and dry; the arm was solid and powerful. A thick tendon bulged beneath the skin with the movement, yet the saber flourished in his grip with astonishing lightness and playfulness.","Smack!","Smack! Smack!","The blade struck She Wenjie’s face three times in quick succession, each blow landing solidly!","Three red, swollen slap marks immediately appeared on his cheeks.","“What? You hurt someone and now you want to leave?”","The man spoke lazily, his bamboo hat still concealing most of his face.","“Wen... ren... Ying!”","She Wenjie’s voice sounded as though it had been forced up from the depths of hell.","Wenren Ying said, “Bring me some medicine!”","Although She Wenjie had suffered a silent loss, the matter of his injuring Lu Datong was not over yet. Sun Deng had already helped Lu Datong back into the inn to rest. Even while being tightly surrounded by the guests, Little Shopkeeper Wu had not forgotten to widen her eyes and signal for Wenren Ying to follow.","Of course, Wenren Ying had intended to do so anyway. He didn’t need her signal.","She Wenjie glared at the Vagabond Swordsman with venomous eyes. After a long while, he finally said, “I will never forget the grudge over those three saber strikes today!”","Wenren Ying smiled, then raised the hand holding his saber.","A line of saber-light flashed!","She Wenjie felt the blade-shadow tear through the air toward him. Saber qi spread across the heavens and earth, sweeping him completely into terror. It seemed that in the next instant, his head would be severed from his body!","“Ah!!!!”","She Wenjie let out a great cry and fell flat on the ground.","“Don’t make me say it again. Bring me some medicine.”","Wenren Ying’s voice remained lazy, but his smile had vanished completely. The line of the Vagabond Swordsman’s jaw now looked so cold and hard, so utterly devoid of human warmth, as though nothing in the world could move his heart.","“Give it to him! Give it to him!”","She Wenjie suddenly shouted. His attendants had been standing less than ten yards away, but were so frightened that they had frozen in place. They hurriedly pulled out the finest Lotus Dipsacus Paste from their robes and shakily handed it to Wenren Ying.","Wenren Ying snatched it, stuffed it into his robes, and walked away without sparing She Wenjie another glance.","She Wenjie suddenly felt something wet around his neck.","Only belatedly did he raise a hand to touch it, finding his fingers covered in blood.","“Ah!!!!”","He screamed again, rolled his eyes back, and fainted dead away.","***","Naturally, news of She Wenjie and Chu Yingfeng fighting over rooms at a certain inn did not remain known only within the city.","On the immortal mountains of Meishan, stretching endlessly beneath swirling clouds and mist, the news had already spread as well.","A young woman dressed in a palace-style robe, her hair arranged in a high coiffure, stood amid a sea of flowers.","The flowers of spring had long since faded from the human world. Autumn was almost upon them, yet peach blossoms still bloomed in profusion here.","Peonies, begonias, golden-yellow peonies, green-snow peonies... Every rare and beautiful flower in the world, every exotic fruit beneath the heavens, seemed to be found within this small realm.","This was Hundred Flowers Valley, and the woman was Baili Yuling.","Baili Yuling, the young mistress of the Baili clan of Hundred Flowers Palace, belonged to one of Meishan’s most distinguished families. Master Lingbo, the sword-wielding elder of Azure Cloud Grotto-Heaven, had also come from the Baili clan.","“Hmph. That useless She Wenjie is incapable of accomplishing anything and excels at ruining everything. I knew he would cause trouble like this sooner or later. He deserves it!”","Baili Yuling lifted her chin proudly as she spoke.","Baili Yuling was about the same age as She Wenjie. They had both entered Azure Cloud Grotto-Heaven in the same year. As the young mistress of the Baili clan, how could Baili Yuling possibly look favorably upon the conduct of a useless, spoiled young master like She Wenjie?","And to make matters worse, She Wenjie expected everyone to bow to him!","The two of them had fought several times in earnest, with victory and defeat evenly divided between them. In any case, their grudge had long since been forged.","Now that she had heard She Wenjie had made a fool of himself in the city, how could Baili Yuling possibly pass up the opportunity to comment on it—and mock him?","As she spoke, the young ladies beside her naturally chimed in one after another.","“But do you really believe he fought over rooms at the inn west of the city?”","She suddenly smiled, her expression filled with disdain and contempt.","“I think someone probably set him up... Still, for the innkeeper to arrange such a scheme, she must have some ability! Very well. Let me go take a look at her!”","She spun around abruptly. Her gold-and-crimson armlet gleamed faintly beneath her palace robe, losing none of its warmth or vividness.","She was bold and impulsive, the sort who left the moment she made up her mind. In less than half an hour, Miss Baili had already arrived on Qihua Road—though, of course, she had kept a low profile and brought only a modest retinue.","Hmm... This place...","Five out of every ten bluestone paving slabs were cracked, making the road extremely uncomfortable to walk on. The lintels and signboards of the various shops and households were also badly weathered and old-fashioned.","Baili Yuling rarely came to a place like this. In her view, people who lived in such surroundings were usually lifeless and lacking in vitality.","Yet now, to her surprise, she discovered that this was not the case at all.","Although the lintels were shabby, the people themselves looked full of spirit. The shop assistants, dressed in worn but clean clothes, bustled about welcoming customers and seeing them off. From time to time, someone pushed a handcart piled with snacks commonly found in Meishan City—fried cakes, yellow-rice cold cakes, and various chilled drinks—waiting for passersby to buy one or two.","And without question, the liveliest place on the street was that inn.","Sounds drifted from within in wave after wave: the clinking of cups, plates, and bowls; the scraping of tables and chairs being moved... But the most attention-grabbing sound of all was a strange kind of music, accompanied, during the pauses between its notes, by the crowd’s cries of either approval or regret.","How noisy...","Baili Yuling did not particularly enjoy such a chaotic, raucous place.","This was probably the inn where She Wenjie had suffered his humiliation, wasn’t it? Its name was...","The young mistress lifted her head to look at the sign above the entrance—and promptly fell silent.","At that moment, the inn’s front doors opened. The inn was packed with people, with only the servers from the various food stalls weaving in and out, baskets in hand, hawking their wares... Compared to an ordinary inn, this place seemed more like a teahouse—a place where people gathered to listen to stories.","And yet it also seemed far more immersive than simply listening to stories.","Hmm...","Baili Yuling stood some distance away, eyeing the inn’s weathered signboard with undisguised disdain. In the end, however, her curiosity proved stronger than her reservations. She lifted her foot and walked over.","...She’d only take a look.","The moment she entered, Baili Yuling spotted the curtain of water hanging in the middle of the inn’s main hall.","Of course... water screens were nothing new. What was new, however, was the picture displayed on it!","The drawings were so crude that Miss Baili suspected someone had drawn them with their feet. Under normal circumstances, a work of this quality would never have been displayed before Baili Yuling’s eyes... Yet now, she was completely captivated by it!","Because the picture was moving!","A strange, ugly, bipedal cat advanced and leaped across the water screen, dodging all sorts of unexpected obstacles. At the end, it reached the finish line, pulled down a flag, and entered an entirely different adventure.","And that ugly, upright cat was being controlled by the cultivator standing in front of the water screen, using spiritual energy!","Could this be... Cat Mario?","That was right! This was the brand-new form of Cat Mario invented by Wu Guanyue!","When one person was tormented, it was merely torment. But when a group of people watched one person being tormented—well, everyone except the person suffering got to enjoy themselves!","Besides, Cat Mario was actually a serious test of skill.","At first, the difficulty of Cat Mario lay in not knowing what traps awaited you along the way. But as one played more rounds, the traps gradually became familiar. After that, the real challenge was control.","How could one quickly dodge the mushrooms dropping from above? How could one land precisely on the single tile that would not collapse? All of this required the cultivators to coordinate their hands and eyes... while precisely controlling their spiritual energy to manipulate the character.","Otherwise, the slightest mistake would send them a thousand miles off course.","After she opened the inn’s Cat Mario hall, it naturally received an enthusiastic response.","After all, cultivation was the act of climbing a road filled with hardship and suffering. Anyone who could persist on that road could not possibly be frightened away by setbacks. The more challenging something was, the more it stirred their competitive spirit.","Cat Mario was indeed the perfect game!","Baili Yuling was a bona fide cultivator herself, and at this moment, her attention had been completely captured. Her eyes, usually narrowed in disdain as she looked down on others, had opened wide and round. Her heart rose and fell along with the ugly upright cat as it jumped up and down.","She had heard that She Wenjie had gotten into a fight with Chu Yingfeng because he was addicted to Cat Mario... At first, she had assumed it was nothing more than a rumor.","But now, after only one glance, she was already captivated by this novel game.","“Hiss—who would have thought there’d be a hidden block here!”","“Oh, you have to lure the mushroom monster out first before moving on!”","“You already died here once just now. How are you making the exact same mistake again?”","Miss Baili could not help complaining.","The young ladies beside her tried to suppress their laughter. Only then did Baili Yuling realize that she seemed to have lost a little too much composure.","She raised her chin and said haughtily, “This thing isn’t interesting at all... I simply can’t stand watching people make foolish mistakes! If it were me, I certainly wouldn’t make the same mistake twice!”","She had just made the classic “I could do that too” declaration.","Her companions continued to smile as they asked, “Then... want to give it a try?”","Baili Yuling replied solemnly, “Although indulging in amusements can distract one from the Dao, I must admit that Cat Mario seems capable of improving one’s control over spiritual energy. The shopkeeper here truly is an ingenious person... I admire her very much. In that case, I’ll play one round, if only to show my support.”","Miss Baili purchased a game slot for herself and stood before the water screen, infusing it with her spiritual energy.","Naturally, she was nothing like that good-for-nothing She Wenjie. She had not piled up her cultivation through heavenly treasures and earthly riches. She Wenjie had stuffed himself with enough rare treasures to fill a basket, and although he had reached the Great Perfection of the Foundation Establishment realm, his techniques and control had failed to keep up. He had no idea how to use his spiritual energy in actual combat.","Baili Yuling, on the other hand, had advanced one steady step at a time, laying a solid foundation as she progressed.","As a result, her control over Cat Mario was indeed exceptionally precise. She had said that she could do it too—and she really could. She sailed smoothly through the first stage, only crashing and burning in the second. But that was because she had not known what obstacles awaited her there, so it was perfectly normal.","It was nothing special.","Baili Yuling said nothing. A faint smile merely appeared on her face.","Low-key. Low-key.","Just then, Little Shopkeeper Wu, who had been sprawled over the counter, suddenly rang a bell and called out loudly, “The new leaderboard is up~~!”","The images on the water screen suddenly changed!","Rows of names appeared, followed by their completion times: one stick of incense, half a stick, a quarter hour, half a quarter hour...","At the very top of those rows of tiny characters were three extremely easy-to-understand words—","Leaderboard.","Baili Yuling’s gaze immediately glued itself to the screen!","In first place was Chu Yingfeng. His time for clearing the first stage was one lesser heavenly cycle... As expected of the genius renowned throughout the Nine Provinces. He had actually achieved such an impressive result.","Second place, third place, fourth place...","And her ranking was—","Eighth place!","There were actually seven people who had played faster and better than her!!!","Without the leaderboard, it might never have occurred to her to improve her completion time. But the instant she saw it displayed before her eyes... a fierce desire to win suddenly surged up from the depths of Baili Yuling’s heart!","Baili Yuling: “............”","Baili Yuling: “..................”","With a blank expression, Miss Baili rolled up her sleeves.","“Again!!!”","None"]},{"number":25,"title":"Chapter 25","paragraphs":["Thanks to Little Shopkeeper Wu’s extraordinary wisdom, the Nametoo-Long Inn went from an obscure little establishment on Qihua Road to the hottest, most sought-after inn in the entire city—so popular that every room was impossible to book!","The inn had only five guest rooms, yet they were already fully reserved through next month.","A game room cost five taels of Tongxuan silver. On Qihua Road... or even throughout Meishan City, that was by no means a cheap price.","But providing cultivators with food and drink that could improve their cultivation was never going to be an inexpensive service.","A bowl of fire-prawn noodles at Xihua Restaurant cost two hundred copper coins—and that was only because fire prawns were the slow-witted shrimp most easily caught in the Suwen River.","As for the rooms at Yuelai Inn, which could nourish a five-colored spirit root, you couldn’t even afford to stay there without at least a tael of silver.","Really, if you didn’t have money, why bother cultivating?","And so, under these circumstances, Little Shopkeeper Wu’s five-tael rooms were, in fact... not that expensive.","At five taels of silver per room, all five rooms reserved through next month had already brought Wu Guanyue a total turnover of one thousand taels of silver. Naturally, the inn’s popularity had long since exceeded one thousand as well. In other words—","The inn had leveled up!","[Inn Level: LV.3]","[Inn Popularity: 5,003\\10,000 (Your inn has earned a modest reputation in the city)]","[Inn Turnover: 1,050\\10,000 (Your turnover is now calculated in units of silver taels)]","[Shopkeeper Details]","[Shopkeeper: Wu Guanyue]","[Level: LV.3 (Your strength is closely tied to the fate of the inn)]","The increase in both the inn’s level and her personal level naturally came with new rewards!","First were her personal proficiency skills.","[Acquired: [Proficiency Skill · Game Editing]!]","[Game Editing: Your game rooms have made your inn a success. You can now modify the games you already own according to your own ideas!]","[Acquired: [Advanced Pickpocketing]!]","[Advanced Pickpocketing: You have a dream—to become a superstar of the underworld! All that lockpicking has made you deft of hand... You can now pick the pockets of higher-level NPCs!]","She had gained one new skill and one advanced skill!","Pickpocketing was, of course, Wu Guanyue’s favorite skill. After advancing, her success rate against higher-level NPCs had increased considerably, making it an extremely useful ability.","However, Wu Guanyue only now realized that breaking into someone’s home by picking the lock and leaving them a gift used the Pickpocketing skill...","Hmm... Could that be why Wenren Ying didn’t like her showing up at his door that way? It probably counted as a hostile action, didn’t it?","Little Shopkeeper Wu cupped her chin in her hands and pondered solemnly.","Oh, well! His favorability hadn’t decreased anyway!","The second proficiency skill was [Game Editing]. As soon as Wu Guanyue selected it, the Cat Mario game interface appeared before her. She could freely move all the bricks, mushrooms, and traps around on the screen...","...but why would she want to do that?","Apart from Chu Yingfeng, no one had cleared the entire game yet. At present, the appeal of Cat Mario lay in mastering precise controls and finding ways to complete the game faster...","Wouldn’t suddenly changing the levels just be a complete trap for everyone?","She had a feeling that, after making changes, she would become the kind of game planner cursed by thousands of players...","It felt... like a rather useless skill.","Oh, well. She could leave it for now. Maybe it would come in handy someday?","And then there was the new mode unlocked when the inn leveled up!","[Unlocked: CG Mode!]","[CG Mode: Unforgettable memories! Heartwarming moments! And all the countless instants you want to record... You can now record your very own CG moments in the inn~~]","Ohhh—it was for collecting CGs!","She had actually been meaning to ask for a long time... Why didn’t this game support taking pictures? She hadn’t expected it to be an upgrade reward!","...Er, wasn’t this a little too stingy?","It was really... hard to comment on.","Still, Wu Guanyue didn’t particularly care. After all, the LV.3 reward wasn’t the main event.","Her main quest, [Lotus Contest], required the inn to reach LV.4 before it could be completed. LV.3 was merely a transitional stage.","LV.4 required both popularity and inn turnover to reach 10,000. Popularity was easy enough. Ever since she launched the Cat Mario Fun-for-All event and the Cat Mario leaderboard, the inn had developed a lively competitive atmosphere. Every day, it attracted curious people who came in to take a look.","On top of that, she didn’t stop the other merchants on Qihua Road from selling food at the inn. Everyone was making money thanks to Cat Mario, so of course they were happy to help promote it!","Just the other day, Wu Guanyue had even spotted the old man running the tea stall at the crossroads enthusiastically recommending Cat Mario to his customers...","Anyone who didn’t know better would think he owned shares in the place.","And so, the inn’s popularity increased every day. Reaching ten thousand popularity was only a matter of time.","The problem was the turnover.","No matter how popular Cat Mario became, Wu Guanyue still had only five guest rooms...","With all of them booked through next month, she had reached the limit. Many of the wealthier guests had come from out of town, and once the Lotus Contest ended, they would be leaving. Why would they stay here after that?","As for those who lived in Meishan City year-round... Poor itinerant cultivators couldn’t afford to stay here, while the wealthy...","She Wenjie had made a spectacular fool of himself here. If the disciples of Cuiyun Grotto-Heaven still wanted to maintain a superficial relationship with him, they wouldn’t set foot in the inn at a time like this.","Besides, the Cat Mario Fun-for-All event was an important way to expand her influence, so she couldn’t charge high fees.","The event was bustling and lively, but as for the turnover...","It was still only one-tenth of the target.","How was she supposed to get her hands on more money...?","Wu Guanyue stood in the back courtyard with her arms folded, looking extremely serious.","“What are you thinking about, Little Shopkeeper Wu?” Wenren Ying asked casually as he passed by on his way to the kitchen to ladle himself some water.","“I’m thinking about how I can pull off a really big score!”","Wu Guanyue’s voice was ringing and forceful—and especially loud.","Wenren Ying: “Pfft—cough, cough, cough!”","He spat out all the water in his mouth.","Wu Guanyue didn’t think this had anything to do with her at all. Instead, she hurried over with concern and pulled out of her robes...","the golden plum blossom he had given her.","Wenren Ying: “...”","Wenren Ying: “......”","For some reason, Wenren Ying couldn’t help laughing again. He casually accepted the little golden flower and even pretended to examine how to use it to wipe his mouth.","Then he looked up and saw Wu Guanyue staring at him as though he were an idiot.","“Did the game glitch? Hey, Brother Wenren, what would you do without a player to look after you...?”","Wenren Ying: “......”","He wanted to say that if “being looked after” meant someone picking the lock, breaking into his home, and leaving gifts behind, then he really could do without it...","At that moment, sweet Little Shopkeeper Wu had already pulled a handkerchief from her robes and leaned over to wipe Wenren Ying’s chin.","She only came up to his chest, so she had to rise up on her tiptoes...","Speaking of Wenren Ying, he was the type of carefree, unconventional wanderer who lived by his own rules... So under normal circumstances, his robes weren’t fastened especially tightly. At moments when his muscles tensed like this, a small glimpse of the deep cleft between them would show...","Hmm? Why were his muscles tensing...?","Just as this thought sprang into Wu Guanyue’s mind, Wenren Ying suddenly reached out and snatched the handkerchief from her hand. He wiped his chin twice in a haphazard fashion and mumbled, “Yes, yes, yes. Many thanks for looking after me, Little Shopkeeper Wu...”","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue seemed a little disappointed. “I haven’t had the chance to look after you yet...”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Another ellipsis bubble appeared above Wenren Ying’s head... Who knew what he was thinking?","He turned his head away and said, “I’ll wash the handkerchief and return it to you.”","Wu Guanyue was still a little disappointed. “Oh...”","Actually, that scene just now would have been perfect for a CG. What a shame she hadn’t thought of it in time... Now the opportunity was gone.","Darn this game that didn’t let her reload!","Wenren Ying’s Adam’s apple bobbed... He seemed about to say something, but at that very moment, his expression suddenly turned cold. Frowning, he said, “What’s going on?”","His gaze was fixed on— the Seven-Treasure Pine.","Chu Yingfeng had come to Meishan City in the first place to search for Daoist Master Songfeng. On the very first day he arrived at the inn, he had asked Wu Guanyue about Daoist Master Songfeng’s whereabouts... After Wenren Ying learned of this, he gave her the merfolk pearl he used for concealment. As long as it was buried in the soil, it would immediately hide the aura of the Seven-Treasure Pine.","The Seven-Treasure Pine had originally only sprouted a tiny shoot, concealed among the weeds in the rear courtyard. Even an Earthly Immortal wouldn’t have been able to spot anything unusual.","But just now, during the brief moment they had been talking, the Seven-Treasure Pine had suddenly shot up from the ground and grown into a tree as tall as a person!","And at that very moment, Chu Yingfeng’s footsteps sounded from the front hall. He was making his way toward the rear courtyard and was about to push open the courtyard gate!","Chu Yingfeng was a hardcore gamer. Ever since he started playing Cat Mario, he had shut himself in his guest room every day to play. After clearing the game, he moved on to trying to beat it in an even faster time... He had practically forgotten his own actual mission...","But “practically forgotten” was one thing. Wu Guanyue certainly didn’t believe that he could remain unmoved when a fully grown Seven-Treasure Pine suddenly appeared right in front of him!","The player’s affection level was only at two hearts. It was nowhere near high enough to complete the quest without a fight!!!","Wu Guanyue: “!!”","Two huge red exclamation marks appeared above Wu Guanyue’s head!","She absolutely had to stop him from coming in! She couldn’t let him see the pine tree that had suddenly grown up!","What should she do?!","Wu Guanyue’s mind raced at top speed!","Just then, Wenren Ying suddenly moved.","He abruptly leaned his entire body heavily against the rear courtyard gate, and a long... sigh escaped his throat.","That’s right—a sigh.","It was as though some deep, almost impossible-to-satisfy longing had suddenly been relieved, or as though his tightly wound muscles had finally been submerged in a pool of sweet, soothing hot spring water...","He suddenly reached out and pushed against the courtyard gate again and again, making the wooden door creak violently.","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue: o(*////-////*)q","The scale of this is way too intense, Brother Wenren!"]},{"number":26,"title":"Chapter 26","paragraphs":["***","Wenren Ying spread the five fingers of one hand against the door. His sleeve had been rolled up, cinched around the middle of his forearm—right over the blue vein bulging beneath the skin.","Although his lips were parted and the breath escaping them carried the faintest hint of a moan, his entire bearing was razor-sharp.","The instant Chu Yingfeng approached, he had switched into a state of readiness, poised to strike.","Chu Yingfeng was certainly not a bad person—Wenren Ying was confident in his ability to judge character—but it was hard to say what he might do if he saw this suddenly sprouted Seven-Treasure Pine.","So it would be best if he didn’t see it.","The situation had arisen too suddenly. Aside from this method, Wenren Ying had no other way to drive him off.","Sure enough, Chu Yingfeng heard the strange sound...and, sure enough, he hesitated and stopped, falling into a baffled silence.","After a moment, he turned and walked away.","Wenren Ying let out a long breath, and the muscles stretched taut across his body gradually relaxed.","Then he turned around—and found the Little Shopkeeper Wu staring at him with eyes wider than bronze bells.","Wenren Ying: “......”","His back seemed to tense up all over again.","“Brother Wenren...”","Little Shopkeeper Wu drew out the words meaningfully.","For some reason, whenever she spoke in that meaningful tone, it made one’s scalp prickle.","Wenren Ying reached up and pressed down on his bamboo hat, hiding his eyes completely in its shadow. In an utterly composed voice, he said, “Sorry. I didn’t want to resort to such a vulgar trick...but...”","“You don’t want Lu Datong to find out what just happened either, do you?”","Little Shopkeeper Wu suddenly shouted, the corners of her mouth curling into a roguish grin that did not suit her at all.","Wenren Ying: “......”","The words Wenren Ying had been about to say abruptly caught in his throat.","Wenren Ying: “......?”","What had she just said?","He felt as if that one sentence had turned his brain into a bowl of mush. He tried to think it through, but failed. In the end, he opened his mouth and voiced his confusion.","“...Why Lu Datong?”","Little Shopkeeper Wu answered with complete righteousness, “Because he’s the only person I know you know!!!”","Wenren Ying: “......”","Wenren Ying: “............”","A huge crossroads suddenly appeared above Wenren Ying’s head.","Little Shopkeeper Wu: “Ah! Are you angry, Brother Wenren?”","Wenren Ying: “......”","Wenren Ying couldn’t be bothered to respond. He walked straight over to the Seven-Treasure Pine and examined it from top to bottom.","The Seven-Treasure Pine stood there quietly. A breeze suddenly swept past, stirring its slender needles and making them rustle.","Wenren Ying suddenly said, “Its primordial spirit hasn’t been destroyed.”","That was precisely why it had remained hidden here, waiting for an opportunity to appear.","Now that he thought about it, the boisterous and hot-tempered Daoist Master Songfeng must have been lying dormant once again for an unknown length of time. The reason Chu Yingfeng had come to the inn to inquire about Daoist Master Songfeng was probably because this pine had secretly sent out some kind of message.","The Xuantian Sect... The Xuantian Sect...","He had already confirmed that Chu Yingfeng was not the only person from the Xuantian Sect who had come this time. The other was Bai Yunsheng, the second disciple under Elder Renhua. Presumably, the two of them had come together to investigate Daoist Master Songfeng’s whereabouts.","He had to find a way to resolve this matter once and for all.","Wenren Ying fell into deep thought.","Wu Guanyue rested her chin in her hands and fell into deep thought as well.","***","“Ah!!!!”","“Ahhhhhh!!!!”","She Wenjie had no intention of thinking things over!","Not only was he not going to think, he was determined to release all the fury bottled up inside him through a series of enraged roars!","Humiliation! Humiliation! Humiliation!","She Wenjie had never experienced such humiliation in his life!","In broad daylight, he had been forced to humiliate himself by admitting that the words spoken by that bastard—someone inferior to him in status, cultivation, and every other regard—were true.","And then there was Wenren Ying... Wenren Ying!","She Wenjie had injured people more than once or twice. Had anyone ever dared to say to his face, “You hurt someone and still want to leave”?","No! Never!","The confidence behind She Wenjie’s tyrannical behavior came precisely from this—from the power and influence possessed by his enormous family.","Yet now, he had suddenly discovered that those things were not omnipotent after all.","Wu Guanyue had no status whatsoever. Simply because she had borrowed the power available to her in that moment, she had trampled all over his identity without the slightest psychological burden and even used the incident to advertise the rooms at her own inn.","Wenren Ying had done the same. His status, position, family, and inheritance seemed to count for nothing in front of She Wenjie. Just for the sake of two bottles of healing medicine, he had...he had nearly sliced off She Wenjie’s head!","But in truth, Wenren Ying had of course taken She Wenjie’s identity into consideration. Wenren Ying lived in Meishan City as well, and the Little Shopkeeper Wu he had helped ran a business there. Once a person became connected to others, it was difficult to act without showing any restraint.","That was why he had not actually cut off She Wenjie’s head.","She Wenjie, however, could never have imagined this. If people did not kneel before him, trembling and bowing obsequiously, he felt insulted.","What was more, the consequences of that incident went far beyond this.","Verdant Cloud Adept had naturally not come to see him. To be honest, although She Wenjie was always boasting about Verdant Cloud Adept’s past achievements, he rarely got to see the adept in person.","Even his own parents could not see the adept more than a few times a year, and whenever they did, they behaved with extreme caution, afraid of saying the wrong thing.","Verdant Cloud Adept had rarely mentioned him at all, yet this time, the adept had sent him a message: He did not need to participate in this year’s Lotus Grand Tournament.","He would not be entering the inner sect.","Those words, delivered to him by a messenger, struck his face like a heavy slap.","She Wenjie had never been particularly devoted to the Dao...but being unable to enter the inner sect meant that he had lost face completely. It meant he would become a laughingstock throughout Meishan’s upper circles!","Of course, a wastrel like him was already looked down upon by others. She Wenjie usually understood perfectly well whom he could bully and whom he could not. But this time...the very soft targets he had believed he could trample at will had dealt him a crushing blow!","A twisted hatred rose within She Wenjie’s heart.","If you were kicking a dog and the dog bit you, wouldn’t you hate it?","Wu Guanyue, Wenren Ying...","Wu Guanyue, Wenren Ying...!","“Ah!!!!”","She Wenjie let out another cry like a groundhog, charged into the courtyard, grabbed the first person he saw, and began punching and kicking him.","Just then, someone entered.","“Young Master, we found out!”","The man hurried over to She Wenjie’s side and whispered into his ear.","The contents of that whisper naturally concerned Wu Guanyue.","Why had Chu Yingfeng appeared at Wu Guanyue’s shabby inn for no apparent reason? There was clearly something suspicious about it.","It was truly difficult to believe that She Wenjie’s brain had managed to think of that much...","Of the two people who had come from the Xuantian Sect, one was Chu Yingfeng, while the other was Bai Yunsheng, a scion of the Yunmeng Bai clan. This time, Chu Yingfeng had arrived at Meishan first, while Bai Yunsheng... had only come up to the grotto-heaven yesterday to pay a visit to the Verdant Cloud Adept.","He made no attempt to hide his purpose, stating plainly that he had come to reclaim the Seven-Treasure Pine, a magical treasure left behind by the Sword Lord Taibai.","This information was no secret. Even a good-for-nothing wastrel like She Wenjie knew about it by now.","As for what he had sent people to investigate... it was Wu Guanyue’s background.","Wu Guanyue had a grudge against Qian Shian of Yongfeng Money House, and Qian Shian’s master was a tree demon... Later, Qian Shian had disappeared without a trace. As for that tree demon master of his... could Wu Guanyue have killed him?","And could that tree demon master have had something to do with the Seven-Treasure Pine?","If he could prove that, then what he had done would not be some wastrel’s reckless mischief at all. He would have been trying to recover a magical treasure belonging to the Xuantian Sect! And Chu Yingfeng... would certainly be unable to escape unscathed either!","The more She Wenjie thought about it, the more restless he became. At last, he could no longer sit still and abruptly rose to his feet.","Naturally, he was not going to find Bai Yunsheng... He did not even have the qualifications to meet the martial uncle from the Xuantian Sect.","The person he intended to see was his elder brother—Master Chongxu.","Only his own brother, born of the same mother, would still be willing to see him at a time like this.","Besides, he had no choice but to go.","The Meishan She clan was a powerful and wealthy family. Although the Verdant Cloud Adept had no children of his own, there were certainly plenty of She clan disciples eager to become his personal disciple and inherit the position of Meishan’s master. If Master Chongxu still wanted to make an impression before the Verdant Cloud Adept, he had better find some way to reverse the impact of this incident—to change the impression their branch had left in the Verdant Cloud Adept’s mind.","This was what happened when you dragged a burden along with you~","She Wenjie understood it perfectly. With an outwardly respectful manner and inwardly delighted heart, he went off to throw his elder brother under the bus.","***","Two days later.","The moon shone clear and bright, and the stars glittered in the pure night sky.","Chu Yingfeng sat cross-legged on the bed, his hands resting on his knees, his mind calm as he meditated.","Moonlight spilled over his jet-black hair and pale face, making his hair appear even darker and his skin even whiter. He looked almost like a male ghost devoid of all human vitality.","At the Xuantian Sect, Chu Yingfeng was, of course, not especially popular.","He was too solitary, had no powerful background, and possessed too great a reputation. His life at the Xuantian Sect could hardly be called pleasant. Even his master, Perfected Renhua... perhaps regarded him as nothing more than a hired fighter.","But to be honest, Chu Yingfeng did not care about any of that.","There were very few things he cared about at all. Even when he had heard the words “Meishan’s Number One Blade engaging in daytime debauchery” that morning, he had not...","...But he had also heard Little Shopkeeper Wu’s voice.","Little Shopkeeper Wu had been threatening Wenren Ying. The threat had been...","“You wouldn’t want Lu Datong to find out, would you?”","Chu Yingfeng: “......”","Chu Yingfeng: “............?”","...Why Lu Datong?","At heart, Chu Yingfeng was someone who enjoyed exploring the unknown. At that moment, he had keenly sensed, from Little Shopkeeper Wu’s threat, the existence of a realm he knew nothing about...","...But his keen sixth sense also told him that he did not particularly want to learn more.","Chu Yingfeng frowned faintly and cast these inexplicable matters from his mind. He quietly continued meditating, allowing the spiritual energy of heaven and earth to enter his meridians through each breath he drew and released—","Suddenly, he opened his eyes, his gaze falling upon his fingers.","A message butterfly rested upon his pale knuckles.","Chu Yingfeng stared silently at the butterfly. His emotionless eyes flashed with unmistakable annoyance.","Bai Yunsheng was looking for him.","After a long while, he finally rose and leapt through the inn window. Then, just like that, he vanished into the darkness.","At the same time, Wenren Ying was standing in the shadows.","No one knew how long he had been lying in wait. His entire presence had been completely concealed, yet his muscles remained in a state that could shift instantly between relaxation and explosive force. It was the posture of a beast lying in ambush for its prey, and he had mastered it with startling ease.","Could it be that this was not the first time he had lain in wait like this? Not the first time he had hunted?","But who, exactly, had he been lying in wait for—and who had he been hunting?","Watching the direction in which Chu Yingfeng had disappeared, Wenren Ying stretched lazily, preparing to follow him.","At that moment, his view suddenly flipped upside down—","He had been lifted high into the air! And the hands holding him were as firm as iron pincers, gripping him so tightly that he could not break free!","The person who had lifted him carried a clean, soft, warm fragrance—the cozy scent of freshly washed bedding, mixed with the smell of a cat’s belly fur after it had been warmed by the sun...","Wenren Ying: “...Little Shopkeeper Wu, put me down.”","He knew Little Shopkeeper Wu was behind him, but he had never expected the other man to be capable of something so outrageously powerful...","Standing atop Wuyun and holding Wenren Ying over his head, Wu Guanyue blinked his round eyes. “Why, Wenren-ge? Wuyun runs really fast! We can catch up with him right away!”","Wenren Ying: “............”","The corner of Wenren Ying’s mouth twitched. He did his best to remain calm as he explained, “But Wuyun makes a lot of noise when he runs, doesn’t he? We’re following him—following him, understand? Be good and put your Wenren-ge down.”","Wu Guanyue thought about it. That did seem to make sense, so he obediently said, “Oh!”","Then he put Wenren Ying down.","Wenren Ying had just breathed a sigh of relief when he felt something heavy land on his back...","Wu Guanyue had placed Wuyun on top of his head, then climbed onto Wenren Ying’s back without the slightest hint of hesitation. In a perfectly reasonable tone, he declared, “Then you be our mount, Wenren-ge! Charge!”","Wuyun was equally justified as he cried, “Meow!”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","Nothing."]},{"number":27,"title":"Chapter 27","paragraphs":["***","Sword flight was forbidden in Meishan City.","And yet, high above this mountain city, one could often see disciples of the celestial grottoes in robes of purple haze, riding upon azure cloud swords. Most of these disciples came from noble backgrounds and could not be bothered to observe rules written for rustic independent cultivators.","Chu Yingfeng was certainly no rustic independent cultivator. Though he was about the same age as those grotto disciples, his seniority surpassed all of theirs combined. Here, he could walk sideways if he wished, or straight up and down if the mood took him.","Yet unexpectedly, he was a quiet and low-key sort of person.","At this moment, rooftops swept past beneath his feet like drifting clouds.","Drawing breath to ride the wind—this was the foundation of sword flight. Every cultivator began with this skill upon entering the path.","Wenren Ying naturally knew it as well. At present, he was carrying a person and a cat on his back as he quietly followed behind Chu Yingfeng.","Chu Yingfeng entered a courtyard.","Wenren Ying took a small vial from his robes and removed two pills, handing them to Wu Guanyue as he explained, “These are Turtle-Breath Concealment Pills. After taking one, your breathing and aura will be hidden for half an hour; unless a Great Vehicle Earth Immortal discovers you, you won’t be detected. People from Guixu City in the Eastern Sea use these for infiltration and assassination. You and Wuyun take one each. Then we’ll go inside and have a look.”","Wu Guanyue obediently swallowed one. Sure enough, a [Stealth] buff appeared on her, incredibly powerful!","With one person and one cat on his back, Wenren Ying slipped into the courtyard.","Though the small courtyard was not lavish or grand, it had rockeries, secluded lotus pools, bamboo cottages, and winding streams. It possessed a tranquil, refined charm.","Voices drifted from the main room.","Carrying Wu Guanyue on his back, Wenren Ying approached from the shadows.","There were two people in the room, one dressed in white and the other in black.","The man in black was, of course, Chu Yingfeng.","The man in white, however, was not looking at him. With his back turned, he was studying a portrait of a beauty hanging on the wall.","Moonlight flowed over his sleeve, illuminating the silver cloud pattern that flashed briefly into view—bright, meticulous, perfectly suited to him, and yet unmistakably arrogant.","The man in white was named Bai Yunsheng.","“Someone told me that the Seven-Treasure Pine is at the inn where you’ve been staying. Have you found anything?”","Bai Yunsheng spoke. He did not sound as though he were addressing his gifted junior disciple; rather, his tone was faintly disdainful.","Chu Yingfeng’s answer, meanwhile, was utterly concise.","“No.”","—After all, he had not investigated at all.","Bai Yunsheng let out a derisive snort.","“I think you’ve simply been distracted by trivial pleasures and have not taken the task assigned by the elders seriously at all!”","There was, of course, nothing wrong with that accusation.","Chu Yingfeng did not know Daoist Master Songfeng, after all. And he found the notion that “some country commoner dared to dispose of a magical treasure belonging to the Profound Heaven Sect” thoroughly repugnant.","In the end, although he and most of the sect belonged to the same Profound Heaven Sect, Chu Yingfeng did not stand on the same side as them...","Indeed, his position was the complete opposite of theirs.","Chu Yingfeng’s expression did not change. Arms folded around his sword, he gazed coldly at Bai Yunsheng, too unwilling even to spare him a word.","Bai Yunsheng, however, did not care about his attitude.","Turning around, he looked at Chu Yingfeng with his hands clasped behind his back and said slowly, “Move out of that inn tonight. Tomorrow, I’ll bring men to arrest the innkeeper. Don’t get in my way.”","Chu Yingfeng frowned. “Do you have proof that she did it?”","A strange, almost-smiling expression suddenly appeared on Bai Yunsheng’s face. It carried an undisguised, exquisitely subtle malice.","Looking at him, Bai Yunsheng drawled, “Proof... Once we capture her, we’ll have all the proof we need.”","A chilling killing intent abruptly erupted from Chu Yingfeng!","Those jet-black eyes, usually almost devoid of emotion, now resembled a wolf’s—fixed on Bai Yunsheng with savage fury.","Chu Yingfeng truly was a genius. He had been in the sect for scarcely more than a decade, yet his dantian sea of qi had already formed a golden core. Bai Yunsheng was more than a decade his senior, yet their cultivation levels were the same.","Moreover, Chu Yingfeng was a martial fanatic through and through. He loved crossing swords with opponents whose styles differed entirely from his own. His genius was not limited to cultivation alone—for cultivators who pursued the Dao through martial arts, temperament, reflexes, quick wits, experience... all these and more were crucial factors in determining victory or defeat.","If they fought now, Bai Yunsheng would not last ten moves against Chu Yingfeng.","Yet beneath such terrifying killing intent, before such a fearsome beast, Bai Yunsheng’s expression did not change in the slightest.","He still wore that almost-smiling look, and that subtle malice still gleamed in his phoenix eyes.","“What? Are you going to interfere with the elders’ affairs? Yingfeng, Yingfeng... you really ought to temper that personality of yours. So willful and reckless—have you ever spared a thought for your elderly mother, who is being cared for in the sect?”","The killing intent faltered at once.","Chu Yingfeng’s pale face twisted abruptly. Bai Yunsheng’s words were like a venomous whip, lashing hard across him—one stroke enough to draw blood and tear away flesh.","The smile on Bai Yunsheng’s face seemed to grow even more pleased.","He liked seeing that expression on Chu Yingfeng’s face... liked seeing him bloodied by that whip.","In truth, there was no substantial enmity between Bai Yunsheng and Chu Yingfeng.","Chu Yingfeng might possess the reputation of a genius... but honestly, how many geniuses were there in the world? The Bai clan of Yunmeng, to which Bai Yunsheng belonged, had produced several peerless talents as well. All of them were now disciples of Dao Lord Tongxuan of the Divine Firmament Dao.","Bai Yunsheng did not hate Chu Yingfeng merely because he was powerful.","Chu Yingfeng himself—and the very reason he had entered the Profound Heaven Sect—were enough to make most people in the sect despise him.","—In an inn, he had butchered a group of disciples from immortal sects.","Certainly, those disciples had been in the wrong. But they ought to have been punished fairly according to sect rules. How could they be beheaded with a butcher’s cleaver, their heads thrown out into the street?","The son of a menial servant and a cook—how could he dare... how could he dare do such a thing?","But Chu Yingfeng had dared. And by chance, he had been saved by the passing Perfected Renhua. At the time, most of the elders of the Profound Heaven Sect had opposed taking in such a vicious criminal, but Perfected Renhua had insisted. In the end, Chu Yingfeng was admitted into the sect.","Bai Yunsheng disliked Chu Yingfeng—hated him—for the simple reason that he saw his own fate bound up with that of his class.","No one who benefited from the existing order could possibly look kindly upon someone like Chu Yingfeng.","So everything he had said just now had been meant to provoke Chu Yingfeng—meant to humiliate him.","He wasn’t actually certain that the Seven-Treasure Pine was with Wu Guanyue. But he knew that Chu Yingfeng was close to her, and had even stood up for her before—and that was enough.","With a casual word, he could make Wu Guanyue suffer badly.","Chu Yingfeng, what are you acting so proud for? Do you think that just because you joined the Mystic Heaven Sect, you can truly stand on equal footing with us?","A stray dog is still a dog, even if it turns into a house pet!","Watching Chu Yingfeng’s furious yet agonized expression, Bai Yunsheng’s eyes gleamed with utter malice.","And Chu Yingfeng couldn’t move!","He truly wanted to run the man before him through with his sword! The expression on this man’s face at this very moment overlapped endlessly with those of the people in his memories who had killed his father. He could do it—if he wanted to, Bai Yunsheng would be dead beyond any doubt tonight. It wouldn’t matter what magical artifacts he possessed!","But—","No. He couldn’t lay a hand on Bai Yunsheng!","The veins in Chu Yingfeng’s neck throbbed, and the muscles beneath his eyelids seemed to twitch. His body had been drawn taut to its limit—as though he might leap up and kill at any moment—yet it felt as if a thin dog leash had truly been looped around his neck.","Bai Yunsheng’s smile grew ever more vicious. He felt simply wonderful!","Then, just then, something unexpected happened!","A pair of Evil Twin-Tails suddenly flew past!","“Rip!”","The sound of fabric tearing rang out in an instant. Bai Yunsheng felt a chill over his body...","His robe of moonlight brocade was gone!","Naturally, the one who had struck with lightning speed was Little Shopkeeper Wu!","【Proficiency Skill Used—Advanced Pickpocketing!】","【Obtained: [Moonlight Brocade Robe] ×1!】","After listening outside for quite some time, Little Shopkeeper Wu had reached an important conclusion—","There were actually red-named players this despicable in the world!","And Wu Guanyue keenly realized that dealing with this red-name was the key to raising Chu Yingfeng’s favorability—and the key to completing the side quest, [Wherever You Go, You Leave Something Behind].","Asking her to flatter this red-name was absolutely out of the question. But if she fought him now, she probably couldn’t beat him at her current level. The only skill she could use to challenge someone above her level was—","Pickpocketing!","Just watch her strip that smug, high-and-mighty face right off him!","Little Shopkeeper Wu: ◣ω◢","【Proficiency Skill Used—Advanced Pickpocketing!】","【Obtained: [Ice Silkworm Silk Undergarment] ×1!】","【Proficiency Skill Used—Advanced Pickpocketing!】","【Obtained: [Heavenly Spider Velvet Undershirt] ×1!】","【Proficiency Skill Used—Advanced Pickpocketing!】","【Obtained: [Heavenly Spider Velvet Shorts] ×1!】","Little Shopkeeper Wu moved even faster than lightning. The arm she used for pickpocketing moved so quickly that not even an afterimage could be seen! This advanced version of the Pickpocketing skill was practically a conceptual god-tier ability!","Wuyun let out an “Awooo!” and, as if marching to its death, raised its tail high!","Wu Guanyue didn’t linger in battle for even a moment. She made her decision at once!","【Proficiency Skill Used—Advanced Pickpocketing!】","【Obtained: [Fur] ×1!】","The Evil Twin-Tails shot away with a swish!","Only then did Bai Yunsheng finally react...","He was already... naked... na... ked...","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Bai Yunsheng: “..................”","Bai Yunsheng flew into a rage... and snapped open his fan, covering the one place on his body that most desperately needed covering!","He couldn’t get a single word out! His entire body was as red as a shrimp freshly hauled from the river, his face flushed scarlet!","After all, being stark naked was always when a person was at their most vulnerable.","Wenren Ying was utterly stunned as well!","...He knew Little Shopkeeper Wu had an unusual way of thinking, but he truly never imagined she could pull off something like this!","And why was she only this nimble when she was stripping someone?!","That move just now... even he wouldn’t dare claim he could have reacted in time.","It left Wenren Ying feeling a powerful sense of crisis about the clothes on his own body... No! That wasn’t the point!","The point was that Little Shopkeeper Wu hadn’t disguised herself at all when she did this... If they didn’t kill Bai Yunsheng tonight, he absolutely wouldn’t let the matter go!","But they couldn’t kill Bai Yunsheng... Killing him would bring endless trouble afterward.","They ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍had to think of a way!","In the time it took for a spark to flash, Wenren Ying suddenly remembered something Little Shopkeeper Wu had once said! How utterly reasonable those words had been—!","Wenren Ying tugged down the brim of his bamboo hat and, with great decisiveness, drawled in his low, hoarse voice—","“Bai Yunsheng, you wouldn’t want anyone to find out what happened today, would you...”","The end."]},{"number":28,"title":"Chapter 28","paragraphs":["***","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Bai Yunsheng: “..................”","The enraged Bai Yunsheng was completely dumbstruck.","In an instant, all the dangerous thoughts of revenge in his mind vanished, replaced by a deep confusion. For a moment, he truly could not understand what those words meant, and his face took on an almost vacant, idiotic expression.","Only after a long while did he suddenly shout, “You dare try to fool me?!”","Everything that had happened tonight was simply too outrageous. If word got out, he would lose all face!","But fortunately, Bai Yunsheng was extremely conceited. He had not brought anyone else with him tonight when meeting Chu Yingfeng here. Though Chu Yingfeng’s damned eyes had seen everything... his terrible popularity meant he had no one to spread it to...","As for the two people outside... Who would really take their word for it without proof?!","Yet the low, hoarse male voice outside rang out once more.","His voice was leisurely, carrying a teasing laugh.","“Surely a disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect knows that in this world there is such a thing as a Tracing Pearl, capable of replaying the movements of anyone within ten zhang of the pearl? Image and sound, all perfectly preserved.”","Of course Bai Yunsheng knew about it!","But the Tracing Pearl required Southern Pearls from the Merfolk Realm, Lunar Essence Marrow, and Styx Cinnabar as materials. Refining such a magical artifact was extraordinarily difficult, and even a fortune could not buy one! Even within the Profound Heaven Sect, this item was kept only in the Exquisite Grotto-Heaven, where magical artifacts were collected—for the obvious purpose of preventing theft.","How could a small city like Meishan possibly have such a thing?!","Bai Yunsheng said coldly, “You know quite a lot, but unfortunately, you can’t fool me!”","The person outside let out a long sigh. “As expected of a disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect. Indeed, you’re not easy to fool. In that case, you can come out and battle me for three hundred rounds.”","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","A vein throbbed at Bai Yunsheng’s temple.","The person outside laughed. “Whether you believe me or not, tomorrow you’ll find out whether I have a Tracing Pearl.”","Bai Yunsheng remained where he was, holding his fan over himself. He stood perfectly still, practically like a statue.","Opposite him, Chu Yingfeng stood motionless as well, his arms folded around his sword. His dark eyes studied Bai Yunsheng’s current appearance, as though he found it quite interesting and wanted to look a little longer.","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Bai Yunsheng did not want to face Chu Yingfeng!","But even more than that, he could not turn his back on Chu Yingfeng. At least when facing him, he had a fan to cover his shame. If he turned his back on him, then wouldn’t that mean... uh...!","At last, Bai Yunsheng spoke. His voice sounded as though it had been squeezed out from between his clenched teeth.","“You... what do you want?!”","A crisp female voice rang out almost immediately. “Hand over every last bit of money on you!”","Bai Yunsheng flew into a rage. “You took even my underwear! Do you really think I have any money left to give you?!”","“Oh... I suppose that’s true...”","The female voice sounded rather disappointed.","But soon, she brightened again and declared righteously, “Then give me your fan!”","It looked like a jade-boned fan. It ought to fetch quite a bit of money, right?","Moonlight shone against the paper-covered window, revealing her silhouette. Her twin ponytails swayed back and forth. She was indeed so wicked that no one dared look at her for long.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying was terrified that she would provoke Bai Yunsheng into making his eyes turn red and actually rushing out to battle them for three hundred rounds... If that happened, there would truly be no way to end things tonight.","He hurriedly clapped a hand over Wu Guanyue’s mouth to stop her from saying anything else, then patiently tried to persuade her. “Let’s not take the fan. It’s been contaminated by filthy things, Little... Little Yue.”","He had originally intended to call her Little Shopkeeper Wu, but just as the words reached his lips, he suddenly realized that doing so would reveal her identity. His mind short-circuited, and he called her Little Yue instead.","But the moment those two words left his mouth, he suddenly came back to his senses... Bai Yunsheng had already set his sights on them anyway. Besides, Little Shopkeeper Wu had just appeared before him. Whether her identity was exposed or not... what difference did it make now?","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue’s eyes widened. She abruptly turned her head and looked up at Wenren Ying.","Moonlight shone against the paper-covered window, casting the silent silhouettes of the two of them as they stared at each other.","“...Ahem.”","After they had gazed at each other for quite some time, the evil conical-hat man gave an ambiguous cough and somewhat awkwardly reached up to press down on his hat.","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng suddenly remembered that afternoon when he had played Cat Mario.","For some inexplicable reason, Bai Yunsheng felt as though he had become a toy for the two people outside...","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","A gigantic cross-shaped bulging vein appeared on Bai Yunsheng’s forehead.","Fortunately, the two of them did not keep making eyes at each other for long. The adulterer spoke up. “Since that’s the case, we won’t disturb you two any longer.”","Bai Yunsheng: “............?!!!”","Who was disturbing whom here?!","Were they not the ones who were impatient to find somewhere to sneak off and fool around—ah, no, that was not the point right now—","“Wait! Give me the Tracing Pearl!”","The conical-hat man slung the twin-tailed girl over his back. Then he soared into the air, riding the wind. Only his lazy voice remained in the night sky, along with an object that came spinning through the window.","“The Tracing Pearl is here. Young Master Bai, take good care of it!”","Bai Yunsheng stretched out his arm and snatched up the “Tracing Pearl.”","It was not a Tracing Pearl at all. It was clearly just a scrap of paper.","On the paper was a drawing of a turtle. The turtle’s mouth was crooked, its eyes askew, and it looked so idiotic that it seemed on the verge of drooling. One hand even clutched a turtle shell, shielding the area between its legs...","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Bai Yunsheng: “..................”","Veins bulged across the back of Bai Yunsheng’s hand. He clenched the scrap of paper so tightly that it was completely shredded!","Meanwhile, Chu Yingfeng had already leaped into action!","When he flew out, it was like an arrow fired from the Divine Mechanism Pavilion—he shot forward in a straight line!","Beneath the moonlight, atop the roof ridge, Chu Yingfeng’s sword flashed into motion!","Wenren Ying was rolling his wrists.","After leaping onto this stretch of roof, he had gently set Wu Guanyue down to one side, casually patted Wuyun on the head, and then begun stretching his wrists and regulating his breathing—","Then he drew his blade!","The blade-light condensed into a single line, and the sound of the wind turned razor-sharp!","In an instant, the black-clad swordsman and the conical-hat saber wielder were locked in combat atop the roof ridge.","The black-clad swordsman’s wrist gave a slight twist, and the treasured sword in his hand burst into ten thousand points of dazzling light. Amid the raging wind and driving rain of sword-light, however, the radiance suddenly shifted, with a thread of blade-light concealed within it.","Wenren Ying’s expression did not change. Amid the torrential rain of sword-light, he intercepted that single streak of saber-light!","Yet the saber-light abruptly transformed, becoming two curved hooks like crescent moons—","The weapon in Chu Yingfeng’s hand suddenly changed from a three-inch-seven-long treasured sword into a pair of double hooks!","Chu Yingfeng possessed a metal spiritual root, so the Kunwu Sword in his hand could transform at will into any of the eighteen types of weapons, allowing him to wield whatever he pleased!","The hook was an especially unusual weapon. Across the entire Nine Provinces, there were not many people who knew how to use it. Its technique lay in hooking and warding with one hook in each hand, making it exceptionally difficult to control. At this moment, Chu Yingfeng used the hook in his right hand to catch Wenren Ying’s long saber, while the hook in his left hand flashed out its edge and drove straight toward Wenren Ying’s centerline.","Wenren Ying’s foot shot up high, striking Chu Yingfeng’s crescent hook dead-on.","At the same moment, the hand gripping his saber went slack. The blade flashed through several dazzling flourishes in midair before dropping neatly back into his hand, his fingers firm and his knuckles sharply defined.","The two men crossed paths and came to a stop a short distance apart.","Chu Yingfeng stood where he was, quietly gazing at Wu Guanyue.","After a long pause, he said, “Thank you.”","Wu Guanyue: “............”","Wu Guanyue: “............?”","Was this how he expressed his gratitude—by picking a fight with Brother Wenren?","But when she checked Chu Yingfeng’s affection meter, it had actually gone up...","At that very moment, Chu Yingfeng’s affection had risen all the way to three hearts. That meant that, in his mind, the two of them could genuinely be considered friends now.","Chu Yingfeng flicked his twin hooks, and they transformed back into a sword, which he slid into its sheath.","He asked only, “Was it you who took down the Seven-Treasure Pine?”","Wu Guanyue nodded.","Chu Yingfeng said, “Good. I’ll handle this for you.”","Wu Guanyue: “How are you going to handle it?”","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Whenever he encountered a difficult question, Chu Yingfeng stopped talking.","A tangled-knot bubble, symbolizing a muddled mind, appeared above the black-clad swordsman’s head.","As expected! This guy really was a natural airhead!","He looked cool as he took the matter upon himself, but in reality, he didn’t have the slightest idea what to do!","Wu Guanyue: stare.jpg","The black-clad swordsman’s expression did not change. His handsome face remained as cold as snowdrifts... yet a string of awkward cold-sweat bubbles kept popping up above his head.","Chu Yingfeng said coldly, “You needn’t concern yourself with it.”","Wenren Ying struggled not to laugh. “All right, all right... Solutions are meant to be discussed. Why don’t we head back to the inn and think carefully about how to deal with Bai Yunsheng?”","Wu Guanyue: “Mm-hm!”","Wu Guanyue was naturally all for it. Chu Yingfeng also thought it was a good idea, but he was used to keeping to himself. When he saw Wu Guanyue walking side by side with Wenren Ying, a string of ellipsis bubbles appeared above his head.","Then he suddenly rode the wind away, leaving not even a silhouette behind.","Moonlight spilled across the street, illuminating the tall and short figures of the two people walking along it.","Hugging Wuyun, Wu Guanyue sighed. “He’s such a strange person... Why did he have to fight you, Brother Wenren?”","Wenren Ying pressed down on the brim of his bamboo hat and drawled lazily, “A person like him gets itchy all over if he doesn’t get some fresh air every day... It’s nothing to worry about. Neither of us was really taking it seriously just now.”","Wu Guanyue sank into deep thought. After a long while, she said, “Hmm... Pay attention to your grooming... Is that what you mean?”","Wenren Ying: “?”","What did she mean by “grooming”?","Before he could ask, Wu Guanyue had already moved on to her next question.","“Brother Wenren! Brother Wenren! Why do you always wear that hat?”","Wenren Ying said, “Because I like wearing it.”","“Then won’t the part of your forehead sticking out from beneath the hat be dark, while the part underneath is pale?”","Wenren Ying: “............”","“I want to see what you look like when you take off your hat!”","Wu Guanyue’s twin ponytails swayed back and forth as she made this perfectly reasonable request.","“Meow! Meow! Meow!”","Wuyun voiced its enthusiastic agreement.","Wenren Ying: “...If I refuse, are you going to—”","...tear my clothes off like you did to Bai Yunsheng today?","He cut himself off halfway through, because he realized that if he actually said it aloud, he might only be giving Wu Guanyue ideas.","Wu Guanyue: “Hmm? Going to what?”","Wenren Ying let out a long sigh. “...Nothing.”","He reached out and caught the brim of his hat. After taking two long, deep breaths, he slowly removed it, lowering his head to gaze at her.","They ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍were a pair of... deep, melancholy eyes.","His features were actually rather stern overall, giving him an unapproachable air... But his eyes seemed to hold the gentle starlight of this very night.","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue suddenly took a step backward.","Then she abruptly turned around, facing away from Wenren Ying, and murmured as though nothing had happened, “Wu Guanyue never became emperor in her entire life because she could never forget those melancholy eyes of Wenren Ying...” (*)","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “............?”","What did she mean by “became emperor”? What was she talking about?","(*): Quoted from Yi Zhongtian’s Lecture Room. Here we go."]},{"number":29,"title":"Chapter 29","paragraphs":["***","Little Shopkeeper Wu often says the strangest things...","At this very moment, she seemed a little embarrassed and a little happy, her hands clasped behind her back as she twisted them together.","Wenren Ying walked behind her, watching her bounce along on tiptoe. Her twin ponytails hung down in front of her, leaping just as merrily as her mood.","Her footsteps fell into the moonlight, and her whole person seemed immersed in it.","Wenren ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍Ying could not help following her silhouette with his eyes... It was strange. There was something special and incredibly attractive about Wu Guanyue.","What was that quality, exactly?","It seemed to be an aura of boundless optimism.","No matter what happened, she always seemed certain she could solve it. She seemed to believe that as long as she put her mind to it, there was nothing in the world she could not overcome... It was an almost completely irrational confidence, but that confidence truly drew Wenren Ying’s gaze.","Cheerful Little Shopkeeper Wu. Little Shopkeeper Wu, who was always coming up with the unexpected...","Her ponytails continued to bounce, and the dark cloud perched atop her head seemed to cheer up as well, swaying back and forth in perfect harmony with her. It looked almost like her third ponytail.","Wenren Ying could not help laughing. In a lazy voice, he called, “Hey, Little Shopkeeper Wu—”","Wu Guanyue spun around with a whoosh, turning half her body along with her.","“You just called me Little Yue a moment ago! You’re not allowed to go back to the old name now!”","As she said this, she walked backward down the empty street, eyeing Wenren Ying with an expression of mild displeasure.","Wenren Ying’s expression, however, seemed a little unnatural. He raised a hand as though to adjust the brim of his bamboo hat... but when his fingers closed on empty air, he remembered that he had already taken it off.","Wu Guanyue stared at him with her eyes opened wide. Wuyun’s eyes were also opened wide as it stared at him... To be honest, being watched so intently by two pairs of eyes as round as copper bells was rather... embarrassing.","After a long moment, he finally opened his mouth and said, somewhat stiffly, “L... Little Shopkeeper Yue.”","Wu Guanyue: O-O","Wu Guanyue: o(*////-////*)q","Little Shopkeeper Yue’s face flushed faintly...","She seemed to ponder the matter, murmuring thoughtfully for quite a while before saying, “Hmm... Calling you Brother Wenren does feel a little distant too. What should I call you instead?”","Wu Guanyue suddenly stopped.","Wenren Ying stopped as well. His shadow fell over her, covering her shadow—and her entire person.","He stood there quietly, looking down at her in silence... He seemed to want to say something, yet also seemed to want to retreat.","He appeared to be a fairly bold and carefree man... But perhaps his boldness came from simply not caring what others thought. Once he genuinely began to care, he could no longer be so free and easy.","He suddenly drew a deep breath... He was about to say something to Wu Guanyue, but Little Shopkeeper Wu had already spoken up in an especially loud voice.","“Ah! I’ve got it!”","She sounded delighted.","Then she suddenly reached out and very carefully knocked three times on Wenren Ying’s broad, double-door-sized chest. In a solemn little voice, she chanted, “Yingzi, open up! Daddy!”","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","A huge, cross-shaped vein popped out on Wenren Ying’s forehead.","***","Meishan City was not particularly small, but neither was it especially large. A cultivator could travel from the east side of the city to the west in less than half a quarter of an hour.","But this journey... took Wu Guanyue and Wenren Ying a full half hour. By the time they reached the end, Wuyun was literally dripping down from the top of Wu Guanyue’s head...","...It was too sleepy to stay perched up there.","By the time they returned to the inn, the sky was already beginning to pale.","Chu Yingfeng... Er, Chu Yingfeng had gone to bed early. He had not waited for them at all.","...He seemed to possess an instinctive, almost feral sense of when the best course of action was to go to sleep.","At that moment, Chu Yingfeng was wearing only his inner shirt as he made his way downstairs to the kitchen to ladle himself some water. He drifted past the two of them like a ghost, sparing them a stingy sidelong glance. Then he let out a soft “Hmph,” the spiteful meaning of which was practically unmistakable: As expected.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wu Guanyue, on the other hand, was genuinely concerned about him. The moment she saw him, she rushed over and began circling him.","“Chu Yingfeng! Chu Yingfeng! Do you want some garlic-crispy mini bread?”","Chu Yingfeng: “............”","Chu Yingfeng: “............Mm.”","Wu Guanyue rummaged around inside her sleeve—rummaged and rummaged and rummaged—and pulled out a piece of garlic-crispy mini bread to hand to him. Then she walked over to Wenren Ying and, as though nothing were amiss, pulled out some large-intestine sashimi for him.","Wenren Ying: “............”","Wenren Ying: “..................”","Wenren Ying did not move a muscle. Ellipsis bubbles began appearing above his head at a rate of two per second.","Little Shopkeeper Wu: (*^▽^*)","Little Shopkeeper Wu revealed her trademark sweet smile. She took the large-intestine sashimi back and brought out another piece of garlic-crispy mini bread to offer Wenren Ying.","At last, the ellipsis bubbles above Wenren Ying’s head stopped appearing... Any more of them and they would have flooded Wu Guanyue’s inn.","“All right, back to business. Let’s talk about the important stuff.”","Wenren Ying said this as he took a bite of the mini bread... Then, without changing expression, spat out the little hairs mixed into the garlic-crispy filling.","...Well, the bread had been synthesized from [milk] and [Wuyun’s propeller tail], after all.","Chu Yingfeng also spat out a hair without changing expression, then began to speak.","In short—Daoist Master Songfeng had quite a background.","Daoist Master Songfeng’s true origin was a magical treasure known as the Seven-Treasure Pine. The master of the Seven-Treasure Pine had been the leader of the Profound Heaven Sect a thousand years ago—the Sword Lord Taibai, Yan Chongyang.","The Sword Lord Taibai was a grandmaster of his generation. By the time he was five hundred years old, he had already attained great mastery of the Dao. He was also a man who cared deeply for the world. When he served as sect leader, peace reigned throughout the Yuntai Domain, and the people lived and worked in contentment.","As a result, the Ninth Heaven sent down an auspicious omen. A celestial crane arrived bearing a jade gem, condensed from his merit. It could help him survive the tribulation and ascend to the Ninth Heaven. This event became a celebrated legend throughout the Yuntai Domain.","In this world, the lifespans of earthly half-immortals—in other words, cultivators—were not eternal like those of Heaven and Earth. At most, they could live for a thousand or eight hundred years. Moreover, ascension required the recognition of the Ninth Heaven. Only when the Ninth Heaven sent down an auspicious omen could one ascend safely. Anyone who attempted to ascend by force would be blasted into oblivion by the heavenly lightning.","If they failed to receive the recognition of the Ninth Heaven, then when their natural lifespan came to an end, cultivators would grow old and die just like ordinary mortals. This was known as the “Five Declines of Heaven and Man.”","Since the Sword Lord Taibai had received jade from a celestial crane, he should have been able to ascend safely... Yet his actual end was to die without leaving even ashes behind.","Before he ascended, an unprecedented great demon appeared in the Yuntai Domain. People of that era called him the “Hundred-Eyed Demon Lord.” His source of power was not any of the five elemental energies—metal, wood, water, fire, or earth—but rather “soulfire,” which drew its strength from human souls.","Sword Lord Taibai paid for suppressing this evil demon with his life.","And according to legend... the place where the Hundred-Eyed Demon Lord was sealed lies somewhere amid the rolling mountains of Mount Mei. The only problem was that no one knew exactly where.","But back to the matter at hand—the Seven-Treasure Pine had indeed committed countless evil deeds, yet it truly had a good master. After Sword Lord Taibai sacrificed himself to suppress the Hundred-Eyed Demon Lord, his direct descendants continued to enjoy the benefits of his legacy. Many members of the Yuntai Yan clan now held important positions in the Divine Firmament Dao’s Lingshu Pavilion. Even those with the least impressive circumstances held the honored position of elder in the Profound Heaven Sect.","And the one doing the worst of all... was, of course, Perfected Renhua, the master of Chu Yingfeng and Bai Yunsheng.","This time, it was precisely because Perfected Renhua had received news of the Seven-Treasure Pine that he had sent Chu Yingfeng and Bai Yunsheng to Mount Mei.","Er... what...","Was this Journey to the West or something?!","Whenever a monster got beaten to death, there was always some god or Buddha behind it!","And, objectively speaking, even if Perfected Renhua was the least successful member of the Yuntai Yan clan... Wu Guanyue probably still couldn’t afford to provoke him...","...Bai Yunsheng wasn’t someone she could afford to provoke, either.","She didn’t even need Chu Yingfeng. Wenren Ying alone could give her a full lesson on Bai Yunsheng’s background. The Yunmeng Bai clan, from which Bai Yunsheng came, was a thousand-year-old aristocratic family of Yunmeng Marsh.","As mentioned before, the cultivation sects in this world were somewhat like a feudal system bound together by master-disciple relationships. But that did not mean bloodline clans didn’t exist. In fact, these aristocratic families were firmly embedded within the system.","For example, the master of Verdant Cloud Grotto-Heaven had always been chosen from among the She clan of Mount Mei. Nearly all of the current Verdant Cloud Adept’s direct disciples were surnamed She.","From this, it was easy enough to understand the status of the Yunmeng Bai clan.","Bai Yunsheng being sent to the Profound Heaven Sect as a disciple was, in fact, equivalent to a diplomatic exchange of hostages meant to demonstrate goodwill between the two sides.","Er...","Relying on nothing but Daoist Master Songfeng as her only tree to cling to, Wu Guanyue had somehow managed to offend members of two great clans!","...Wasn’t this supposed to be a cultivation-management game?","Why did it have such a complicated setting?!","No... Calm down, Wu Guanyue. Since the game had provided such a detailed background, that must mean brute force absolutely wasn’t the way to solve this problem. So, if she took a more roundabout approach...","Wu Guanyue sank into deep thought.","Wenren Ying sank into deep thought as well... and, for some reason, his expression changed ever so slightly when he heard the name Perfected Renhua.","Chu Yingfeng also sank into deep thought... though whether he was actually thinking or simply letting his mind go blank was impossible to say. His expression gave nothing away.","Wu Guanyue murmured to herself as she pondered, “Bai Yunsheng... the Seven-Treasure Pine... Cat Mario... You wouldn’t want anyone finding out about what happened today, would you...”","Wenren Ying: “...?”","Chu Yingfeng: “...?”","The two of them turned around in unison and stared at Wu Guanyue, utterly baffled as to why someone would make that sort of noise while thinking.","Meanwhile, a lightbulb suddenly lit up above the head of the Little Shopkeeper Wu.","“I know what to do! I know what to do!”","The Little Shopkeeper Wu pointed at the inn and declared confidently, “All we have to do is lay an ambush here. I guarantee that Bai Yunsheng will surrender willingly and bow at our feet! Keh heh heh heh heh heh!”"]},{"number":30,"title":"Chapter 30","paragraphs":["***","The following night, Bai Yunsheng appeared right on schedule, standing in front of the inn right on schedule as well.","As for why he had come here... the reason was quite simple: Wu Guanyue had sent him a message through Chu Yingfeng.","Chu Yingfeng had taken the initiative to show up early that morning... Because he had been forced to see Bai Yunsheng in the flesh the night before, Bai Yunsheng really didn’t want to see him. Every time he caught sight of that expressionless face, cold as snow and ice, his entire body felt uncomfortable.","Then Chu Yingfeng opened his mouth, and he felt even worse...","Chu Yingfeng’s tone was as flat as ever. “Bai Yunsheng, you don’t want anyone finding out about what happened last night, do you?”","Bai Yunsheng: “......”","Bai Yunsheng exploded. “What the hell did you just say?!”","Chu Yingfeng’s expression didn’t change in the slightest. He merely said coldly, “The innkeeper would like you to come to the inn tonight. That’s what she asked me to tell you.”","Bai Yunsheng: “......”","Bai Yunsheng fell silent.","A threat... This was a threat... It was practically a naked, blatant threat.","But what a useful threat it was!","Although he didn’t believe for a second that Chu Yingfeng actually had a Trace-Shadow Pearl... whenever he imagined the possibility of everyone seeing him with his bare bottom exposed, the terror rising from the depths of his heart drowned out every last bit of rational analysis...","Thus, after his face twisted for an instant, Bai Yunsheng still agreed—though with immense humiliation.","Chu Yingfeng looked at him with an extremely strange expression.","Bai Yunsheng was already annoyed beyond words. “What are you looking at?!”","Chu Yingfeng withdrew his gaze. As he walked away, he seemed to sigh faintly. “So concerned with your dignity. A fatal flaw...”","Bai Yunsheng: “......”","Bai Yunsheng exploded again. “Easy for you to say! If you’ve got the guts, you strip too!!!”","His shout had been so loud that it attracted the curious gazes of several Dongtian disciples.","Chu Yingfeng ignored him and disappeared from the spot.","And so, Bai Yunsheng still came.","Even though he knew he shouldn’t, he came anyway.","Wu Guanyue had gone to such lengths and risked her life... er, she had stripped him of his clothes, clearly not because those clothes were particularly expensive or exquisite. She must have had some other purpose. She must want to discuss something with him.","Now, he was willing to sit down and have a talk with her.","This was a banquet at Hongmen, but certainly not one intended to kill him.","Since that was the case, what was there to worry about? Things couldn’t possibly be worse than they had been yesterday anyway...","Bai Yunsheng gave himself this little pep talk before coming alone to the banquet.","Of course, he had still brought along every last piece of equipment he had.","The Immortal-Slaying Saber, the Origin-Returning Sword, the Heart-Protecting Mirror, the Soft-Spined Armor...","At that moment, Bai Yunsheng stood on Qihua Road with his hands clasped behind his back, gazing up at the inn’s signboard.","The sign was densely covered in tiny, minuscule characters recording who-knew-what. It radiated an evil aura that made Bai Yunsheng unable to resist taking a closer look and reading it carefully...","“Ah ah ah, oh oh oh, uh uh uh...”","Bai Yunsheng: “......”","Bai Yunsheng stopped reading and called out loudly from in front of the inn, “Bai Yunsheng of the Profound Heaven Sect has come to seek your instruction!”","The lantern hanging outside the inn suddenly swayed in the wind, its flame flickering eerily.","No one answered, but the door creaked open by itself.","Bai Yunsheng furrowed his brows... but he was not a coward.","He had gone out of his way to come here tonight. Nothing had happened yet—could he really just slink away with his tail between his legs?","Bai Yunsheng gave a heavy snort, flicked back his robe, and strode into the inn.","At that very instant, he was suddenly surrounded by a cloud of mist!","Bai Yunsheng sensed that something was wrong and immediately tried to retreat—but it was already too late!","The mist had completely swallowed him up!","His body suddenly underwent a tremendous transformation... Bai Yunsheng widened his eyes in horror as he discovered that he was changing from a human into... er, a cat?","...Was it a cat?","The cat had an ugly face and stood upright on two legs, its posture grotesque. At the same time, the inn before Bai Yunsheng’s eyes vanished, replaced by a crude road paved with brown bricks. Above the road floated several individual blocks of brick.","If he had arrived in Meishan City a little earlier and enjoyed keeping up with the latest trends, he would have realized at once—","It was Cat Mario! The Cat Mario that had taken Meishan by storm!","But he didn’t know... didn’t... know...","Bai Yunsheng was shocked and flustered... but after finally calming down, he discovered that he could no longer soar through the air. All he could do was jump and move forward...","...A mirage beast.","That was his conclusion.","Indeed! This was, of course, Wuyun’s handiwork!","These past few days, with Cat Mario becoming wildly popular, the spiritual energy Wuyun had absorbed had been truly substantial. Its level had risen along with it, and at this very moment, the Black Cloud Cat was already a seasoned LV.4 mirage beast—chest puffed out proudly!","...Its size had increased along with its level, too. Recently, whenever Wu Guanyue balanced it on top of her head, she could feel the heavy weight of life pressing down on her neck.","All right, enough digressing. In short, creating illusions was a mirage beast’s specialty. Bringing a two-dimensional version of Cat Mario into the three-dimensional world was naturally no problem at all!","Bai Yunsheng, trapped inside the mirage beast’s illusion, could only obey the rules of the illusion... Once someone fell into a mirage beast’s mirage-scape, they had to find the key to the illusion before they could successfully escape...","Where was the key?","Bai Yunsheng warily hopped forward.","Every time he landed, a “toot~~~~” sounded beside his ears. It didn’t resemble the sound of any musical instrument he had ever heard. Although it was ridiculous, it kept his nerves stretched taut.","The road ahead gradually revealed itself... There was only one path to take. Bai Yunsheng tried jumping forward...","...and then he returned to the starting point.","...It seemed that something had suddenly shot out of a green pipe and killed him.","After all, this was Cat Mario. Such a thing was perfectly normal. The guests who frequently played games at the inn had long since grown indifferent to it; their mental states did not change in the slightest.","But Bai Yunsheng didn’t know... didn’t... know...","Bai Yunsheng: “......”","Bai Yunsheng’s rage meter increased by 10%.","He drew a deep breath, regrouped, and set off again.","A disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect was a disciple of the Profound Heaven Sect. Even though Bai Yunsheng was technically a hostage-like disciple, his skills were still up to par. He wouldn’t be defeated twice by the same trick. This time, he successfully made it past the dangerous pipe and continued onward...","...and then he returned to the starting point again.","...It seemed that a cloud had just dropped from the sky and crushed him to death.","In the course of playing Cat Mario, this was also perfectly normal. After all, the game was designed to be torturous. During the early stages, dying any number of times was entirely ordinary.","But Bai Yunsheng had never been tormented before...","And besides, Wu Guanyue possessed [Skill: Game Editor]!","She hadn’t dared use this skill before, because she hadn’t had any idea how to modify the game... But now things were different. In order to deal with Bai Yunsheng, she had come up with the perfect plan!","Cancel the checkpoints!","That was it—cancel the checkpoints!","Every time he died, he would have to start all over again, with absolutely no shortcuts! It had gone from a torturous game to the ultimate torture game!","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Back at the starting point, Bai Yunsheng’s anger slowly climbed to fifty percent...","But that wasn’t all. Just as he began making his way forward from the starting point for the eighteenth time, the voice in his ears suddenly changed, transforming into a complete and beautiful melody!","A dignified male voice boomed out in song: “Three hundred and sixty-five li~~yeah~~crossing~~spring, summer, autumn, and winter~~~” (*)","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Blood vessels stood out in Bai Yunsheng’s eyes...","What the hell kind of mirage was this?!!","Bai Yunsheng felt as if he could sense the malice of the entire world—! Never in his wildest dreams had he imagined that today’s Hongmen Banquet would turn out like this!","What kind of Hongmen Banquet was this supposed to be?! What on earth was that Evil Twin-Tails, Wu Guanyue, trying to do?!","Bai Yunsheng felt completely and utterly toyed with. The fury in his heart was simply impossible to suppress!","He let out a furious shout and cursed, “Wu Guanyue! Come out! Hiding behind a mirage beast—do you call yourself a worthy opponent?! Can’t we talk things over?! Why are you doing this?! Why?!”","...No one answered him.","The mocking, beautiful singing continued in his ears, while that damn Cat Mario remained in front of his eyes.","Bai Yunsheng: “............”","Swallowing his anger, Bai Yunsheng continued onward...","This time, he finally made it safely to the end of the first stage. According to the normal game progression, he should have entered the second stage at this point—but the benevolent Wu Guanyue had placed a stage boss here.","Bai Yunsheng also suddenly discovered that, besides jumping and moving forward, he now had a third thing he could do—","Attack!","The stage boss slowly appeared. It was a simply drawn blade of grass.","But at that moment, Bai Yunsheng didn’t dare act rashly... Although his rage had nearly driven him out of his mind, he could still keenly sense the aura of a conspiracy...","Something was wrong. Something was definitely wrong. He couldn’t make a careless move.","Bai Yunsheng did not attack immediately. Instead, he circled around the simply drawn blade of grass, which was taller than he was...","Then he returned to the starting point!!!","At that very moment, the blade of grass suddenly split into two. The two halves trapped him between them, one on either side, shouting something about a “pincer attack from both sides” before crushing him to death!!","And so he had to hear it again...","“Three hundred and sixty-five li~~yeah~~”","The beautiful male voice continued to sing...","Bai Yunsheng’s anger level broke through eighty percent!","The veins at his temples bulged, and his temples throbbed violently... Truth be told, he wasn’t particularly good at keeping his temper in check. And especially after someone had seen him at his most vulnerable yesterday, he was unusually sensitive today...","At this moment, he was on the verge of exploding!","And after he died three more times on the way before finally reaching the stage boss, his fury reached its absolute peak!","The stage boss quickly split into two again, attempting to repeat its old trick and execute that “pincer attack from both sides”!","Bai Yunsheng’s eyes were bloodshot, his features twisted with rage. With a furious roar, he shot straight into the air and struck first!!","The Immortal-Slaying Saber flashed into action!!","The ​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌‌​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌​‌​​​‌‌​​​​‌​‌‌​​​‌​​​‌‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​‌​‌​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​​​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​‌​​‌‌​​​​​‌‌​​​‌‌​​‌‌​​‌​​​‌‌​‌‌​​‌‌​​​‌‌‍saber wind condensed into a single line and came whistling toward them, carrying enough force to cleave even a person’s primordial spirit in two!","“Crack!”","Bai Yunsheng brought his saber down in a single slash, and the sound of a tree splitting apart rang out sharply...","At the same time, the scene before his eyes suddenly changed. The illusory mirage vanished completely, replaced by the courtyard wall, a well, and...","A fallen pine tree?!","This pine tree was, of course, the Seven-Treasure Pine planted in Wu Guanyue’s backyard!","Let’s not forget that Wu Guanyue had [Construction Mode]. Once [Construction Mode] was activated, she could freely move anything inside the inn. Since the Seven-Treasure Pine had been planted within the inn, it naturally counted as an object she could move at will.","The instant Bai Yunsheng stepped into the inn, he had fallen into Wu Guanyue’s trap. Once his anger had been provoked, Wu Guanyue had naturally sent the Seven-Treasure Pine directly into the path of his saber!","And now...","[Activating [CG Mode] to record this beautiful moment!]","—Although she didn’t have a Memory-Reflection Orb, she could genuinely record video~","(*) Zhuang Xuezhong’s “Three Hundred and Sixty-Five Li.” Here it is!"]}]);
